sures the overlap of knowledge. It quantifies how much knowing the state of one variable actively reduces your mathematical uncertainty about another. Right. And relative entropy, which is often called the Kolbach-Leibler divergence, measures the pure informational distance between two competing descriptions of reality. If the universe is flipping a fair coin, but your internal model stubbornly insists the coin is heavily biased, the relative entropy mathematically quantifies exactly how many bits of information you are wasting by clinging to the wrong model. It is the geometric distance between your belief and the actual truth. I think we need to take a massive step back and look at the whole board because the arc of this deep dive is staggering. The text calls it the grand unification. We started with the basic algebra of high school functions. We did. We explored the geometric collapse of the isomorphism theorems. We rebuilt math using the arrows of category theory. We translated coordinates, diagonalized matrices, and bypassed calculus with the Fourier transform. It's been a long journey. We watched iterative feedback loops breed chaos. And we measured the limits of human knowledge with entropy and algorithmic complexity. It spans nearly every major discipline of mathematics. But the revelation is that whether we are talking about an injective function perfectly preserving its domain, a lossless compression algorithm packing data, or a hamming space protecting a CD from a physical scratch, it is all the exact same math. It truly is. At every level, mathematics is simply the rigorous study of what distinctions survive a transformation. Every single field is just asking a variation of the same question. Do the differences between these original states survive this new process? Which brings us to the final and undoubtedly most provocative concept from the source material's closing chapter, chapter 7. I have been waiting for this. The ultimate implication of the manuscript. Throughout this entire journey, we have learned how to track what changes, what is lost, and how to measure the remainder. But tracking what changes naturally leads to the ultimate question of both modern physics and mathematics, symmetry. Symmetry. Usually when I hear symmetry, I just picture a square being rotated 90 degrees and looking the same. Take that geometric intuition and expand it to the fabric of reality. A mathematical object is not defined by its physical substance. It is entirely defined by the set of transformations that leave it completely unchanged. Unchanged. Okay. A sphere is defined by the fact that it is invariant under continuous rotation. The fundamental laws of physics, conservation of energy, conservation of momentum are entirely defined by their invariance across shifts in time and space. The invariants are the reality. Right. The core properties that stubbornly survive all the representation changes. So if every single property we mathematically care about is ultimately just an invariant under some specific transformation, the author poses a final provocation. Do the physical objects of our universe even truly exist? Or is reality itself just a complex web of intersecting symmetries? Hmm. When we study a particle, are we actually studying a physical thing? Or are we merely studying the empty mathematical spaces where various transformations happen to cancel out? Wow. Is there even a there there or is it nothing but the network of relationships? It drags us right back to our very first analogy. The filing system. Exactly. Maybe the physical documents and the folders don't even exist. Maybe the only thing that is actually real are the rules for how we sort the empty space. It fundamentally challenges you to question the physical nature of the landscape we started this entire conversation on. It absolutely does. And on that slightly existential note, we will leave you to ponder it. We invite you to look around your world today and think about the invisible structures, the deliberate blind spots in your own mental transformations and the intersecting mathematical symmetries that are secretly governing your daily life. Thanks for joining us on this Deep Dive.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.7600000000000002, "text": " So imagine you're sitting in your high school algebra class.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 3811, 291, 434, 3798, 294, 428, 1090, 1395, 21989, 1508, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15382987055285224, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 1.2255502602337431e-12}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 3.84, "end": 5.62, "text": " Oh, bringing back the trauma right away, huh?", "tokens": [50557, 876, 11, 5062, 646, 264, 11407, 558, 1314, 11, 7020, 30, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15382987055285224, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 1.2255502602337431e-12}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 5.78, "end": 6.44, "text": " Right, exactly.", "tokens": [50654, 1779, 11, 2293, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15382987055285224, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 1.2255502602337431e-12}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 6.5600000000000005, "end": 7.86, "text": " But just, you know, bear with me.", "tokens": [50693, 583, 445, 11, 291, 458, 11, 6155, 365, 385, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15382987055285224, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 1.2255502602337431e-12}, {"id": 4, "seek": 0, "start": 8.64, "end": 14.5, "text": " You're staring at this piece of paper, and on it is this incredibly messy, complicated equation.", "tokens": [50797, 509, 434, 18043, 412, 341, 2522, 295, 3035, 11, 293, 322, 309, 307, 341, 6252, 16191, 11, 6179, 5367, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15382987055285224, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 1.2255502602337431e-12}, {"id": 5, "seek": 0, "start": 14.82, "end": 15.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51106, 1779, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15382987055285224, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 1.2255502602337431e-12}, {"id": 6, "seek": 0, "start": 15.06, "end": 28.2, "text": " And your teacher is standing up in the front, and basically the implicit promise of the whole educational system in that moment is this mathematics is just a machine for calculating the correct answer.", "tokens": [51118, 400, 428, 5027, 307, 4877, 493, 294, 264, 1868, 11, 293, 1936, 264, 26947, 6228, 295, 264, 1379, 10189, 1185, 294, 300, 1623, 307, 341, 18666, 307, 445, 257, 3479, 337, 28258, 264, 3006, 1867, 13, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15382987055285224, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 1.2255502602337431e-12}, {"id": 7, "seek": 0, "start": 28.44, "end": 28.86, "text": " A calculator.", "tokens": [51787, 316, 24993, 13, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15382987055285224, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 1.2255502602337431e-12}, {"id": 8, "seek": 2886, "start": 28.86, "end": 30.3, "text": " Yeah, a glorified calculator.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 257, 26623, 2587, 24993, 13, 50437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 2886, "start": 30.64, "end": 38.62, "text": " You plug a number into the equation, you do a series of mechanical steps, turn the crank, and out pops like a single undeniable truth.", "tokens": [50454, 509, 5452, 257, 1230, 666, 264, 5367, 11, 291, 360, 257, 2638, 295, 12070, 4439, 11, 1261, 264, 21263, 11, 293, 484, 16795, 411, 257, 2167, 674, 268, 9364, 3494, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2886, "start": 38.74, "end": 38.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50859, 1779, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 2886, "start": 39.18, "end": 40.7, "text": " And if you get the right number, you win.", "tokens": [50881, 400, 498, 291, 483, 264, 558, 1230, 11, 291, 1942, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 12, "seek": 2886, "start": 40.96, "end": 41.32, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50970, 7587, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 13, "seek": 2886, "start": 41.480000000000004, "end": 43.3, "text": " And if you get the wrong number, you fail.", "tokens": [50996, 400, 498, 291, 483, 264, 2085, 1230, 11, 291, 3061, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 14, "seek": 2886, "start": 43.68, "end": 47.5, "text": " I mean, that is how almost all of us were taught to think about math, right?", "tokens": [51106, 286, 914, 11, 300, 307, 577, 1920, 439, 295, 505, 645, 5928, 281, 519, 466, 5221, 11, 558, 30, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 15, "seek": 2886, "start": 48.0, "end": 50.379999999999995, "text": " That it's just this exalted form of accounting.", "tokens": [51322, 663, 309, 311, 445, 341, 454, 35906, 1254, 295, 19163, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 16, "seek": 2886, "start": 50.9, "end": 52.480000000000004, "text": " Yeah, the mechanical view of mathematics.", "tokens": [51467, 865, 11, 264, 12070, 1910, 295, 18666, 13, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 17, "seek": 2886, "start": 52.78, "end": 57.519999999999996, "text": " It's incredibly common, and honestly, I think it's comforting for a lot of people.", "tokens": [51561, 467, 311, 6252, 2689, 11, 293, 6095, 11, 286, 519, 309, 311, 38439, 337, 257, 688, 295, 561, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 18, "seek": 2886, "start": 57.6, "end": 57.9, "text": " Comforting.", "tokens": [51802, 2432, 2728, 278, 13, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 19, "seek": 2886, "start": 57.9, "end": 58.42, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51817, 1012, 370, 30, 51843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13949136610154983, "compression_ratio": 1.6930379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 7.065638222072956e-13}, {"id": 20, "seek": 5842, "start": 58.42, "end": 64.14, "text": " Well, when you treat math as just a glorified calculator, you get to live in a very binary world.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 562, 291, 2387, 5221, 382, 445, 257, 26623, 2587, 24993, 11, 291, 483, 281, 1621, 294, 257, 588, 17434, 1002, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077376234120336, "compression_ratio": 1.4551724137931035, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858814912325658e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 5842, "start": 64.3, "end": 68.58, "text": " There's a definitive input, a definitive output, and a very clear path between them.", "tokens": [50659, 821, 311, 257, 28152, 4846, 11, 257, 28152, 5598, 11, 293, 257, 588, 1850, 3100, 1296, 552, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077376234120336, "compression_ratio": 1.4551724137931035, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858814912325658e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 5842, "start": 68.66, "end": 68.74000000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50877, 1779, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077376234120336, "compression_ratio": 1.4551724137931035, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858814912325658e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 5842, "start": 68.8, "end": 69.6, "text": " There's no ambiguity.", "tokens": [50884, 821, 311, 572, 46519, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077376234120336, "compression_ratio": 1.4551724137931035, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858814912325658e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 6960, "start": 69.6, "end": 70.83999999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29461681842803955, "compression_ratio": 0.9436619718309859, "no_speech_prob": 1.2060483904965946e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 6960, "start": 70.83999999999999, "end": 74.88, "text": " But today we're going to completely shatter that illusion.", "tokens": [50427, 583, 965, 321, 434, 516, 281, 2584, 402, 1161, 300, 18854, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29461681842803955, "compression_ratio": 0.9436619718309859, "no_speech_prob": 1.2060483904965946e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 7488, "start": 74.88, "end": 85.74, "text": " We really are, because when you step away from that high school chalkboard and look at the absolute bleeding edge of modern abstract mathematics, that calculator isn't just broken.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 534, 366, 11, 570, 562, 291, 1823, 1314, 490, 300, 1090, 1395, 28660, 3787, 293, 574, 412, 264, 8236, 19312, 4691, 295, 4363, 12649, 18666, 11, 300, 24993, 1943, 380, 445, 5463, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1342500887419048, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815797886093886e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 8574, "start": 85.74, "end": 86.74, "text": " It's entirely irrelevant.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 7696, 28682, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.5438173294067383, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.2868094177026501e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 8574, "start": 86.74, "end": 88.74, "text": " It's entirely irrelevant.", "tokens": [50415, 467, 311, 7696, 28682, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.5438173294067383, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.2868094177026501e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 8574, "start": 88.74, "end": 89.74, "text": " Completely irrelevant.", "tokens": [50515, 39978, 28682, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.5438173294067383, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.2868094177026501e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 8574, "start": 89.74, "end": 90.17999999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50565, 865, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.5438173294067383, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.2868094177026501e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 9018, "start": 90.18, "end": 95.5, "text": " So what if I told you that mathematics isn't actually about calculating the right answer at all?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 437, 498, 286, 1907, 291, 300, 18666, 1943, 380, 767, 466, 28258, 264, 558, 1867, 412, 439, 30, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664962042932925, "compression_ratio": 1.0909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.3460944598558955e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 9550, "start": 95.5, "end": 102.02, "text": " What if, at its very core, math is actually the rigorous study of what we can tell apart?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 498, 11, 412, 1080, 588, 4965, 11, 5221, 307, 767, 264, 29882, 2979, 295, 437, 321, 393, 980, 4936, 30, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15062721252441405, "compression_ratio": 1.0853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.7178334492731762e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 10202, "start": 102.02, "end": 107.84, "text": " Moving the focus from computation to distinguishability, I mean, that is a massive paradigm shift right there.", "tokens": [50365, 14242, 264, 1879, 490, 24903, 281, 20206, 2310, 11, 286, 914, 11, 300, 307, 257, 5994, 24709, 5513, 558, 456, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15503783226013185, "compression_ratio": 1.134020618556701, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308701572028238e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 10784, "start": 107.84, "end": 108.48, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20065649696018384, "compression_ratio": 1.1204819277108433, "no_speech_prob": 2.210014072787092e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 10784, "start": 108.48, "end": 111.64, "text": " It completely changes the definition of what a mathematician is actually doing.", "tokens": [50397, 467, 2584, 2962, 264, 7123, 295, 437, 257, 48281, 307, 767, 884, 13, 50555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20065649696018384, "compression_ratio": 1.1204819277108433, "no_speech_prob": 2.210014072787092e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 11164, "start": 111.64, "end": 113.8, "text": " And we are going to explore exactly what that means.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 321, 366, 516, 281, 6839, 2293, 437, 300, 1355, 13, 50473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19638614890016157, "compression_ratio": 1.400943396226415, "no_speech_prob": 2.101108566646137e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 11164, "start": 114.26, "end": 117.42, "text": " So today's Deep Diet is centered on this truly mind-bending manuscript.", "tokens": [50496, 407, 965, 311, 14895, 29606, 307, 18988, 322, 341, 4908, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 23928, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19638614890016157, "compression_ratio": 1.400943396226415, "no_speech_prob": 2.101108566646137e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 11164, "start": 117.84, "end": 121.48, "text": " It was published in July 2026 by an author named Flyxion.", "tokens": [50675, 467, 390, 6572, 294, 7370, 945, 10880, 538, 364, 3793, 4926, 3235, 970, 952, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19638614890016157, "compression_ratio": 1.400943396226415, "no_speech_prob": 2.101108566646137e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 11164, "start": 121.76, "end": 122.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50871, 1779, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19638614890016157, "compression_ratio": 1.400943396226415, "no_speech_prob": 2.101108566646137e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 11164, "start": 122.24, "end": 123.66, "text": " The Geometry of Distinction.", "tokens": [50895, 440, 2876, 34730, 295, 9840, 12987, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19638614890016157, "compression_ratio": 1.400943396226415, "no_speech_prob": 2.101108566646137e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 11164, "start": 124.64, "end": 128.76, "text": " Information, representation, and structure across mathematics.", "tokens": [51015, 15357, 11, 10290, 11, 293, 3877, 2108, 18666, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19638614890016157, "compression_ratio": 1.400943396226415, "no_speech_prob": 2.101108566646137e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 11164, "start": 128.98, "end": 129.44, "text": " That's the one.", "tokens": [51232, 663, 311, 264, 472, 13, 51255], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19638614890016157, "compression_ratio": 1.400943396226415, "no_speech_prob": 2.101108566646137e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 12944, "start": 129.44, "end": 145.88, "text": " And our mission today is to take the dense, profound thesis of this manuscript and trace a single unbroken thread from that basic algebra you remember all the way to, like, chaos theory, category theory, and information theory.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 527, 4447, 965, 307, 281, 747, 264, 18011, 11, 14382, 22288, 295, 341, 23928, 293, 13508, 257, 2167, 517, 37947, 7207, 490, 300, 3875, 21989, 291, 1604, 439, 264, 636, 281, 11, 411, 11, 14158, 5261, 11, 7719, 5261, 11, 293, 1589, 5261, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0983457789701574, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.555396978748791e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 12944, "start": 146.02, "end": 146.68, "text": " It's quite a journey.", "tokens": [51194, 467, 311, 1596, 257, 4671, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0983457789701574, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.555396978748791e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 12944, "start": 146.86, "end": 147.2, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51236, 467, 307, 13, 51253], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0983457789701574, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.555396978748791e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 12944, "start": 147.34, "end": 153.2, "text": " We're going to prove to you that almost all of modern mathematics boils down to just three fundamental actions.", "tokens": [51260, 492, 434, 516, 281, 7081, 281, 291, 300, 1920, 439, 295, 4363, 18666, 35049, 760, 281, 445, 1045, 8088, 5909, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0983457789701574, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.555396978748791e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 15320, "start": 153.2, "end": 160.67999999999998, "text": " Just three actions that govern, you know, everything from how your computer compresses a file to how the universe organizes itself.", "tokens": [50365, 1449, 1045, 5909, 300, 1980, 11, 291, 458, 11, 1203, 490, 577, 428, 3820, 14778, 279, 257, 3991, 281, 577, 264, 6445, 4645, 279, 2564, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344512122017997, "compression_ratio": 1.738562091503268, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051469406431427e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 15320, "start": 160.79999999999998, "end": 160.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50745, 1779, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344512122017997, "compression_ratio": 1.738562091503268, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051469406431427e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 15320, "start": 161.26, "end": 164.94, "text": " Because according to the text, whenever you are doing math, you're doing one of three things.", "tokens": [50768, 1436, 4650, 281, 264, 2487, 11, 5699, 291, 366, 884, 5221, 11, 291, 434, 884, 472, 295, 1045, 721, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344512122017997, "compression_ratio": 1.738562091503268, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051469406431427e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 15320, "start": 165.04, "end": 171.79999999999998, "text": " You're either preserving distinctions, you're deliberately collapsing distinctions, or you are simply changing how those distinctions are represented.", "tokens": [50957, 509, 434, 2139, 33173, 1483, 49798, 11, 291, 434, 23506, 45339, 1483, 49798, 11, 420, 291, 366, 2935, 4473, 577, 729, 1483, 49798, 366, 10379, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344512122017997, "compression_ratio": 1.738562091503268, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051469406431427e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 15320, "start": 171.92, "end": 172.14, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51301, 1033, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344512122017997, "compression_ratio": 1.738562091503268, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051469406431427e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 15320, "start": 172.26, "end": 177.89999999999998, "text": " So I was trying to wrap my head around this three-action framework earlier, and I came up with an analogy to sort of ground us.", "tokens": [51318, 407, 286, 390, 1382, 281, 7019, 452, 1378, 926, 341, 1045, 12, 2894, 8388, 3071, 11, 293, 286, 1361, 493, 365, 364, 21663, 281, 1333, 295, 2727, 505, 13, 51600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344512122017997, "compression_ratio": 1.738562091503268, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051469406431427e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 15320, "start": 177.92, "end": 178.44, "text": " Let's hear it.", "tokens": [51601, 961, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344512122017997, "compression_ratio": 1.738562091503268, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051469406431427e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 17844, "start": 178.44, "end": 186.56, "text": " Okay, if you're listening to this, I want you to think of math not as a calculator, but as a massive filing system for reality.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 498, 291, 434, 4764, 281, 341, 11, 286, 528, 291, 281, 519, 295, 5221, 406, 382, 257, 24993, 11, 457, 382, 257, 5994, 26854, 1185, 337, 4103, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 17844, "start": 186.94, "end": 187.82, "text": " A filing system, okay.", "tokens": [50790, 316, 26854, 1185, 11, 1392, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 17844, "start": 188.04, "end": 188.26, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50845, 865, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 17844, "start": 188.5, "end": 191.6, "text": " Let's say you have a giant stack of physical documents.", "tokens": [50868, 961, 311, 584, 291, 362, 257, 7410, 8630, 295, 4001, 8512, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 17844, "start": 192.1, "end": 198.46, "text": " Sometimes you need to keep every single document in its own clearly labeled separate folder.", "tokens": [51048, 4803, 291, 643, 281, 1066, 633, 2167, 4166, 294, 1080, 1065, 4448, 21335, 4994, 10820, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 17844, "start": 198.64, "end": 202.34, "text": " Because you need to know that document A is not document B.", "tokens": [51375, 1436, 291, 643, 281, 458, 300, 4166, 316, 307, 406, 4166, 363, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 17844, "start": 202.46, "end": 202.98, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51566, 7587, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 17844, "start": 203.46, "end": 204.88, "text": " You preserve all the distinctions.", "tokens": [51616, 509, 15665, 439, 264, 1483, 49798, 13, 51687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 17844, "start": 205.28, "end": 206.28, "text": " Nothing gets mixed up.", "tokens": [51707, 6693, 2170, 7467, 493, 13, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 17844, "start": 206.36, "end": 207.26, "text": " That is action one.", "tokens": [51761, 663, 307, 3069, 472, 13, 51806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14342726071675618, "compression_ratio": 1.6556776556776556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492056201591887e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 20726, "start": 207.26, "end": 208.95999999999998, "text": " A perfectly organized archive.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 6239, 9983, 23507, 13, 50450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12434420634790794, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.2943679331481328e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 20726, "start": 209.1, "end": 209.32, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50457, 1779, 13, 50468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12434420634790794, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.2943679331481328e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 20726, "start": 209.57999999999998, "end": 215.7, "text": " But then there are times when, say, you're doing your taxes, and you have this massive pile of grocery receipts.", "tokens": [50481, 583, 550, 456, 366, 1413, 562, 11, 584, 11, 291, 434, 884, 428, 10041, 11, 293, 291, 362, 341, 5994, 14375, 295, 14410, 2268, 48908, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12434420634790794, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.2943679331481328e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 20726, "start": 215.84, "end": 216.76, "text": " Oh, the worst.", "tokens": [50794, 876, 11, 264, 5855, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12434420634790794, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.2943679331481328e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 20726, "start": 216.89999999999998, "end": 218.14, "text": " Yeah, the absolute worst.", "tokens": [50847, 865, 11, 264, 8236, 5855, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12434420634790794, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.2943679331481328e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 20726, "start": 218.39999999999998, "end": 225.12, "text": " But for your specific tax purposes, you just do not care about the difference between a receipt for apples and a receipt for bread.", "tokens": [50922, 583, 337, 428, 2685, 3366, 9932, 11, 291, 445, 360, 406, 1127, 466, 264, 2649, 1296, 257, 33882, 337, 16814, 293, 257, 33882, 337, 5961, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12434420634790794, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.2943679331481328e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 20726, "start": 225.23999999999998, "end": 226.48, "text": " They're all just food expenses.", "tokens": [51264, 814, 434, 439, 445, 1755, 15506, 13, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12434420634790794, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.2943679331481328e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 20726, "start": 226.7, "end": 227.14, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51337, 7587, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12434420634790794, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.2943679331481328e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 22714, "start": 227.14, "end": 231.23999999999998, "text": " So you intentionally dump them all into one giant shoebox.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 291, 22062, 11430, 552, 439, 666, 472, 7410, 12796, 4995, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 22714, "start": 231.66, "end": 234.44, "text": " You deliberately destroy the differences between them.", "tokens": [50591, 509, 23506, 5293, 264, 7300, 1296, 552, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 22714, "start": 234.77999999999997, "end": 236.23999999999998, "text": " You collapse the distinctions.", "tokens": [50747, 509, 15584, 264, 1483, 49798, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 22714, "start": 236.77999999999997, "end": 237.85999999999999, "text": " That is action two.", "tokens": [50847, 663, 307, 3069, 732, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 22714, "start": 238.05999999999997, "end": 240.39999999999998, "text": " The intentional forgetting of your relevant details.", "tokens": [50911, 440, 21935, 25428, 295, 428, 7340, 4365, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 22714, "start": 240.51999999999998, "end": 240.77999999999997, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51034, 1079, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 22714, "start": 240.95999999999998, "end": 241.17999999999998, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51056, 1033, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 22714, "start": 241.27999999999997, "end": 242.22, "text": " So what's the third action?", "tokens": [51072, 407, 437, 311, 264, 2636, 3069, 30, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 22714, "start": 242.33999999999997, "end": 247.77999999999997, "text": " Action three is when you take a critical document and you translate it from English to Spanish.", "tokens": [51125, 16261, 1045, 307, 562, 291, 747, 257, 4924, 4166, 293, 291, 13799, 309, 490, 3669, 281, 8058, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 22714, "start": 248.04, "end": 252.5, "text": " You haven't merged it with another document, and you haven't lost any of its original meaning.", "tokens": [51410, 509, 2378, 380, 36427, 309, 365, 1071, 4166, 11, 293, 291, 2378, 380, 2731, 604, 295, 1080, 3380, 3620, 13, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2028823505748402, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096242840182626e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 25250, "start": 252.5, "end": 254.34, "text": " You just change the representation of it.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 445, 1319, 264, 10290, 295, 309, 13, 50457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19299634297688803, "compression_ratio": 1.4294117647058824, "no_speech_prob": 1.3823484457803348e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 25250, "start": 254.56, "end": 254.72, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50468, 1779, 13, 50476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19299634297688803, "compression_ratio": 1.4294117647058824, "no_speech_prob": 1.3823484457803348e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 25250, "start": 254.86, "end": 256.96, "text": " So that completely different person can read it.", "tokens": [50483, 407, 300, 2584, 819, 954, 393, 1401, 309, 13, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19299634297688803, "compression_ratio": 1.4294117647058824, "no_speech_prob": 1.3823484457803348e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 25250, "start": 257.34, "end": 260.38, "text": " The structure is identical, but the language has shifted.", "tokens": [50607, 440, 3877, 307, 14800, 11, 457, 264, 2856, 575, 18892, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19299634297688803, "compression_ratio": 1.4294117647058824, "no_speech_prob": 1.3823484457803348e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 25250, "start": 260.58, "end": 265.34, "text": " That filing system analogy maps perfectly onto the architecture we're about to explore.", "tokens": [50769, 663, 26854, 1185, 21663, 11317, 6239, 3911, 264, 9482, 321, 434, 466, 281, 6839, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19299634297688803, "compression_ratio": 1.4294117647058824, "no_speech_prob": 1.3823484457803348e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 26534, "start": 265.34, "end": 278.59999999999997, "text": " Because, you know, whether you're navigating a geometric space or analyzing a probability distribution or training a complex machine learning algorithm, you're constantly asking the same fundamental questions.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 11, 291, 458, 11, 1968, 291, 434, 32054, 257, 33246, 1901, 420, 23663, 257, 8482, 7316, 420, 3097, 257, 3997, 3479, 2539, 9284, 11, 291, 434, 6460, 3365, 264, 912, 8088, 1651, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566684223781122, "compression_ratio": 1.6597938144329898, "no_speech_prob": 1.680957456562382e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 26534, "start": 279.29999999999995, "end": 279.56, "text": " Which are?", "tokens": [51063, 3013, 366, 30, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566684223781122, "compression_ratio": 1.6597938144329898, "no_speech_prob": 1.680957456562382e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 26534, "start": 279.59999999999997, "end": 281.91999999999996, "text": " Which distinctions survive this process?", "tokens": [51078, 3013, 1483, 49798, 7867, 341, 1399, 30, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566684223781122, "compression_ratio": 1.6597938144329898, "no_speech_prob": 1.680957456562382e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 26534, "start": 282.4, "end": 283.26, "text": " Which ones are forgotten?", "tokens": [51218, 3013, 2306, 366, 11832, 30, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566684223781122, "compression_ratio": 1.6597938144329898, "no_speech_prob": 1.680957456562382e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 26534, "start": 284.0, "end": 286.73999999999995, "text": " And which ones are merely expressed in a new language?", "tokens": [51298, 400, 597, 2306, 366, 17003, 12675, 294, 257, 777, 2856, 30, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566684223781122, "compression_ratio": 1.6597938144329898, "no_speech_prob": 1.680957456562382e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 26534, "start": 286.91999999999996, "end": 291.5, "text": " So let's start with the first action and look at the actual engines that drive these changes.", "tokens": [51444, 407, 718, 311, 722, 365, 264, 700, 3069, 293, 574, 412, 264, 3539, 12982, 300, 3332, 613, 2962, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566684223781122, "compression_ratio": 1.6597938144329898, "no_speech_prob": 1.680957456562382e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 26534, "start": 291.65999999999997, "end": 293.14, "text": " I want to talk about functions.", "tokens": [51681, 286, 528, 281, 751, 466, 6828, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566684223781122, "compression_ratio": 1.6597938144329898, "no_speech_prob": 1.680957456562382e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 26534, "start": 293.14, "end": 294.7, "text": " Ah, functions.", "tokens": [51755, 2438, 11, 6828, 13, 51833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566684223781122, "compression_ratio": 1.6597938144329898, "no_speech_prob": 1.680957456562382e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 29534, "start": 295.34, "end": 296.02, "text": " The classic.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7230, 13, 50399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 29534, "start": 296.2, "end": 296.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50408, 1779, 13, 50418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 29534, "start": 296.47999999999996, "end": 300.46, "text": " Because, again, I was taught that a function is just a rule, like a factory machine.", "tokens": [50422, 1436, 11, 797, 11, 286, 390, 5928, 300, 257, 2445, 307, 445, 257, 4978, 11, 411, 257, 9265, 3479, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 29534, "start": 300.64, "end": 304.76, "text": " You put an X on the conveyor belt, the machine hammers on it, and a Y comes out the other side.", "tokens": [50630, 509, 829, 364, 1783, 322, 264, 18053, 2454, 10750, 11, 264, 3479, 36600, 433, 322, 309, 11, 293, 257, 398, 1487, 484, 264, 661, 1252, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 29534, "start": 304.82, "end": 304.97999999999996, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50839, 1779, 13, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 29534, "start": 305.06, "end": 306.58, "text": " The classical input-output mapping.", "tokens": [50851, 440, 13735, 4846, 12, 346, 2582, 18350, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 29534, "start": 307.11999999999995, "end": 310.7, "text": " And it's a perfectly functional way to teach basic algebra.", "tokens": [50954, 400, 309, 311, 257, 6239, 11745, 636, 281, 2924, 3875, 21989, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 29534, "start": 311.09999999999997, "end": 311.44, "text": " But?", "tokens": [51153, 583, 30, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 29534, "start": 311.73999999999995, "end": 317.02, "text": " But the text argues that it's intentionally economical to the point of being deceptive.", "tokens": [51185, 583, 264, 2487, 38218, 300, 309, 311, 22062, 42473, 281, 264, 935, 295, 885, 368, 1336, 488, 13, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 29534, "start": 317.28, "end": 317.71999999999997, "text": " Deceptive.", "tokens": [51462, 1346, 1336, 488, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 29534, "start": 317.88, "end": 318.12, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51492, 3153, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13308224251599815, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892572852004404e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 31812, "start": 318.12, "end": 321.02, "text": " Yeah, because it tells you the mechanics of the evaluation, sure.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 570, 309, 5112, 291, 264, 12939, 295, 264, 13344, 11, 988, 13, 50510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14288863506945934, "compression_ratio": 1.5587044534412955, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 31812, "start": 321.74, "end": 326.48, "text": " But it completely conceals what the function is fundamentally accomplishing on a structural level.", "tokens": [50546, 583, 309, 2584, 10413, 1124, 437, 264, 2445, 307, 17879, 6548, 3807, 322, 257, 15067, 1496, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14288863506945934, "compression_ratio": 1.5587044534412955, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 31812, "start": 326.7, "end": 328.04, "text": " Okay, so how should we look at it?", "tokens": [50794, 1033, 11, 370, 577, 820, 321, 574, 412, 309, 30, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14288863506945934, "compression_ratio": 1.5587044534412955, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 31812, "start": 328.58, "end": 332.64, "text": " To really grasp modern math, you have to pivot to a much richer view.", "tokens": [50888, 1407, 534, 21743, 4363, 5221, 11, 291, 362, 281, 14538, 281, 257, 709, 29021, 1910, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14288863506945934, "compression_ratio": 1.5587044534412955, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 31812, "start": 333.58, "end": 340.92, "text": " Imagine a function not as a machine, but as a geological force transforming an entire landscape of distinct states.", "tokens": [51138, 11739, 257, 2445, 406, 382, 257, 3479, 11, 457, 382, 257, 1519, 4383, 3464, 27210, 364, 2302, 9661, 295, 10644, 4368, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14288863506945934, "compression_ratio": 1.5587044534412955, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 34092, "start": 340.92, "end": 342.42, "text": " A landscape of states.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 9661, 295, 4368, 13, 50440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10666717182506215, "compression_ratio": 1.286764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609824851644082e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 34092, "start": 342.6, "end": 353.74, "text": " Okay, so instead of one X on a conveyor belt, I need to visualize a massive field where every single point on the ground is a completely distinct input.", "tokens": [50449, 1033, 11, 370, 2602, 295, 472, 1783, 322, 257, 18053, 2454, 10750, 11, 286, 643, 281, 23273, 257, 5994, 2519, 689, 633, 2167, 935, 322, 264, 2727, 307, 257, 2584, 10644, 4846, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10666717182506215, "compression_ratio": 1.286764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609824851644082e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 35374, "start": 353.74, "end": 354.94, "text": " Yes, exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 2293, 13, 50425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571113686812551, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940833079942316e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 35374, "start": 355.62, "end": 362.78000000000003, "text": " Before you apply any mathematical function, every element in your starting space, what we call the domain, is completely distinct from every other element.", "tokens": [50459, 4546, 291, 3079, 604, 18894, 2445, 11, 633, 4478, 294, 428, 2891, 1901, 11, 437, 321, 818, 264, 9274, 11, 307, 2584, 10644, 490, 633, 661, 4478, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571113686812551, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940833079942316e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 35374, "start": 362.90000000000003, "end": 363.98, "text": " They all have their own identity.", "tokens": [50823, 814, 439, 362, 641, 1065, 6575, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571113686812551, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940833079942316e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 35374, "start": 364.26, "end": 365.86, "text": " Right, they possess their own sovereign identity.", "tokens": [50891, 1779, 11, 436, 17490, 641, 1065, 28756, 6575, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571113686812551, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940833079942316e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 35374, "start": 366.26, "end": 372.0, "text": " But when the function acts on that landscape, it forces those points to move to a new landscape, the target space.", "tokens": [50991, 583, 562, 264, 2445, 10672, 322, 300, 9661, 11, 309, 5874, 729, 2793, 281, 1286, 281, 257, 777, 9661, 11, 264, 3779, 1901, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571113686812551, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940833079942316e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 35374, "start": 372.08, "end": 372.86, "text": " Okay, I'm with you.", "tokens": [51282, 1033, 11, 286, 478, 365, 291, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571113686812551, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940833079942316e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 35374, "start": 373.04, "end": 378.96000000000004, "text": " And the first major possibility is that the function preserves every single distinction from the original landscape.", "tokens": [51330, 400, 264, 700, 2563, 7959, 307, 300, 264, 2445, 1183, 9054, 633, 2167, 16844, 490, 264, 3380, 9661, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571113686812551, "compression_ratio": 1.7353951890034365, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940833079942316e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 37896, "start": 378.96, "end": 385.76, "text": " So if no two inputs ever land on the exact same output, the text refers to this as an injective function.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 572, 732, 15743, 1562, 2117, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 5598, 11, 264, 2487, 14942, 281, 341, 382, 364, 10711, 488, 2445, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14052421355915962, "compression_ratio": 1.6401515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250544324966418e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 37896, "start": 386.03999999999996, "end": 386.53999999999996, "text": " Injective.", "tokens": [50719, 682, 1020, 488, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14052421355915962, "compression_ratio": 1.6401515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250544324966418e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 37896, "start": 386.64, "end": 388.18, "text": " Okay, so that lines up with action one.", "tokens": [50749, 1033, 11, 370, 300, 3876, 493, 365, 3069, 472, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14052421355915962, "compression_ratio": 1.6401515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250544324966418e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 37896, "start": 388.94, "end": 391.2, "text": " My documents all stay in separate folders.", "tokens": [50864, 1222, 8512, 439, 1754, 294, 4994, 31082, 13, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14052421355915962, "compression_ratio": 1.6401515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250544324966418e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 37896, "start": 391.82, "end": 392.96, "text": " Nothing gets mixed up.", "tokens": [51008, 6693, 2170, 7467, 493, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14052421355915962, "compression_ratio": 1.6401515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250544324966418e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 37896, "start": 393.24, "end": 393.71999999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51079, 7587, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14052421355915962, "compression_ratio": 1.6401515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250544324966418e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 37896, "start": 394.0, "end": 399.17999999999995, "text": " The critical feature of an injective function is that no information is ever destroyed.", "tokens": [51117, 440, 4924, 4111, 295, 364, 10711, 488, 2445, 307, 300, 572, 1589, 307, 1562, 8937, 13, 51376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14052421355915962, "compression_ratio": 1.6401515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250544324966418e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 37896, "start": 399.94, "end": 407.47999999999996, "text": " Because every single output traces back to exactly one unique input, you can always reverse engineer the process.", "tokens": [51414, 1436, 633, 2167, 5598, 26076, 646, 281, 2293, 472, 3845, 4846, 11, 291, 393, 1009, 9943, 11403, 264, 1399, 13, 51791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14052421355915962, "compression_ratio": 1.6401515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250544324966418e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 40748, "start": 407.48, "end": 409.6, "text": " Perfect reconstruction is possible.", "tokens": [50365, 10246, 31565, 307, 1944, 13, 50471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 40748, "start": 409.8, "end": 410.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50481, 1779, 13, 50491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 40748, "start": 410.18, "end": 413.46000000000004, "text": " You haven't lost the ability to distinguish between your starting points.", "tokens": [50500, 509, 2378, 380, 2731, 264, 3485, 281, 20206, 1296, 428, 2891, 2793, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 40748, "start": 413.62, "end": 419.28000000000003, "text": " But the function might not actually reach all the possible points in the new landscape, right?", "tokens": [50672, 583, 264, 2445, 1062, 406, 767, 2524, 439, 264, 1944, 2793, 294, 264, 777, 9661, 11, 558, 30, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 40748, "start": 419.40000000000003, "end": 423.16, "text": " Like, it might preserve all my documents, but only fill up half the filing cabinet.", "tokens": [50961, 1743, 11, 309, 1062, 15665, 439, 452, 8512, 11, 457, 787, 2836, 493, 1922, 264, 26854, 15188, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 40748, "start": 423.32, "end": 424.22, "text": " That is a great point.", "tokens": [51157, 663, 307, 257, 869, 935, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 40748, "start": 424.48, "end": 428.0, "text": " And it introduces the second major concept, surjective function.", "tokens": [51215, 400, 309, 31472, 264, 1150, 2563, 3410, 11, 1022, 1020, 488, 2445, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 40748, "start": 428.12, "end": 428.64000000000004, "text": " Surjective.", "tokens": [51397, 6732, 1020, 488, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 40748, "start": 428.74, "end": 428.88, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51428, 1779, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 40748, "start": 428.98, "end": 431.92, "text": " Surjectivity does not care about preserving distinctions.", "tokens": [51440, 6732, 1020, 4253, 775, 406, 1127, 466, 33173, 1483, 49798, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 40748, "start": 432.44, "end": 433.58000000000004, "text": " It only cares about coverage.", "tokens": [51613, 467, 787, 12310, 466, 9645, 13, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18114574619981108, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352505949873472e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 43358, "start": 433.58, "end": 438.53999999999996, "text": " A surjective function exhausts the absolute potential of the target space.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 1022, 1020, 488, 2445, 14687, 82, 264, 8236, 3995, 295, 264, 3779, 1901, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827853441238403, "compression_ratio": 1.7300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 1.554966008385228e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 43358, "start": 438.8, "end": 439.71999999999997, "text": " So it hits everything.", "tokens": [50626, 407, 309, 8664, 1203, 13, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827853441238403, "compression_ratio": 1.7300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 1.554966008385228e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 43358, "start": 440.0, "end": 444.3, "text": " It guarantees that every single possible output is hit by at least one input.", "tokens": [50686, 467, 32567, 300, 633, 2167, 1944, 5598, 307, 2045, 538, 412, 1935, 472, 4846, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827853441238403, "compression_ratio": 1.7300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 1.554966008385228e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 43358, "start": 444.56, "end": 450.34, "text": " Okay, so if a function manages to do both, if it perfectly preserves every distinction so nothing is mixed up,", "tokens": [50914, 1033, 11, 370, 498, 257, 2445, 22489, 281, 360, 1293, 11, 498, 309, 6239, 1183, 9054, 633, 16844, 370, 1825, 307, 7467, 493, 11, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827853441238403, "compression_ratio": 1.7300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 1.554966008385228e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 43358, "start": 450.58, "end": 454.03999999999996, "text": " and it hits every single possible output in the new space.", "tokens": [51215, 293, 309, 8664, 633, 2167, 1944, 5598, 294, 264, 777, 1901, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827853441238403, "compression_ratio": 1.7300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 1.554966008385228e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 43358, "start": 454.4, "end": 456.76, "text": " Then you are looking at a bijective function.", "tokens": [51406, 1396, 291, 366, 1237, 412, 257, 3228, 1020, 488, 2445, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827853441238403, "compression_ratio": 1.7300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 1.554966008385228e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 45676, "start": 456.76, "end": 461.92, "text": " It establishes a flawless one-to-one correspondence between the two landscapes.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 8327, 279, 257, 45693, 472, 12, 1353, 12, 546, 38135, 1296, 264, 732, 29822, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 45676, "start": 462.03999999999996, "end": 463.76, "text": " Nothing is identified with anything else.", "tokens": [50629, 6693, 307, 9234, 365, 1340, 1646, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 45676, "start": 463.8, "end": 465.08, "text": " And nothing is left unused.", "tokens": [50717, 400, 1825, 307, 1411, 44383, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 45676, "start": 465.26, "end": 465.46, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50790, 1779, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 45676, "start": 465.59999999999997, "end": 468.08, "text": " It is the gold standard of perfect reversibility.", "tokens": [50807, 467, 307, 264, 3821, 3832, 295, 2176, 14582, 2841, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 45676, "start": 468.21999999999997, "end": 470.03999999999996, "text": " See, this is where my intuition hits a wall.", "tokens": [50938, 3008, 11, 341, 307, 689, 452, 24002, 8664, 257, 2929, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 45676, "start": 470.42, "end": 470.96, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51048, 1012, 370, 30, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 45676, "start": 471.18, "end": 476.08, "text": " Well, if projective functions are this perfect reversible ideal where no data is lost,", "tokens": [51086, 1042, 11, 498, 1716, 488, 6828, 366, 341, 2176, 44788, 7157, 689, 572, 1412, 307, 2731, 11, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 45676, "start": 476.65999999999997, "end": 479.65999999999997, "text": " aren't non-injective functions just fundamentally broken?", "tokens": [51360, 3212, 380, 2107, 12, 259, 1020, 488, 6828, 445, 17879, 5463, 30, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 45676, "start": 479.9, "end": 480.24, "text": " Broken.", "tokens": [51522, 46624, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1827903323703342, "compression_ratio": 1.615686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.7932530460562646e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 48024, "start": 480.24, "end": 487.72, "text": " If a function forces two distinct inputs to crash into the exact same output, it destroys information.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 2445, 5874, 732, 10644, 15743, 281, 8252, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 5598, 11, 309, 36714, 1589, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18655484517415363, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485461863142593e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 48024, "start": 488.32, "end": 493.12, "text": " Why would mathematicians spend so much time studying functions that actively destroy information?", "tokens": [50769, 1545, 576, 32811, 2567, 3496, 370, 709, 565, 7601, 6828, 300, 13022, 5293, 1589, 30, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18655484517415363, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485461863142593e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 48024, "start": 493.6, "end": 498.88, "text": " That instinct right there, that information loss, is a deficiency or a flaw that's incredibly common.", "tokens": [51033, 663, 16556, 558, 456, 11, 300, 1589, 4470, 11, 307, 257, 37500, 420, 257, 13717, 300, 311, 6252, 2689, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18655484517415363, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485461863142593e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 48024, "start": 499.28000000000003, "end": 502.7, "text": " But the text flips that assumption completely upside down.", "tokens": [51317, 583, 264, 2487, 40249, 300, 15302, 2584, 14119, 760, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18655484517415363, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485461863142593e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 48024, "start": 502.84000000000003, "end": 503.16, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51495, 4083, 30, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18655484517415363, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485461863142593e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 48024, "start": 503.48, "end": 503.76, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51527, 1079, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18655484517415363, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485461863142593e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 48024, "start": 504.06, "end": 506.58, "text": " In mathematics, information loss is not a mistake.", "tokens": [51556, 682, 18666, 11, 1589, 4470, 307, 406, 257, 6146, 13, 51682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18655484517415363, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485461863142593e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 48024, "start": 507.08, "end": 509.32, "text": " It is a highly structured, intentional tool.", "tokens": [51707, 467, 307, 257, 5405, 18519, 11, 21935, 2290, 13, 51819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18655484517415363, "compression_ratio": 1.709090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485461863142593e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 50932, "start": 509.32, "end": 514.64, "text": " When a function collapses distinctions, it doesn't just randomly mash things together.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 257, 2445, 48765, 1483, 49798, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 445, 16979, 31344, 721, 1214, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17422477944383344, "compression_ratio": 1.6293436293436294, "no_speech_prob": 1.721604846530167e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 50932, "start": 514.96, "end": 516.04, "text": " It does so systematically.", "tokens": [50647, 467, 775, 370, 39531, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17422477944383344, "compression_ratio": 1.6293436293436294, "no_speech_prob": 1.721604846530167e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 50932, "start": 516.3199999999999, "end": 517.92, "text": " Systematically collapsing things.", "tokens": [50715, 8910, 5030, 45339, 721, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17422477944383344, "compression_ratio": 1.6293436293436294, "no_speech_prob": 1.721604846530167e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 50932, "start": 518.12, "end": 518.36, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50805, 1033, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17422477944383344, "compression_ratio": 1.6293436293436294, "no_speech_prob": 1.721604846530167e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 50932, "start": 518.56, "end": 521.3, "text": " To explain this, the author introduces the concept of fibers.", "tokens": [50827, 1407, 2903, 341, 11, 264, 3793, 31472, 264, 3410, 295, 25252, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17422477944383344, "compression_ratio": 1.6293436293436294, "no_speech_prob": 1.721604846530167e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 50932, "start": 521.78, "end": 522.42, "text": " Fibers.", "tokens": [50988, 479, 897, 433, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17422477944383344, "compression_ratio": 1.6293436293436294, "no_speech_prob": 1.721604846530167e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 50932, "start": 523.0, "end": 525.04, "text": " Like threads connecting the two landscapes.", "tokens": [51049, 1743, 19314, 11015, 264, 732, 29822, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17422477944383344, "compression_ratio": 1.6293436293436294, "no_speech_prob": 1.721604846530167e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 50932, "start": 525.36, "end": 527.06, "text": " That's actually a good way to visualize it.", "tokens": [51167, 663, 311, 767, 257, 665, 636, 281, 23273, 309, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17422477944383344, "compression_ratio": 1.6293436293436294, "no_speech_prob": 1.721604846530167e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 50932, "start": 528.14, "end": 535.86, "text": " Think of a fiber as a collection of inputs from your starting landscape that all map to the exact same output.", "tokens": [51306, 6557, 295, 257, 12874, 382, 257, 5765, 295, 15743, 490, 428, 2891, 9661, 300, 439, 4471, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 5598, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17422477944383344, "compression_ratio": 1.6293436293436294, "no_speech_prob": 1.721604846530167e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 53586, "start": 535.86, "end": 540.28, "text": " So if my function isn't injective, multiple inputs are colliding.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 452, 2445, 1943, 380, 10711, 488, 11, 3866, 15743, 366, 1263, 2819, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428839206695557, "compression_ratio": 1.5144508670520231, "no_speech_prob": 1.617153893435086e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 53586, "start": 540.58, "end": 540.88, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50601, 1779, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428839206695557, "compression_ratio": 1.5144508670520231, "no_speech_prob": 1.617153893435086e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 53586, "start": 541.28, "end": 544.1, "text": " The fiber is the family of all those colliding points.", "tokens": [50636, 440, 12874, 307, 264, 1605, 295, 439, 729, 1263, 2819, 2793, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428839206695557, "compression_ratio": 1.5144508670520231, "no_speech_prob": 1.617153893435086e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 53586, "start": 544.54, "end": 553.16, "text": " The function has made a deliberate mathematical choice that, for its specific purposes, those points are completely indistinguishable.", "tokens": [50799, 440, 2445, 575, 1027, 257, 30515, 18894, 3922, 300, 11, 337, 1080, 2685, 9932, 11, 729, 2793, 366, 2584, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17428839206695557, "compression_ratio": 1.5144508670520231, "no_speech_prob": 1.617153893435086e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 55316, "start": 553.16, "end": 557.02, "text": " Let me test this with an example from the source material, just to make sure I'm getting it.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 385, 1500, 341, 365, 364, 1365, 490, 264, 4009, 2527, 11, 445, 281, 652, 988, 286, 478, 1242, 309, 13, 50558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12734213220067772, "compression_ratio": 1.7094972067039107, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106017344461043e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 55316, "start": 557.0799999999999, "end": 558.68, "text": " The absolute value function.", "tokens": [50561, 440, 8236, 2158, 2445, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12734213220067772, "compression_ratio": 1.7094972067039107, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106017344461043e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 55316, "start": 558.9399999999999, "end": 560.1, "text": " Ah, perfect example.", "tokens": [50654, 2438, 11, 2176, 1365, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12734213220067772, "compression_ratio": 1.7094972067039107, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106017344461043e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 55316, "start": 560.28, "end": 562.92, "text": " If I take the absolute value of 5, the answer is 5.", "tokens": [50721, 759, 286, 747, 264, 8236, 2158, 295, 1025, 11, 264, 1867, 307, 1025, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12734213220067772, "compression_ratio": 1.7094972067039107, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106017344461043e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 55316, "start": 563.02, "end": 566.42, "text": " If I take the absolute value of negative 5, the answer is also 5.", "tokens": [50858, 759, 286, 747, 264, 8236, 2158, 295, 3671, 1025, 11, 264, 1867, 307, 611, 1025, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12734213220067772, "compression_ratio": 1.7094972067039107, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106017344461043e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 55316, "start": 566.6, "end": 568.76, "text": " A beautifully simple illustration of a fiber.", "tokens": [51037, 316, 16525, 2199, 22645, 295, 257, 12874, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12734213220067772, "compression_ratio": 1.7094972067039107, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106017344461043e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 56876, "start": 568.76, "end": 572.0, "text": " So the absolute value function creates a collision.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 8236, 2158, 2445, 7829, 257, 24644, 13, 50527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 56876, "start": 572.48, "end": 575.74, "text": " It takes 5 and negative 5 and collapses them into the exact same output.", "tokens": [50551, 467, 2516, 1025, 293, 3671, 1025, 293, 48765, 552, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 5598, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 56876, "start": 575.84, "end": 576.66, "text": " It has a blind spot.", "tokens": [50719, 467, 575, 257, 6865, 4008, 13, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 56876, "start": 576.9399999999999, "end": 577.22, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50774, 7587, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 56876, "start": 577.34, "end": 578.36, "text": " A mathematical blind spot.", "tokens": [50794, 316, 18894, 6865, 4008, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 56876, "start": 578.56, "end": 583.68, "text": " It completely ignores the sign of the number, whether it's on the positive side of the number line or the negative side.", "tokens": [50855, 467, 2584, 5335, 2706, 264, 1465, 295, 264, 1230, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 322, 264, 3353, 1252, 295, 264, 1230, 1622, 420, 264, 3671, 1252, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 56876, "start": 583.9399999999999, "end": 585.74, "text": " But it doesn't forget the magnitude.", "tokens": [51124, 583, 309, 1177, 380, 2870, 264, 15668, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 56876, "start": 586.34, "end": 589.02, "text": " The distance from zero is preserved perfectly.", "tokens": [51244, 440, 4560, 490, 4018, 307, 22242, 6239, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 56876, "start": 589.48, "end": 594.96, "text": " And that structured forgetting is precisely what makes the absolute value function useful.", "tokens": [51401, 400, 300, 18519, 25428, 307, 13402, 437, 1669, 264, 8236, 2158, 2445, 4420, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 56876, "start": 595.26, "end": 596.36, "text": " Because it's intentional.", "tokens": [51690, 1436, 309, 311, 21935, 13, 51745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16927013397216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7836879432624113, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125537521231696e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 59636, "start": 596.36, "end": 603.6, "text": " Right. It intentionally declares that the distinction between positive and negative is irrelevant for whatever distance you were trying to calculate.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 467, 22062, 979, 19415, 300, 264, 16844, 1296, 3353, 293, 3671, 307, 28682, 337, 2035, 4560, 291, 645, 1382, 281, 8873, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12806238986477994, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841239131743733e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 59636, "start": 604.1800000000001, "end": 608.3000000000001, "text": " You're intentionally throwing away the sign to focus purely on the magnitude.", "tokens": [50756, 509, 434, 22062, 10238, 1314, 264, 1465, 281, 1879, 17491, 322, 264, 15668, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12806238986477994, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841239131743733e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 59636, "start": 608.6, "end": 609.74, "text": " Okay. That makes sense.", "tokens": [50977, 1033, 13, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12806238986477994, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841239131743733e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 59636, "start": 609.86, "end": 615.6, "text": " In linear algebra, this concept of the mathematical blind spot is formalized into something called the kernel.", "tokens": [51040, 682, 8213, 21989, 11, 341, 3410, 295, 264, 18894, 6865, 4008, 307, 9860, 1602, 666, 746, 1219, 264, 28256, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12806238986477994, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841239131743733e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 59636, "start": 616.0, "end": 619.1800000000001, "text": " The kernel. That sounds intimidating. How does that work in geometry?", "tokens": [51347, 440, 28256, 13, 663, 3263, 29714, 13, 1012, 775, 300, 589, 294, 18426, 30, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12806238986477994, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841239131743733e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 59636, "start": 619.52, "end": 620.7, "text": " It's not as scary as it sounds.", "tokens": [51523, 467, 311, 406, 382, 6958, 382, 309, 3263, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12806238986477994, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841239131743733e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 62070, "start": 620.7, "end": 627.1, "text": " Imagine you have a three-dimensional object, like a cube, and you shine a light on it to create a two-dimensional shadow on the wall.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 291, 362, 257, 1045, 12, 18759, 2657, 11, 411, 257, 13728, 11, 293, 291, 12207, 257, 1442, 322, 309, 281, 1884, 257, 732, 12, 18759, 8576, 322, 264, 2929, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031774420487254, "compression_ratio": 1.716, "no_speech_prob": 1.943049453972945e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 62070, "start": 627.24, "end": 629.2, "text": " Okay. 3D cube, 2D shadow.", "tokens": [50692, 1033, 13, 805, 35, 13728, 11, 568, 35, 8576, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031774420487254, "compression_ratio": 1.716, "no_speech_prob": 1.943049453972945e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 62070, "start": 629.5200000000001, "end": 633.9000000000001, "text": " The transformation from a 3D object to a 2D shadow loses information.", "tokens": [50806, 440, 9887, 490, 257, 805, 35, 2657, 281, 257, 568, 35, 8576, 18293, 1589, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031774420487254, "compression_ratio": 1.716, "no_speech_prob": 1.943049453972945e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 62070, "start": 634.36, "end": 635.34, "text": " You lose the depth.", "tokens": [51048, 509, 3624, 264, 7161, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031774420487254, "compression_ratio": 1.716, "no_speech_prob": 1.943049453972945e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 62070, "start": 635.62, "end": 635.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51111, 1779, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031774420487254, "compression_ratio": 1.716, "no_speech_prob": 1.943049453972945e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 62070, "start": 636.34, "end": 640.1, "text": " The kernel is the formal mathematical description of that lost depth.", "tokens": [51147, 440, 28256, 307, 264, 9860, 18894, 3855, 295, 300, 2731, 7161, 13, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031774420487254, "compression_ratio": 1.716, "no_speech_prob": 1.943049453972945e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 62070, "start": 640.84, "end": 644.2, "text": " It is the set of all directions that the transformation simply cannot see.", "tokens": [51372, 467, 307, 264, 992, 295, 439, 11095, 300, 264, 9887, 2935, 2644, 536, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031774420487254, "compression_ratio": 1.716, "no_speech_prob": 1.943049453972945e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 62070, "start": 644.34, "end": 645.6, "text": " Because it's blind to them.", "tokens": [51547, 1436, 309, 311, 6865, 281, 552, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031774420487254, "compression_ratio": 1.716, "no_speech_prob": 1.943049453972945e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 64560, "start": 645.6, "end": 653.26, "text": " Yes. Any movement strictly along the direction of the kernel produces absolutely zero observable change in the output shadow.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 2639, 3963, 20792, 2051, 264, 3513, 295, 264, 28256, 14725, 3122, 4018, 9951, 712, 1319, 294, 264, 5598, 8576, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12017120255364312, "compression_ratio": 1.5377777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.3147464887619531e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 64560, "start": 653.6800000000001, "end": 658.4, "text": " It is a precise geometric measurement of the transformation's blindness.", "tokens": [50769, 467, 307, 257, 13600, 33246, 13160, 295, 264, 9887, 311, 46101, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12017120255364312, "compression_ratio": 1.5377777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.3147464887619531e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 64560, "start": 659.02, "end": 667.26, "text": " Okay. So if every function has a specific blind spot and a specific way it collapses information, how does that help us understand math as a whole?", "tokens": [51036, 1033, 13, 407, 498, 633, 2445, 575, 257, 2685, 6865, 4008, 293, 257, 2685, 636, 309, 48765, 1589, 11, 577, 775, 300, 854, 505, 1223, 5221, 382, 257, 1379, 30, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12017120255364312, "compression_ratio": 1.5377777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.3147464887619531e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 66726, "start": 667.26, "end": 672.6, "text": " Oh, it leads to one of the most profound structural realizations in all of algebra.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 309, 6689, 281, 472, 295, 264, 881, 14382, 15067, 957, 14455, 294, 439, 295, 21989, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757421071550488, "compression_ratio": 1.717241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130199610552397e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 66726, "start": 673.1, "end": 676.64, "text": " The text leans heavily on this. It's called the first isomorphism theorem.", "tokens": [50657, 440, 2487, 476, 599, 10950, 322, 341, 13, 467, 311, 1219, 264, 700, 307, 32702, 1434, 20904, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757421071550488, "compression_ratio": 1.717241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130199610552397e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 66726, "start": 677.06, "end": 682.62, "text": " The first isomorphism theorem. The text treats this almost like a holy grail. Let's unpack it. What does it actually do?", "tokens": [50855, 440, 700, 307, 32702, 1434, 20904, 13, 440, 2487, 19566, 341, 1920, 411, 257, 10622, 1295, 388, 13, 961, 311, 26699, 309, 13, 708, 775, 309, 767, 360, 30, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757421071550488, "compression_ratio": 1.717241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130199610552397e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 66726, "start": 682.86, "end": 687.68, "text": " It reveals a universal architecture hiding inside every single mathematical transformation.", "tokens": [51145, 467, 20893, 257, 11455, 9482, 10596, 1854, 633, 2167, 18894, 9887, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757421071550488, "compression_ratio": 1.717241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130199610552397e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 66726, "start": 688.34, "end": 696.52, "text": " The theorem proves that every transformation you can possibly imagine is not a single action, but secretly a two-step process.", "tokens": [51419, 440, 20904, 25019, 300, 633, 9887, 291, 393, 6264, 3811, 307, 406, 257, 2167, 3069, 11, 457, 22611, 257, 732, 12, 16792, 1399, 13, 51828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757421071550488, "compression_ratio": 1.717241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130199610552397e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 69652, "start": 696.52, "end": 698.54, "text": " Two steps. Okay. Walk me through the mechanics of that.", "tokens": [50365, 4453, 4439, 13, 1033, 13, 10818, 385, 807, 264, 12939, 295, 300, 13, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851203650758978, "compression_ratio": 1.6258992805755397, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252661330136807e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 69652, "start": 698.6999999999999, "end": 700.74, "text": " Step one is the irreversible collapse.", "tokens": [50474, 5470, 472, 307, 264, 16014, 840, 964, 15584, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851203650758978, "compression_ratio": 1.6258992805755397, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252661330136807e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 69652, "start": 700.9, "end": 701.42, "text": " The collapse.", "tokens": [50584, 440, 15584, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851203650758978, "compression_ratio": 1.6258992805755397, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252661330136807e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 69652, "start": 701.6, "end": 708.5799999999999, "text": " The function surveys its domain, identifies every single distinction that lives inside its blind spot as kernel, and deliberately crushes them.", "tokens": [50619, 440, 2445, 22711, 1080, 9274, 11, 34597, 633, 2167, 16844, 300, 2909, 1854, 1080, 6865, 4008, 382, 28256, 11, 293, 23506, 10321, 279, 552, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851203650758978, "compression_ratio": 1.6258992805755397, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252661330136807e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 69652, "start": 708.72, "end": 710.12, "text": " So it forces them together.", "tokens": [50975, 407, 309, 5874, 552, 1214, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851203650758978, "compression_ratio": 1.6258992805755397, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252661330136807e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 69652, "start": 710.5799999999999, "end": 718.92, "text": " Yes. It groups all the indistinguishable elements into clusters, forming a new compressed space called a quotient.", "tokens": [51068, 1079, 13, 467, 3935, 439, 264, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 4959, 666, 23313, 11, 15745, 257, 777, 30353, 1901, 1219, 257, 9641, 1196, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851203650758978, "compression_ratio": 1.6258992805755397, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252661330136807e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 69652, "start": 719.04, "end": 721.9, "text": " So the quotient is the shoebox for my receipts.", "tokens": [51491, 407, 264, 9641, 1196, 307, 264, 12796, 4995, 337, 452, 2268, 48908, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851203650758978, "compression_ratio": 1.6258992805755397, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252661330136807e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 69652, "start": 722.02, "end": 722.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51640, 7587, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851203650758978, "compression_ratio": 1.6258992805755397, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252661330136807e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 72248, "start": 722.48, "end": 731.0600000000001, "text": " The function says, I am blind to the difference between an apple receipt and a bread receipt, so I am going to compress them both into a single object called food expense.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2445, 1619, 11, 286, 669, 6865, 281, 264, 2649, 1296, 364, 10606, 33882, 293, 257, 5961, 33882, 11, 370, 286, 669, 516, 281, 14778, 552, 1293, 666, 257, 2167, 2657, 1219, 1755, 18406, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08177334641757077, "compression_ratio": 1.5069767441860464, "no_speech_prob": 1.555207677049475e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 72248, "start": 731.4, "end": 738.82, "text": " The math actually supports your intuition perfectly there. That is the collapse. You are quotienting out the irrelevant information.", "tokens": [50811, 440, 5221, 767, 9346, 428, 24002, 6239, 456, 13, 663, 307, 264, 15584, 13, 509, 366, 9641, 1196, 278, 484, 264, 28682, 1589, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08177334641757077, "compression_ratio": 1.5069767441860464, "no_speech_prob": 1.555207677049475e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 72248, "start": 738.96, "end": 739.86, "text": " Okay. And step two.", "tokens": [51189, 1033, 13, 400, 1823, 732, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08177334641757077, "compression_ratio": 1.5069767441860464, "no_speech_prob": 1.555207677049475e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 73986, "start": 739.86, "end": 749.3000000000001, "text": " Step two. Once you have collapsed, the invisible directions, once you've formed your shoeboxes, what you are left with is a highly compressed structure.", "tokens": [50365, 5470, 732, 13, 3443, 291, 362, 24578, 11, 264, 14603, 11095, 11, 1564, 291, 600, 8693, 428, 12796, 4995, 279, 11, 437, 291, 366, 1411, 365, 307, 257, 5405, 30353, 3877, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09790854705007453, "compression_ratio": 1.6789297658862876, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897989526058142e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 73986, "start": 749.72, "end": 758.02, "text": " And the theorem guarantees that this new compressed structure can be embedded perfectly with absolute faithful preservation into the target space.", "tokens": [50858, 400, 264, 20904, 32567, 300, 341, 777, 30353, 3877, 393, 312, 16741, 6239, 365, 8236, 17808, 27257, 666, 264, 3779, 1901, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09790854705007453, "compression_ratio": 1.6789297658862876, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897989526058142e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 73986, "start": 758.14, "end": 760.2, "text": " Oh, wow. So it's a massive bait and switch.", "tokens": [51279, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 407, 309, 311, 257, 5994, 16865, 293, 3679, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09790854705007453, "compression_ratio": 1.6789297658862876, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897989526058142e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 73986, "start": 760.46, "end": 760.82, "text": " How do you mean?", "tokens": [51395, 1012, 360, 291, 914, 30, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09790854705007453, "compression_ratio": 1.6789297658862876, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897989526058142e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 73986, "start": 760.86, "end": 764.1, "text": " Step one is aggressively destroy all the information you can't see.", "tokens": [51415, 5470, 472, 307, 32024, 5293, 439, 264, 1589, 291, 393, 380, 536, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09790854705007453, "compression_ratio": 1.6789297658862876, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897989526058142e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 73986, "start": 764.24, "end": 768.02, "text": " Step two is take whatever survives that purge and preserve it flawlessly.", "tokens": [51584, 5470, 732, 307, 747, 2035, 46231, 300, 1864, 432, 293, 15665, 309, 13717, 12048, 13, 51773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09790854705007453, "compression_ratio": 1.6789297658862876, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897989526058142e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 76802, "start": 768.02, "end": 776.02, "text": " That is exactly it. Every homomorphism in algebra, every linear transformation in geometry follows this exact blueprint.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 2293, 309, 13, 2048, 3655, 32702, 1434, 294, 21989, 11, 633, 8213, 9887, 294, 18426, 10002, 341, 1900, 35868, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562551567353397, "compression_ratio": 1.5696202531645569, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 76802, "start": 776.72, "end": 779.96, "text": " Collapse the invisible, then faithfully represent the remainder.", "tokens": [50800, 4586, 11145, 264, 14603, 11, 550, 4522, 2277, 2906, 264, 29837, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562551567353397, "compression_ratio": 1.5696202531645569, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 76802, "start": 780.42, "end": 781.84, "text": " That is fascinating.", "tokens": [50985, 663, 307, 10343, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562551567353397, "compression_ratio": 1.5696202531645569, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 76802, "start": 782.0799999999999, "end": 788.3, "text": " And once you understand this, it naturally generates a cosmic accounting system for information,", "tokens": [51068, 400, 1564, 291, 1223, 341, 11, 309, 8195, 23815, 257, 27614, 19163, 1185, 337, 1589, 11, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562551567353397, "compression_ratio": 1.5696202531645569, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 76802, "start": 788.74, "end": 792.8, "text": " which in linear algebra is formalized as the Rankin-Nullity theorem.", "tokens": [51401, 597, 294, 8213, 21989, 307, 9860, 1602, 382, 264, 35921, 259, 12, 45, 858, 507, 20904, 13, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562551567353397, "compression_ratio": 1.5696202531645569, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 79280, "start": 792.8, "end": 798.8, "text": " The conservation of degrees of freedom. I read this section three times because it felt so, I don't know, so satisfying.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 16185, 295, 5310, 295, 5645, 13, 286, 1401, 341, 3541, 1045, 1413, 570, 309, 2762, 370, 11, 286, 500, 380, 458, 11, 370, 18348, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11548186185067161, "compression_ratio": 1.7985611510791366, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897485793741397e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 79280, "start": 799.04, "end": 804.8, "text": " It is deeply satisfying because it acts as a fundamental law of conservation for mathematical structure.", "tokens": [50677, 467, 307, 8760, 18348, 570, 309, 10672, 382, 257, 8088, 2101, 295, 16185, 337, 18894, 3877, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11548186185067161, "compression_ratio": 1.7985611510791366, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897485793741397e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 79280, "start": 805.1999999999999, "end": 812.16, "text": " It dictates that the total number of dimensions you start with must equal the dimensions of what survives, which we call the Rank,", "tokens": [50985, 467, 12569, 1024, 300, 264, 3217, 1230, 295, 12819, 291, 722, 365, 1633, 2681, 264, 12819, 295, 437, 46231, 11, 597, 321, 818, 264, 35921, 11, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11548186185067161, "compression_ratio": 1.7985611510791366, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897485793741397e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 79280, "start": 812.52, "end": 816.0999999999999, "text": " plus the dimensions of what disappears into the kernel, which we call the Nullity.", "tokens": [51351, 1804, 264, 12819, 295, 437, 25527, 666, 264, 28256, 11, 597, 321, 818, 264, 426, 858, 507, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11548186185067161, "compression_ratio": 1.7985611510791366, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897485793741397e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 79280, "start": 816.3199999999999, "end": 819.54, "text": " Rank plus Nullity. So nothing is magically lost to the void.", "tokens": [51541, 35921, 1804, 426, 858, 507, 13, 407, 1825, 307, 39763, 2731, 281, 264, 22009, 13, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11548186185067161, "compression_ratio": 1.7985611510791366, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897485793741397e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 81954, "start": 819.54, "end": 824.52, "text": " And nothing is magically created out of thin air. If you start with a five-dimensional space,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1825, 307, 39763, 2942, 484, 295, 5862, 1988, 13, 759, 291, 722, 365, 257, 1732, 12, 18759, 1901, 11, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14415945573286576, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.524893709567432e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 81954, "start": 824.74, "end": 828.7199999999999, "text": " every single one of those independent directions experiences exactly one of two fates.", "tokens": [50625, 633, 2167, 472, 295, 729, 6695, 11095, 5235, 2293, 472, 295, 732, 283, 1024, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14415945573286576, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.524893709567432e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 81954, "start": 828.92, "end": 829.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50834, 1779, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14415945573286576, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.524893709567432e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 81954, "start": 829.12, "end": 836.78, "text": " It either survives the process as an observable degree of freedom, or it falls into the blind spot and vanishes into the kernel.", "tokens": [50844, 467, 2139, 46231, 264, 1399, 382, 364, 9951, 712, 4314, 295, 5645, 11, 420, 309, 8804, 666, 264, 6865, 4008, 293, 3161, 16423, 666, 264, 28256, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14415945573286576, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.524893709567432e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 81954, "start": 837.14, "end": 839.54, "text": " You can account for every single drop of information.", "tokens": [51245, 509, 393, 2696, 337, 633, 2167, 3270, 295, 1589, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14415945573286576, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.524893709567432e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 81954, "start": 840.2199999999999, "end": 842.54, "text": " Which naturally pushes us toward a much bigger question.", "tokens": [51399, 3013, 8195, 21020, 505, 7361, 257, 709, 3801, 1168, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14415945573286576, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.524893709567432e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 81954, "start": 842.88, "end": 844.48, "text": " I feel like there's always a bigger question.", "tokens": [51532, 286, 841, 411, 456, 311, 1009, 257, 3801, 1168, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14415945573286576, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.524893709567432e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 84448, "start": 844.48, "end": 855.5600000000001, "text": " There is. If this two-step architecture, this rhythm of collapse, followed by faithful embedding, applies to numbers, and to geometric vectors, and to symmetries.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 307, 13, 759, 341, 732, 12, 16792, 9482, 11, 341, 11801, 295, 15584, 11, 6263, 538, 17808, 12240, 3584, 11, 13165, 281, 3547, 11, 293, 281, 33246, 18875, 11, 293, 281, 14232, 302, 2244, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0812685489654541, "compression_ratio": 1.6055045871559632, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549645989224037e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 84448, "start": 855.72, "end": 859.2, "text": " Is there a master language that governs all of them?", "tokens": [50927, 1119, 456, 257, 4505, 2856, 300, 1980, 82, 439, 295, 552, 30, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0812685489654541, "compression_ratio": 1.6055045871559632, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549645989224037e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 84448, "start": 859.22, "end": 865.9, "text": " Exactly. Is there a way to study the architecture itself without getting bogged down in whether we're talking about shapes or numbers?", "tokens": [51102, 7587, 13, 1119, 456, 257, 636, 281, 2979, 264, 9482, 2564, 1553, 1242, 26132, 3004, 760, 294, 1968, 321, 434, 1417, 466, 10854, 420, 3547, 30, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0812685489654541, "compression_ratio": 1.6055045871559632, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549645989224037e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 86590, "start": 865.9, "end": 871.8, "text": " And that question pulls us out of the realm of classical algebra and drops us straight into category theory.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 1168, 16982, 505, 484, 295, 264, 15355, 295, 13735, 21989, 293, 11438, 505, 2997, 666, 7719, 5261, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14003741066410857, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165596422243467e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 86590, "start": 871.92, "end": 872.6, "text": " Category theory.", "tokens": [50666, 383, 48701, 5261, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14003741066410857, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165596422243467e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 86590, "start": 872.76, "end": 876.98, "text": " Which, from what I gather, requires us to completely unlearn how we look at objects.", "tokens": [50708, 3013, 11, 490, 437, 286, 5448, 11, 7029, 505, 281, 2584, 25272, 1083, 577, 321, 574, 412, 6565, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14003741066410857, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165596422243467e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 86590, "start": 877.18, "end": 877.52, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50929, 467, 775, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14003741066410857, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165596422243467e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 86590, "start": 877.9, "end": 881.24, "text": " Category theory represents a radical philosophical pivot.", "tokens": [50965, 383, 48701, 5261, 8855, 257, 12001, 25066, 14538, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14003741066410857, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165596422243467e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 86590, "start": 882.22, "end": 885.6999999999999, "text": " Traditionally, if you want to define a mathematical object, you dissect it.", "tokens": [51181, 22017, 15899, 11, 498, 291, 528, 281, 6964, 257, 18894, 2657, 11, 291, 48332, 309, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14003741066410857, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165596422243467e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 86590, "start": 885.92, "end": 887.24, "text": " You look at its internal parts.", "tokens": [51366, 509, 574, 412, 1080, 6920, 3166, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14003741066410857, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165596422243467e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 86590, "start": 887.3199999999999, "end": 888.22, "text": " Like what's inside it.", "tokens": [51436, 1743, 437, 311, 1854, 309, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14003741066410857, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165596422243467e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 86590, "start": 888.62, "end": 888.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51501, 1779, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14003741066410857, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165596422243467e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 88890, "start": 888.9, "end": 892.74, "text": " What are the specific elements inside this set?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 366, 264, 2685, 4959, 1854, 341, 992, 30, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 88890, "start": 893.16, "end": 895.28, "text": " What do the vectors in this space look like?", "tokens": [50578, 708, 360, 264, 18875, 294, 341, 1901, 574, 411, 30, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 88890, "start": 895.72, "end": 900.1999999999999, "text": " But category theory argues that looking inside the object is a trap.", "tokens": [50706, 583, 7719, 5261, 38218, 300, 1237, 1854, 264, 2657, 307, 257, 11487, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 88890, "start": 900.52, "end": 900.88, "text": " A trap.", "tokens": [50946, 316, 11487, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 88890, "start": 901.12, "end": 901.38, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50976, 1079, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 88890, "start": 901.9, "end": 907.0799999999999, "text": " You cannot truly understand an object by dissecting its internal organs.", "tokens": [51015, 509, 2644, 4908, 1223, 364, 2657, 538, 48332, 278, 1080, 6920, 20659, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 88890, "start": 907.6, "end": 909.06, "text": " Let me try out an analogy here.", "tokens": [51300, 961, 385, 853, 484, 364, 21663, 510, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 88890, "start": 909.14, "end": 910.4, "text": " Tell me if I'm on track.", "tokens": [51377, 5115, 385, 498, 286, 478, 322, 2837, 13, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 88890, "start": 910.6, "end": 911.02, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [51450, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 88890, "start": 911.18, "end": 913.9399999999999, "text": " Imagine you're trying to define who I am as a human being.", "tokens": [51479, 11739, 291, 434, 1382, 281, 6964, 567, 286, 669, 382, 257, 1952, 885, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19550451242698813, "compression_ratio": 1.5648535564853556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552900984982076e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 91394, "start": 914.5600000000001, "end": 918.6800000000001, "text": " The traditional classical mathematical approach would be to put me under a microscope.", "tokens": [50396, 440, 5164, 13735, 18894, 3109, 576, 312, 281, 829, 385, 833, 257, 29753, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 91394, "start": 919.0200000000001, "end": 919.6600000000001, "text": " Dissect you.", "tokens": [50619, 4208, 9632, 291, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 91394, "start": 919.94, "end": 920.1600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50665, 1779, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 91394, "start": 920.34, "end": 921.72, "text": " You'd look at my cellular biology.", "tokens": [50685, 509, 1116, 574, 412, 452, 29267, 14956, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 91394, "start": 921.9000000000001, "end": 928.1600000000001, "text": " You'd say, this host is composed of this specific sequence of DNA, these carbon atoms, this organ structure.", "tokens": [50763, 509, 1116, 584, 11, 341, 3975, 307, 18204, 295, 341, 2685, 8310, 295, 8272, 11, 613, 5954, 16871, 11, 341, 1798, 3877, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 91394, "start": 928.2800000000001, "end": 928.7800000000001, "text": " They're analytical.", "tokens": [51082, 814, 434, 29579, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 91394, "start": 929.08, "end": 933.22, "text": " But category theory says, no, that doesn't tell us anything useful about who you are in the world.", "tokens": [51122, 583, 7719, 5261, 1619, 11, 572, 11, 300, 1177, 380, 980, 505, 1340, 4420, 466, 567, 291, 366, 294, 264, 1002, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 91394, "start": 933.62, "end": 936.8000000000001, "text": " To define you, we need to look at your network of relationships.", "tokens": [51349, 1407, 6964, 291, 11, 321, 643, 281, 574, 412, 428, 3209, 295, 6159, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 91394, "start": 937.22, "end": 938.34, "text": " Who do you love?", "tokens": [51529, 2102, 360, 291, 959, 30, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 91394, "start": 938.46, "end": 939.34, "text": " Who do you work with?", "tokens": [51591, 2102, 360, 291, 589, 365, 30, 51635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 91394, "start": 939.34, "end": 940.44, "text": " Who do you owe money to?", "tokens": [51635, 2102, 360, 291, 16655, 1460, 281, 30, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 91394, "start": 940.86, "end": 942.98, "text": " Your identity isn't what you're made of.", "tokens": [51711, 2260, 6575, 1943, 380, 437, 291, 434, 1027, 295, 13, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18633524138351967, "compression_ratio": 1.6483180428134556, "no_speech_prob": 1.455292050062118e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 94298, "start": 942.98, "end": 947.22, "text": " Your identity is entirely determined by your position in the broader network.", "tokens": [50365, 2260, 6575, 307, 7696, 9540, 538, 428, 2535, 294, 264, 13227, 3209, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 94298, "start": 947.6, "end": 948.48, "text": " Look at it from this angle.", "tokens": [50596, 2053, 412, 309, 490, 341, 5802, 13, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 94298, "start": 948.86, "end": 952.74, "text": " That analogy captures the exact mathematical mechanics of a category.", "tokens": [50659, 663, 21663, 27986, 264, 1900, 18894, 12939, 295, 257, 7719, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 94298, "start": 953.08, "end": 953.34, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50870, 1079, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 94298, "start": 953.84, "end": 957.6, "text": " In this framework, those relationships you just described are called morphisms.", "tokens": [50908, 682, 341, 8388, 11, 729, 6159, 291, 445, 7619, 366, 1219, 25778, 13539, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 94298, "start": 958.0600000000001, "end": 963.64, "text": " The mathematical objects themselves, the sets, the spaces, become almost passive.", "tokens": [51119, 440, 18894, 6565, 2969, 11, 264, 6352, 11, 264, 7673, 11, 1813, 1920, 14975, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 94298, "start": 963.74, "end": 964.3000000000001, "text": " Passive.", "tokens": [51403, 10319, 488, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 94298, "start": 964.36, "end": 965.38, "text": " Like they don't do anything.", "tokens": [51434, 1743, 436, 500, 380, 360, 1340, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 94298, "start": 965.62, "end": 968.34, "text": " They're simply the nodes where morphisms intersect.", "tokens": [51497, 814, 434, 2935, 264, 13891, 689, 25778, 13539, 27815, 13, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 94298, "start": 968.54, "end": 968.8000000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51643, 865, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874411241063532, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 1.3779647995565414e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 96880, "start": 968.8, "end": 976.62, "text": " The morphisms, the transformations, the arrows pointing between the objects are elevated to become the true fundamental actors of mathematics.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 25778, 13539, 11, 264, 34852, 11, 264, 19669, 12166, 1296, 264, 6565, 366, 23457, 281, 1813, 264, 2074, 8088, 10037, 295, 18666, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12672540376771171, "compression_ratio": 1.360759493670886, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881448074348768e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 96880, "start": 976.8599999999999, "end": 979.52, "text": " But wait, I have a major logistical problem with this.", "tokens": [50768, 583, 1699, 11, 286, 362, 257, 2563, 3565, 42686, 1154, 365, 341, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12672540376771171, "compression_ratio": 1.360759493670886, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881448074348768e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 96880, "start": 979.5999999999999, "end": 979.8, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50905, 1033, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12672540376771171, "compression_ratio": 1.360759493670886, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881448074348768e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 96880, "start": 979.9, "end": 980.3399999999999, "text": " What is it?", "tokens": [50920, 708, 307, 309, 30, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12672540376771171, "compression_ratio": 1.360759493670886, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881448074348768e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 98034, "start": 980.34, "end": 983.74, "text": " If we throw away the internal elements, how do we actually do the math?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 3507, 1314, 264, 6920, 4959, 11, 577, 360, 321, 767, 360, 264, 5221, 30, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15146432604108537, "compression_ratio": 1.4125, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615855404963684e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 98034, "start": 984.08, "end": 991.5600000000001, "text": " Earlier, we defined an injective function by saying, if I take two distinct inputs, they don't map to the same output.", "tokens": [50552, 24552, 11, 321, 7642, 364, 10711, 488, 2445, 538, 1566, 11, 498, 286, 747, 732, 10644, 15743, 11, 436, 500, 380, 4471, 281, 264, 912, 5598, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15146432604108537, "compression_ratio": 1.4125, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615855404963684e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 98034, "start": 991.9200000000001, "end": 993.02, "text": " I had to look at the inputs.", "tokens": [50944, 286, 632, 281, 574, 412, 264, 15743, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15146432604108537, "compression_ratio": 1.4125, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615855404963684e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 98034, "start": 993.1800000000001, "end": 993.3000000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51007, 1779, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15146432604108537, "compression_ratio": 1.4125, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615855404963684e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 99330, "start": 993.3, "end": 1000.56, "text": " If category theory makes it illegal to look at the individual elements, how can I possibly prove that a function preserves information?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 7719, 5261, 1669, 309, 11905, 281, 574, 412, 264, 2609, 4959, 11, 577, 393, 286, 6264, 7081, 300, 257, 2445, 1183, 9054, 1589, 30, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051093373979842, "compression_ratio": 1.6367713004484306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724441284308387e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 99330, "start": 1001.0999999999999, "end": 1005.5799999999999, "text": " This is exactly where category theory flexes its muscles and shows its brilliance.", "tokens": [50755, 639, 307, 2293, 689, 7719, 5261, 5896, 279, 1080, 9530, 293, 3110, 1080, 8695, 6276, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051093373979842, "compression_ratio": 1.6367713004484306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724441284308387e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 99330, "start": 1005.8199999999999, "end": 1011.9, "text": " It rebuilds the entire concept of injectivity from scratch using nothing but the network of relationships.", "tokens": [50991, 467, 16877, 82, 264, 2302, 3410, 295, 10711, 4253, 490, 8459, 1228, 1825, 457, 264, 3209, 295, 6159, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051093373979842, "compression_ratio": 1.6367713004484306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724441284308387e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 99330, "start": 1012.0999999999999, "end": 1012.64, "text": " Just the arrows.", "tokens": [51305, 1449, 264, 19669, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051093373979842, "compression_ratio": 1.6367713004484306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724441284308387e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 99330, "start": 1012.7199999999999, "end": 1013.3, "text": " Just the arrows.", "tokens": [51336, 1449, 264, 19669, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051093373979842, "compression_ratio": 1.6367713004484306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724441284308387e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 99330, "start": 1013.4399999999999, "end": 1013.5999999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51372, 865, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051093373979842, "compression_ratio": 1.6367713004484306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724441284308387e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 101360, "start": 1013.6, "end": 1015.9200000000001, "text": " It introduces a concept called a monomorphism.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 31472, 257, 3410, 1219, 257, 1108, 32702, 1434, 13, 50481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 101360, "start": 1016.76, "end": 1017.32, "text": " Monomorphism.", "tokens": [50523, 4713, 32702, 1434, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 101360, "start": 1017.5, "end": 1019.38, "text": " Break down the mechanics of that for me.", "tokens": [50560, 16925, 760, 264, 12939, 295, 300, 337, 385, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 101360, "start": 1019.64, "end": 1023.14, "text": " How do you prove distinguishability without looking inside?", "tokens": [50667, 1012, 360, 291, 7081, 20206, 2310, 1553, 1237, 1854, 30, 50842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 101360, "start": 1023.52, "end": 1030.76, "text": " Instead of asking if a function, let's call it f, can distinguish between two individual elements inside a set,", "tokens": [50861, 7156, 295, 3365, 498, 257, 2445, 11, 718, 311, 818, 309, 283, 11, 393, 20206, 1296, 732, 2609, 4959, 1854, 257, 992, 11, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 101360, "start": 1031.18, "end": 1035.92, "text": " we ask if it can distinguish between two entirely different processes that enter the set.", "tokens": [51244, 321, 1029, 498, 309, 393, 20206, 1296, 732, 7696, 819, 7555, 300, 3242, 264, 992, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 101360, "start": 1036.1, "end": 1036.3600000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51490, 1033, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 101360, "start": 1036.5, "end": 1037.56, "text": " I need to visualize this.", "tokens": [51510, 286, 643, 281, 23273, 341, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 101360, "start": 1037.6200000000001, "end": 1042.02, "text": " So instead of elements sitting inside a circle, I'm looking at arrows pointing into the circle.", "tokens": [51566, 407, 2602, 295, 4959, 3798, 1854, 257, 6329, 11, 286, 478, 1237, 412, 19669, 12166, 666, 264, 6329, 13, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 101360, "start": 1042.18, "end": 1042.48, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51794, 1079, 13, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.159303773709429, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037814080926196e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 104248, "start": 1042.48, "end": 1047.32, "text": " Suppose you have two completely different mathematical transformations, let's call them g and h,", "tokens": [50365, 21360, 291, 362, 732, 2584, 819, 18894, 34852, 11, 718, 311, 818, 552, 290, 293, 276, 11, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12801823944881044, "compression_ratio": 1.6992753623188406, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994294225701641e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 104248, "start": 1047.54, "end": 1049.44, "text": " and they're both pointing into your object.", "tokens": [50618, 293, 436, 434, 1293, 12166, 666, 428, 2657, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12801823944881044, "compression_ratio": 1.6992753623188406, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994294225701641e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 104248, "start": 1049.52, "end": 1049.8600000000001, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [50717, 5803, 309, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12801823944881044, "compression_ratio": 1.6992753623188406, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994294225701641e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 104248, "start": 1050.02, "end": 1051.54, "text": " G and h are pointing in.", "tokens": [50742, 460, 293, 276, 366, 12166, 294, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12801823944881044, "compression_ratio": 1.6992753623188406, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994294225701641e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 104248, "start": 1051.6200000000001, "end": 1054.88, "text": " Now, you apply your function f to the results of both.", "tokens": [50822, 823, 11, 291, 3079, 428, 2445, 283, 281, 264, 3542, 295, 1293, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12801823944881044, "compression_ratio": 1.6992753623188406, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994294225701641e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 104248, "start": 1055.56, "end": 1063.46, "text": " If applying f afterward makes the final results identical, meaning f composed with g looks exactly the same as f composed with h,", "tokens": [51019, 759, 9275, 283, 40411, 1669, 264, 2572, 3542, 14800, 11, 3620, 283, 18204, 365, 290, 1542, 2293, 264, 912, 382, 283, 18204, 365, 276, 11, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12801823944881044, "compression_ratio": 1.6992753623188406, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994294225701641e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 104248, "start": 1063.94, "end": 1068.24, "text": " does that force us to conclude that g and h were actually the same process all along?", "tokens": [51438, 775, 300, 3464, 505, 281, 16886, 300, 290, 293, 276, 645, 767, 264, 912, 1399, 439, 2051, 30, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12801823944881044, "compression_ratio": 1.6992753623188406, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994294225701641e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 104248, "start": 1068.32, "end": 1069.48, "text": " Let me think about that.", "tokens": [51657, 961, 385, 519, 466, 300, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12801823944881044, "compression_ratio": 1.6992753623188406, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994294225701641e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 106948, "start": 1069.48, "end": 1072.54, "text": " If the answer is yes, then f is a monomorphism.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 1867, 307, 2086, 11, 550, 283, 307, 257, 1108, 32702, 1434, 13, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19349917998680702, "compression_ratio": 0.9848484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106134438295672e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 106948, "start": 1072.72, "end": 1073.72, "text": " I think I see it.", "tokens": [50527, 286, 519, 286, 536, 309, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19349917998680702, "compression_ratio": 0.9848484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106134438295672e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 107372, "start": 1073.72, "end": 1081.04, "text": " It means f is so perfectly transparent that it never, ever destroys the distinctions that g and h created before it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1355, 283, 307, 370, 6239, 12737, 300, 309, 1128, 11, 1562, 36714, 264, 1483, 49798, 300, 290, 293, 276, 2942, 949, 309, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15213331154414586, "compression_ratio": 1.2083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381220823575513e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 108104, "start": 1081.04, "end": 1083.78, "text": " If g and h were different, f keeps them different.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 290, 293, 276, 645, 819, 11, 283, 5965, 552, 819, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17301464080810547, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042415214109987e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 108104, "start": 1083.78, "end": 1086.8799999999999, "text": " It preserves the information of the entire network.", "tokens": [50502, 467, 1183, 9054, 264, 1589, 295, 264, 2302, 3209, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17301464080810547, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042415214109987e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 108104, "start": 1087.28, "end": 1089.6399999999999, "text": " In formal terms, we say the function is left cancelable.", "tokens": [50677, 682, 9860, 2115, 11, 321, 584, 264, 2445, 307, 1411, 10373, 712, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17301464080810547, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042415214109987e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 108104, "start": 1090.1, "end": 1095.62, "text": " And if you apply the exact same logic in reverse, you get the categorical version of surge activity.", "tokens": [50818, 400, 498, 291, 3079, 264, 1900, 912, 9952, 294, 9943, 11, 291, 483, 264, 19250, 804, 3037, 295, 18989, 5191, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17301464080810547, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042415214109987e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 108104, "start": 1096.04, "end": 1096.82, "text": " Let me guess.", "tokens": [51115, 961, 385, 2041, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17301464080810547, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042415214109987e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 108104, "start": 1097.32, "end": 1100.1599999999999, "text": " We look at arrows pointing out of the object instead of in.", "tokens": [51179, 492, 574, 412, 19669, 12166, 484, 295, 264, 2657, 2602, 295, 294, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17301464080810547, "compression_ratio": 1.568075117370892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042415214109987e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 110016, "start": 1100.16, "end": 1102.02, "text": " You are tracking the logic perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 366, 11603, 264, 9952, 6239, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.157166444338285, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671634996661243e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 110016, "start": 1102.74, "end": 1104.38, "text": " It is called an epimorphism.", "tokens": [50494, 467, 307, 1219, 364, 2388, 332, 18191, 1434, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.157166444338285, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671634996661243e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 110016, "start": 1104.98, "end": 1105.5400000000002, "text": " Epimorphism.", "tokens": [50606, 9970, 332, 18191, 1434, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.157166444338285, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671634996661243e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 110016, "start": 1105.74, "end": 1114.5, "text": " If a function f provides such complete coverage of its target space that it can uniquely determine the behavior of any future transformation that follows it,", "tokens": [50644, 759, 257, 2445, 283, 6417, 1270, 3566, 9645, 295, 1080, 3779, 1901, 300, 309, 393, 31474, 6997, 264, 5223, 295, 604, 2027, 9887, 300, 10002, 309, 11, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.157166444338285, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671634996661243e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 110016, "start": 1114.9, "end": 1116.02, "text": " it's an epimorphism.", "tokens": [51102, 309, 311, 364, 2388, 332, 18191, 1434, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.157166444338285, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671634996661243e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 110016, "start": 1116.22, "end": 1117.26, "text": " It is right cancelable.", "tokens": [51168, 467, 307, 558, 10373, 712, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.157166444338285, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671634996661243e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 110016, "start": 1117.46, "end": 1123.3000000000002, "text": " So we have successfully replaced the microscopic study of elements and points with the macroscopic geometry of arrows.", "tokens": [51230, 407, 321, 362, 10727, 10772, 264, 47897, 2979, 295, 4959, 293, 2793, 365, 264, 7912, 38006, 299, 18426, 295, 19669, 13, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.157166444338285, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671634996661243e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 110016, "start": 1123.5, "end": 1123.94, "text": " We have.", "tokens": [51532, 492, 362, 13, 51554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.157166444338285, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671634996661243e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 112394, "start": 1123.94, "end": 1129.3400000000001, "text": " And speaking of the geometry of arrows, the source material spends pages dissecting commutative diagrams,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 4124, 295, 264, 18426, 295, 19669, 11, 264, 4009, 2527, 25620, 7183, 48332, 278, 800, 325, 1166, 36709, 11, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17254542516282767, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173724665951577e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 112394, "start": 1129.8400000000001, "end": 1136.52, "text": " which, to the untrained eye, look like someone drew a complex corporate flowchart and tried to pass it off as math.", "tokens": [50660, 597, 11, 281, 264, 1701, 31774, 3313, 11, 574, 411, 1580, 12804, 257, 3997, 10896, 3095, 339, 446, 293, 3031, 281, 1320, 309, 766, 382, 5221, 13, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17254542516282767, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173724665951577e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 112394, "start": 1136.68, "end": 1138.04, "text": " They do look like flowcharts.", "tokens": [51002, 814, 360, 574, 411, 3095, 339, 11814, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17254542516282767, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173724665951577e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 112394, "start": 1138.56, "end": 1140.66, "text": " But they are incredibly rigorous.", "tokens": [51096, 583, 436, 366, 6252, 29882, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17254542516282767, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173724665951577e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 112394, "start": 1141.3400000000001, "end": 1146.72, "text": " In advanced mathematics, you eventually stop writing out long, horizontal strings of algebraic equations.", "tokens": [51235, 682, 7339, 18666, 11, 291, 4728, 1590, 3579, 484, 938, 11, 12750, 13985, 295, 21989, 299, 11787, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17254542516282767, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173724665951577e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 112394, "start": 1146.78, "end": 1147.66, "text": " You just draw pictures.", "tokens": [51507, 509, 445, 2642, 5242, 13, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17254542516282767, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173724665951577e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 112394, "start": 1148.2, "end": 1148.6000000000001, "text": " Basically.", "tokens": [51578, 8537, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17254542516282767, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173724665951577e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 112394, "start": 1148.8600000000001, "end": 1149.78, "text": " You draw a map.", "tokens": [51611, 509, 2642, 257, 4471, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17254542516282767, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173724665951577e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 112394, "start": 1149.96, "end": 1152.8600000000001, "text": " You draw a diagram of objects connected by arrows.", "tokens": [51666, 509, 2642, 257, 10686, 295, 6565, 4582, 538, 19669, 13, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17254542516282767, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173724665951577e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 115286, "start": 1152.86, "end": 1159.1, "text": " If the mathematician declares that the diagram commutes, it is a powerful statement.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 48281, 979, 19415, 300, 264, 10686, 800, 1819, 11, 309, 307, 257, 4005, 5629, 13, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626782258351643, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204113126114475e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 115286, "start": 1159.24, "end": 1160.9599999999998, "text": " What does it mean for a diagram to commute?", "tokens": [50684, 708, 775, 309, 914, 337, 257, 10686, 281, 36750, 30, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626782258351643, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204113126114475e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 115286, "start": 1161.28, "end": 1169.6799999999998, "text": " It means that no matter which physical path of arrows you follow, from object A to object B, the final resulting transformation is identical.", "tokens": [50786, 467, 1355, 300, 572, 1871, 597, 4001, 3100, 295, 19669, 291, 1524, 11, 490, 2657, 316, 281, 2657, 363, 11, 264, 2572, 16505, 9887, 307, 14800, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626782258351643, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204113126114475e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 115286, "start": 1169.8799999999999, "end": 1171.2199999999998, "text": " So it's like navigating a city.", "tokens": [51216, 407, 309, 311, 411, 32054, 257, 2307, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626782258351643, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204113126114475e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 115286, "start": 1171.4799999999998, "end": 1171.8799999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51296, 1079, 13, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626782258351643, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204113126114475e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 115286, "start": 1172.1799999999998, "end": 1178.0, "text": " If I start at my apartment and I want to get to a specific coffee shop, I can walk three blocks north and two blocks east.", "tokens": [51331, 759, 286, 722, 412, 452, 9587, 293, 286, 528, 281, 483, 281, 257, 2685, 4982, 3945, 11, 286, 393, 1792, 1045, 8474, 6830, 293, 732, 8474, 10648, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626782258351643, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204113126114475e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 115286, "start": 1178.3799999999999, "end": 1181.5, "text": " Or I can walk two blocks east and three blocks north.", "tokens": [51641, 1610, 286, 393, 1792, 732, 8474, 10648, 293, 1045, 8474, 6830, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626782258351643, "compression_ratio": 1.7102473498233215, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204113126114475e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 118150, "start": 1181.5, "end": 1185.8, "text": " It doesn't matter which path of arrows I take, I arrive at the exact same coffee shop.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 1871, 597, 3100, 295, 19669, 286, 747, 11, 286, 8881, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 4982, 3945, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14330567565618776, "compression_ratio": 1.5778688524590163, "no_speech_prob": 1.997086740770926e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 118150, "start": 1186.0, "end": 1187.12, "text": " The diagram commutes.", "tokens": [50590, 440, 10686, 800, 1819, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14330567565618776, "compression_ratio": 1.5778688524590163, "no_speech_prob": 1.997086740770926e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 118150, "start": 1187.32, "end": 1193.1, "text": " And the geometry of that diagram completely replaces the need for the algebraic equation.", "tokens": [50656, 400, 264, 18426, 295, 300, 10686, 2584, 46734, 264, 643, 337, 264, 21989, 299, 5367, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14330567565618776, "compression_ratio": 1.5778688524590163, "no_speech_prob": 1.997086740770926e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 118150, "start": 1193.38, "end": 1193.58, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50959, 865, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14330567565618776, "compression_ratio": 1.5778688524590163, "no_speech_prob": 1.997086740770926e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 118150, "start": 1193.94, "end": 1197.52, "text": " But I sense you have a reservation about this level of abstraction.", "tokens": [50987, 583, 286, 2020, 291, 362, 257, 28922, 466, 341, 1496, 295, 37765, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14330567565618776, "compression_ratio": 1.5778688524590163, "no_speech_prob": 1.997086740770926e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 118150, "start": 1197.66, "end": 1198.06, "text": " I do.", "tokens": [51173, 286, 360, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14330567565618776, "compression_ratio": 1.5778688524590163, "no_speech_prob": 1.997086740770926e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 118150, "start": 1198.18, "end": 1199.42, "text": " I have a massive reservation.", "tokens": [51199, 286, 362, 257, 5994, 28922, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14330567565618776, "compression_ratio": 1.5778688524590163, "no_speech_prob": 1.997086740770926e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 118150, "start": 1199.74, "end": 1200.5, "text": " Lay it on me.", "tokens": [51277, 20084, 309, 322, 385, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14330567565618776, "compression_ratio": 1.5778688524590163, "no_speech_prob": 1.997086740770926e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 118150, "start": 1200.84, "end": 1203.8, "text": " Doesn't this just make math needlessly impossibly complicated?", "tokens": [51332, 12955, 380, 341, 445, 652, 5221, 643, 12048, 38802, 3545, 6179, 30, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14330567565618776, "compression_ratio": 1.5778688524590163, "no_speech_prob": 1.997086740770926e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 120380, "start": 1203.8, "end": 1205.68, "text": " I mean, we started with numbers, which makes sense.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 321, 1409, 365, 3547, 11, 597, 1669, 2020, 13, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15004305406050247, "compression_ratio": 1.555045871559633, "no_speech_prob": 1.410518511886505e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 120380, "start": 1205.78, "end": 1207.94, "text": " Then we abstracted to variables, then to functions.", "tokens": [50464, 1396, 321, 12649, 292, 281, 9102, 11, 550, 281, 6828, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15004305406050247, "compression_ratio": 1.555045871559633, "no_speech_prob": 1.410518511886505e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 120380, "start": 1208.46, "end": 1214.12, "text": " And now we are dealing with abstract networks of arrows where we don't even know what the objects are made of.", "tokens": [50598, 400, 586, 321, 366, 6260, 365, 12649, 9590, 295, 19669, 689, 321, 500, 380, 754, 458, 437, 264, 6565, 366, 1027, 295, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15004305406050247, "compression_ratio": 1.555045871559633, "no_speech_prob": 1.410518511886505e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 120380, "start": 1214.24, "end": 1216.52, "text": " And we're just tracing paths on a flow chart.", "tokens": [50887, 400, 321, 434, 445, 25262, 14518, 322, 257, 3095, 6927, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15004305406050247, "compression_ratio": 1.555045871559633, "no_speech_prob": 1.410518511886505e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 120380, "start": 1217.3, "end": 1218.84, "text": " Why would anyone do this to themselves?", "tokens": [51040, 1545, 576, 2878, 360, 341, 281, 2969, 30, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15004305406050247, "compression_ratio": 1.555045871559633, "no_speech_prob": 1.410518511886505e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 120380, "start": 1218.98, "end": 1220.74, "text": " Aren't we just hiding the actual math?", "tokens": [51124, 15464, 380, 321, 445, 10596, 264, 3539, 5221, 30, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15004305406050247, "compression_ratio": 1.555045871559633, "no_speech_prob": 1.410518511886505e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 122074, "start": 1220.74, "end": 1224.46, "text": " It absolutely feels more complicated when you first encounter it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 3122, 3417, 544, 6179, 562, 291, 700, 8593, 309, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 122074, "start": 1224.6200000000001, "end": 1224.7, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50559, 865, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 122074, "start": 1224.8, "end": 1227.0, "text": " It feels like you were losing your grip on reality.", "tokens": [50568, 467, 3417, 411, 291, 645, 7027, 428, 12007, 322, 4103, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 122074, "start": 1227.3, "end": 1227.5, "text": " Totally.", "tokens": [50693, 22837, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 122074, "start": 1227.86, "end": 1234.14, "text": " But the author addresses this exact friction with a quote that is arguably the thesis of the entire manuscript.", "tokens": [50721, 583, 264, 3793, 16862, 341, 1900, 17710, 365, 257, 6513, 300, 307, 26771, 264, 22288, 295, 264, 2302, 23928, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 122074, "start": 1235.08, "end": 1235.9, "text": " The text states,", "tokens": [51082, 440, 2487, 4368, 11, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 122074, "start": 1236.36, "end": 1238.26, "text": " Abstraction is not the removal of meaning.", "tokens": [51146, 46853, 26766, 307, 406, 264, 17933, 295, 3620, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 122074, "start": 1238.8, "end": 1241.32, "text": " It is the removal of unnecessary detail.", "tokens": [51268, 467, 307, 264, 17933, 295, 19350, 2607, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 122074, "start": 1241.52, "end": 1243.32, "text": " The removal of unnecessary detail.", "tokens": [51404, 440, 17933, 295, 19350, 2607, 13, 51494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 122074, "start": 1243.48, "end": 1244.28, "text": " That sounds nice.", "tokens": [51502, 663, 3263, 1481, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 122074, "start": 1244.32, "end": 1246.78, "text": " But how does that actually help solve a problem?", "tokens": [51544, 583, 577, 775, 300, 767, 854, 5039, 257, 1154, 30, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20963720373205236, "compression_ratio": 1.7061068702290076, "no_speech_prob": 1.861486442419902e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 124678, "start": 1246.78, "end": 1250.26, "text": " Think of abstraction purely as data compression for the human mind.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 295, 37765, 17491, 382, 1412, 19355, 337, 264, 1952, 1575, 13, 50539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 124678, "start": 1251.04, "end": 1252.6399999999999, "text": " Let's say you are a classical mathematician.", "tokens": [50578, 961, 311, 584, 291, 366, 257, 13735, 48281, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 124678, "start": 1253.56, "end": 1254.8, "text": " You study the theory of sets.", "tokens": [50704, 509, 2979, 264, 5261, 295, 6352, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 124678, "start": 1255.54, "end": 1257.06, "text": " Then you study vector spaces.", "tokens": [50803, 1396, 291, 2979, 8062, 7673, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 124678, "start": 1257.5, "end": 1258.34, "text": " Then groups.", "tokens": [50901, 1396, 3935, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 124678, "start": 1258.8999999999999, "end": 1260.1399999999999, "text": " Then topological spaces.", "tokens": [50971, 1396, 1192, 4383, 7673, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 124678, "start": 1260.26, "end": 1260.36, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51039, 1033, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 124678, "start": 1260.48, "end": 1261.36, "text": " Four different fields.", "tokens": [51050, 7451, 819, 7909, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 124678, "start": 1261.56, "end": 1262.56, "text": " In each of those fields,", "tokens": [51104, 682, 1184, 295, 729, 7909, 11, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 124678, "start": 1262.82, "end": 1266.6399999999999, "text": " you are going to discover a version of the first isomorphism theorem.", "tokens": [51167, 291, 366, 516, 281, 4411, 257, 3037, 295, 264, 700, 307, 32702, 1434, 20904, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 124678, "start": 1266.82, "end": 1267.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51367, 1779, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 124678, "start": 1267.12, "end": 1268.8799999999999, "text": " The collapse and embed thing we talked about.", "tokens": [51382, 440, 15584, 293, 12240, 551, 321, 2825, 466, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 124678, "start": 1269.32, "end": 1269.84, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51492, 7587, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 124678, "start": 1270.08, "end": 1276.32, "text": " So you have to rigorously prove and memorize that same foundational theorem 16 different times", "tokens": [51530, 407, 291, 362, 281, 42191, 5098, 7081, 293, 27478, 300, 912, 32195, 20904, 3165, 819, 1413, 51842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2127666175365448, "compression_ratio": 1.6312292358803986, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722215417248274e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 127632, "start": 1276.32, "end": 1279.3, "text": " using 16 completely different sets of vocabulary.", "tokens": [50365, 1228, 3165, 2584, 819, 6352, 295, 19864, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 127632, "start": 1279.54, "end": 1280.54, "text": " That sounds miserable.", "tokens": [50526, 663, 3263, 22321, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 127632, "start": 1280.86, "end": 1282.4399999999998, "text": " It is incredibly inefficient.", "tokens": [50592, 467, 307, 6252, 43495, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 127632, "start": 1282.82, "end": 1287.2, "text": " It's like trying to store a massive computer file that just says the letter A a million times.", "tokens": [50690, 467, 311, 411, 1382, 281, 3531, 257, 5994, 3820, 3991, 300, 445, 1619, 264, 5063, 316, 257, 2459, 1413, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 127632, "start": 1287.32, "end": 1288.54, "text": " Oh, I see where you're going with this.", "tokens": [50915, 876, 11, 286, 536, 689, 291, 434, 516, 365, 341, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 127632, "start": 1289.2, "end": 1291.36, "text": " Category theory is the compression algorithm.", "tokens": [51009, 383, 48701, 5261, 307, 264, 19355, 9284, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 127632, "start": 1292.08, "end": 1296.76, "text": " It strips away the specific vocabulary of geometry or algebra or topology.", "tokens": [51153, 467, 19842, 1314, 264, 2685, 19864, 295, 18426, 420, 21989, 420, 1192, 1793, 13, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 127632, "start": 1296.76, "end": 1299.9399999999998, "text": " It looks at the underlying network of arrows and says,", "tokens": [51387, 467, 1542, 412, 264, 14217, 3209, 295, 19669, 293, 1619, 11, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 127632, "start": 1300.46, "end": 1302.06, "text": " Just store the rule 16A.", "tokens": [51572, 1449, 3531, 264, 4978, 3165, 32, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 127632, "start": 1302.7, "end": 1303.1799999999998, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51684, 3153, 13, 51708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1811830997467041, "compression_ratio": 1.582142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.74004170047748e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 130318, "start": 1303.18, "end": 1306.8400000000001, "text": " You prove one universal categorical theorem about how arrows behave,", "tokens": [50365, 509, 7081, 472, 11455, 19250, 804, 20904, 466, 577, 19669, 15158, 11, 50548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16747426986694336, "compression_ratio": 1.6488549618320612, "no_speech_prob": 1.905460381493307e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 130318, "start": 1307.0800000000002, "end": 1312.74, "text": " and that single proof automatically applies to all 16 distinct mathematical disciplines.", "tokens": [50560, 293, 300, 2167, 8177, 6772, 13165, 281, 439, 3165, 10644, 18894, 21919, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16747426986694336, "compression_ratio": 1.6488549618320612, "no_speech_prob": 1.905460381493307e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 130318, "start": 1313.38, "end": 1315.2, "text": " It isn't making the math harder.", "tokens": [50875, 467, 1943, 380, 1455, 264, 5221, 6081, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16747426986694336, "compression_ratio": 1.6488549618320612, "no_speech_prob": 1.905460381493307e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 130318, "start": 1315.8200000000002, "end": 1320.24, "text": " It's revealing that there are actually an incredibly small number of structural themes", "tokens": [50997, 467, 311, 23983, 300, 456, 366, 767, 364, 6252, 1359, 1230, 295, 15067, 13544, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16747426986694336, "compression_ratio": 1.6488549618320612, "no_speech_prob": 1.905460381493307e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 130318, "start": 1320.24, "end": 1321.88, "text": " running the entire universe.", "tokens": [51218, 2614, 264, 2302, 6445, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16747426986694336, "compression_ratio": 1.6488549618320612, "no_speech_prob": 1.905460381493307e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 130318, "start": 1322.3200000000002, "end": 1323.88, "text": " That is a brilliant way to frame it.", "tokens": [51322, 663, 307, 257, 10248, 636, 281, 3920, 309, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16747426986694336, "compression_ratio": 1.6488549618320612, "no_speech_prob": 1.905460381493307e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 130318, "start": 1324.04, "end": 1328.66, "text": " Category theory strips away the specific language to expose the raw universal structure.", "tokens": [51408, 383, 48701, 5261, 19842, 1314, 264, 2685, 2856, 281, 19219, 264, 8936, 11455, 3877, 13, 51639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16747426986694336, "compression_ratio": 1.6488549618320612, "no_speech_prob": 1.905460381493307e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 132866, "start": 1328.66, "end": 1333.3200000000002, "text": " But what if the structure is fine, and it's the language itself that's the problem?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 437, 498, 264, 3877, 307, 2489, 11, 293, 309, 311, 264, 2856, 2564, 300, 311, 264, 1154, 30, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18740247643512228, "compression_ratio": 1.644927536231884, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965884414524515e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 132866, "start": 1333.38, "end": 1333.72, "text": " What do you mean?", "tokens": [50601, 708, 360, 291, 914, 30, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18740247643512228, "compression_ratio": 1.644927536231884, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965884414524515e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 132866, "start": 1333.88, "end": 1338.18, "text": " Like, what if I'm stuck trying to solve a problem in mathematical English,", "tokens": [50626, 1743, 11, 437, 498, 286, 478, 5541, 1382, 281, 5039, 257, 1154, 294, 18894, 3669, 11, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18740247643512228, "compression_ratio": 1.644927536231884, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965884414524515e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 132866, "start": 1338.5800000000002, "end": 1342.5800000000002, "text": " but the problem desperately wants to be solved in mathematical Spanish?", "tokens": [50861, 457, 264, 1154, 23726, 2738, 281, 312, 13041, 294, 18894, 8058, 30, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18740247643512228, "compression_ratio": 1.644927536231884, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965884414524515e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 132866, "start": 1343.2, "end": 1343.52, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51092, 876, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18740247643512228, "compression_ratio": 1.644927536231884, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965884414524515e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 132866, "start": 1343.76, "end": 1347.3000000000002, "text": " That brings us to the third action of math translation without loss.", "tokens": [51120, 663, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 2636, 3069, 295, 5221, 12853, 1553, 4470, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18740247643512228, "compression_ratio": 1.644927536231884, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965884414524515e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 132866, "start": 1347.5600000000002, "end": 1350.72, "text": " This is where we leave the folders and the shoeboxes behind,", "tokens": [51310, 639, 307, 689, 321, 1856, 264, 31082, 293, 264, 12796, 4995, 279, 2261, 11, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18740247643512228, "compression_ratio": 1.644927536231884, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965884414524515e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 132866, "start": 1350.72, "end": 1354.6200000000001, "text": " and we look at how we represent the distinctions we've decided to keep.", "tokens": [51468, 293, 321, 574, 412, 577, 321, 2906, 264, 1483, 49798, 321, 600, 3047, 281, 1066, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18740247643512228, "compression_ratio": 1.644927536231884, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965884414524515e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 135462, "start": 1354.62, "end": 1360.02, "text": " The text begins this exploration by examining something I thought was completely basic coordinates.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 7338, 341, 16197, 538, 34662, 746, 286, 1194, 390, 2584, 3875, 21056, 13, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 135462, "start": 1360.3, "end": 1362.52, "text": " I always assumed that coordinates were the geometry.", "tokens": [50649, 286, 1009, 15895, 300, 21056, 645, 264, 18426, 13, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 135462, "start": 1362.8999999999999, "end": 1363.56, "text": " A lot of people do.", "tokens": [50779, 316, 688, 295, 561, 360, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 135462, "start": 1363.9399999999998, "end": 1366.9199999999998, "text": " Like, if I put a point on a graph at 3,4,", "tokens": [50831, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 829, 257, 935, 322, 257, 4295, 412, 805, 11, 19, 11, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 135462, "start": 1367.06, "end": 1369.8999999999999, "text": " those numbers are the fundamental truth of where that point is.", "tokens": [50987, 729, 3547, 366, 264, 8088, 3494, 295, 689, 300, 935, 307, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 135462, "start": 1370.26, "end": 1373.56, "text": " But the text argues that coordinates are just an arbitrary dictionary.", "tokens": [51147, 583, 264, 2487, 38218, 300, 21056, 366, 445, 364, 23211, 25890, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 135462, "start": 1373.8999999999999, "end": 1375.5, "text": " It's a crucial conceptual leap.", "tokens": [51329, 467, 311, 257, 11462, 24106, 19438, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 135462, "start": 1376.06, "end": 1378.6599999999999, "text": " A geometric point exists in physical space,", "tokens": [51437, 316, 33246, 935, 8198, 294, 4001, 1901, 11, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 135462, "start": 1378.78, "end": 1382.26, "text": " regardless of how you, the observer, choose to describe it.", "tokens": [51573, 10060, 295, 577, 291, 11, 264, 27878, 11, 2826, 281, 6786, 309, 13, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 135462, "start": 1382.3799999999999, "end": 1382.6599999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51753, 1779, 13, 51767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16243378189969654, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.3398207239848081e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 138266, "start": 1382.66, "end": 1386.28, "text": " You can describe its location using standard Cartesian coordinates", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 6786, 1080, 4914, 1228, 3832, 22478, 42434, 21056, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14062881469726562, "compression_ratio": 1.745583038869258, "no_speech_prob": 1.325053239874252e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 138266, "start": 1386.28, "end": 1389.98, "text": " moving along a rigid x and y axis to get to 3,4.", "tokens": [50546, 2684, 2051, 257, 22195, 2031, 293, 288, 10298, 281, 483, 281, 805, 11, 19, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14062881469726562, "compression_ratio": 1.745583038869258, "no_speech_prob": 1.325053239874252e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 138266, "start": 1390.64, "end": 1393.98, "text": " Or you could describe that exact same point using polar coordinates,", "tokens": [50764, 1610, 291, 727, 6786, 300, 1900, 912, 935, 1228, 12367, 21056, 11, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14062881469726562, "compression_ratio": 1.745583038869258, "no_speech_prob": 1.325053239874252e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 138266, "start": 1394.24, "end": 1397.3600000000001, "text": " where you define an angle from the center and a distance outward.", "tokens": [50944, 689, 291, 6964, 364, 5802, 490, 264, 3056, 293, 257, 4560, 26914, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14062881469726562, "compression_ratio": 1.745583038869258, "no_speech_prob": 1.325053239874252e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 138266, "start": 1397.6000000000001, "end": 1398.8000000000002, "text": " But the point hasn't moved.", "tokens": [51112, 583, 264, 935, 6132, 380, 4259, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14062881469726562, "compression_ratio": 1.745583038869258, "no_speech_prob": 1.325053239874252e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 138266, "start": 1399.0800000000002, "end": 1401.3600000000001, "text": " The physical point hasn't moved a single millimeter.", "tokens": [51186, 440, 4001, 935, 6132, 380, 4259, 257, 2167, 17942, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14062881469726562, "compression_ratio": 1.745583038869258, "no_speech_prob": 1.325053239874252e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 138266, "start": 1402.0600000000002, "end": 1405.98, "text": " You have simply chosen a different dictionary to communicate its location.", "tokens": [51335, 509, 362, 2935, 8614, 257, 819, 25890, 281, 7890, 1080, 4914, 13, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14062881469726562, "compression_ratio": 1.745583038869258, "no_speech_prob": 1.325053239874252e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 138266, "start": 1406.3200000000002, "end": 1408.18, "text": " And because the point hasn't moved,", "tokens": [51548, 400, 570, 264, 935, 6132, 380, 4259, 11, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14062881469726562, "compression_ratio": 1.745583038869258, "no_speech_prob": 1.325053239874252e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 138266, "start": 1408.6200000000001, "end": 1411.8200000000002, "text": " changing the coordinates is a flawless translation.", "tokens": [51663, 4473, 264, 21056, 307, 257, 45693, 12853, 13, 51823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14062881469726562, "compression_ratio": 1.745583038869258, "no_speech_prob": 1.325053239874252e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 141182, "start": 1411.82, "end": 1413.62, "text": " You haven't collapsed any distinctions.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 2378, 380, 24578, 604, 1483, 49798, 13, 50455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 141182, "start": 1414.04, "end": 1416.6, "text": " You haven't lost a single drop of information.", "tokens": [50476, 509, 2378, 380, 2731, 257, 2167, 3270, 295, 1589, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 141182, "start": 1417.08, "end": 1417.76, "text": " None at all.", "tokens": [50628, 14492, 412, 439, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 141182, "start": 1418.08, "end": 1421.8, "text": " And when you scale this concept up in linear algebra,", "tokens": [50678, 400, 562, 291, 4373, 341, 3410, 493, 294, 8213, 21989, 11, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 141182, "start": 1422.1799999999998, "end": 1423.8, "text": " it becomes the theory of basis.", "tokens": [50883, 309, 3643, 264, 5261, 295, 5143, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 141182, "start": 1424.6, "end": 1429.26, "text": " A basis is simply the foundational language you choose to construct your vector space.", "tokens": [51004, 316, 5143, 307, 2935, 264, 32195, 2856, 291, 2826, 281, 7690, 428, 8062, 1901, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 141182, "start": 1429.72, "end": 1429.98, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51260, 1033, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 141182, "start": 1430.08, "end": 1431.72, "text": " So if you change the basis.", "tokens": [51278, 407, 498, 291, 1319, 264, 5143, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 141182, "start": 1431.8, "end": 1432.76, "text": " If you change the basis,", "tokens": [51364, 759, 291, 1319, 264, 5143, 11, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 141182, "start": 1433.28, "end": 1436.34, "text": " the geometric vectors themselves do not warp or bend.", "tokens": [51438, 264, 33246, 18875, 2969, 360, 406, 36030, 420, 11229, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24919747371299594, "compression_ratio": 1.6244725738396624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 143634, "start": 1436.34, "end": 1441.6, "text": " But every single numerical coordinate you use to describe them completely changes.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 633, 2167, 29054, 15670, 291, 764, 281, 6786, 552, 2584, 2962, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15800883318926837, "compression_ratio": 1.5954545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269260686233798e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 143634, "start": 1441.9599999999998, "end": 1444.6599999999999, "text": " Which fundamentally alters how we have to think about matrices.", "tokens": [50646, 3013, 17879, 419, 1559, 577, 321, 362, 281, 519, 466, 32284, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15800883318926837, "compression_ratio": 1.5954545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269260686233798e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 143634, "start": 1445.1599999999999, "end": 1448.36, "text": " Because a matrix is just a grid of numbers representing a transformation.", "tokens": [50806, 1436, 257, 8141, 307, 445, 257, 10748, 295, 3547, 13460, 257, 9887, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15800883318926837, "compression_ratio": 1.5954545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269260686233798e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 143634, "start": 1448.8999999999999, "end": 1452.08, "text": " But those numbers are completely dependent on the language we are using, right?", "tokens": [50993, 583, 729, 3547, 366, 2584, 12334, 322, 264, 2856, 321, 366, 1228, 11, 558, 30, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15800883318926837, "compression_ratio": 1.5954545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269260686233798e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 143634, "start": 1452.1799999999998, "end": 1454.9199999999998, "text": " That is the core insight of representation theory.", "tokens": [51157, 663, 307, 264, 4965, 11269, 295, 10290, 5261, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15800883318926837, "compression_ratio": 1.5954545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269260686233798e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 145492, "start": 1454.92, "end": 1458.8400000000001, "text": " It implies that you can have two completely different grids of numbers.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 18779, 300, 291, 393, 362, 732, 2584, 819, 677, 3742, 295, 3547, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2141375235461314, "compression_ratio": 1.7184115523465704, "no_speech_prob": 1.196914746134925e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 145492, "start": 1459.14, "end": 1465.14, "text": " Two matrices that look absolutely nothing alike that are actually representing the exact same physical transformation.", "tokens": [50576, 4453, 32284, 300, 574, 3122, 1825, 20025, 300, 366, 767, 13460, 264, 1900, 912, 4001, 9887, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2141375235461314, "compression_ratio": 1.7184115523465704, "no_speech_prob": 1.196914746134925e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 145492, "start": 1465.48, "end": 1466.48, "text": " They're just speaking different languages.", "tokens": [50893, 814, 434, 445, 4124, 819, 8650, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2141375235461314, "compression_ratio": 1.7184115523465704, "no_speech_prob": 1.196914746134925e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 145492, "start": 1466.9, "end": 1468.3200000000002, "text": " They're just speaking in different bases.", "tokens": [50964, 814, 434, 445, 4124, 294, 819, 17949, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2141375235461314, "compression_ratio": 1.7184115523465704, "no_speech_prob": 1.196914746134925e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 145492, "start": 1468.6200000000001, "end": 1469.9, "text": " We call them similar matrices.", "tokens": [51050, 492, 818, 552, 2531, 32284, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2141375235461314, "compression_ratio": 1.7184115523465704, "no_speech_prob": 1.196914746134925e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 145492, "start": 1470.2, "end": 1470.4, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51129, 1033, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2141375235461314, "compression_ratio": 1.7184115523465704, "no_speech_prob": 1.196914746134925e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 145492, "start": 1470.46, "end": 1475.76, "text": " But if I can choose literally any language, any basis to describe my transformation,", "tokens": [51142, 583, 498, 286, 393, 2826, 3736, 604, 2856, 11, 604, 5143, 281, 6786, 452, 9887, 11, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2141375235461314, "compression_ratio": 1.7184115523465704, "no_speech_prob": 1.196914746134925e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 145492, "start": 1476.14, "end": 1478.18, "text": " how do I know which one to pick?", "tokens": [51426, 577, 360, 286, 458, 597, 472, 281, 1888, 30, 51528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2141375235461314, "compression_ratio": 1.7184115523465704, "no_speech_prob": 1.196914746134925e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 145492, "start": 1478.26, "end": 1481.18, "text": " Is there a best language for a given problem?", "tokens": [51532, 1119, 456, 257, 1151, 2856, 337, 257, 2212, 1154, 30, 51678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2141375235461314, "compression_ratio": 1.7184115523465704, "no_speech_prob": 1.196914746134925e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 148118, "start": 1481.18, "end": 1481.7, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17354700516681282, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 148118, "start": 1482.38, "end": 1488.48, "text": " And the mathematical process of finding that perfect optimal language is called diagonalization.", "tokens": [50425, 400, 264, 18894, 1399, 295, 5006, 300, 2176, 16252, 2856, 307, 1219, 21539, 2144, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17354700516681282, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 148118, "start": 1489.02, "end": 1491.18, "text": " We need to spend some time on diagonalization.", "tokens": [50757, 492, 643, 281, 3496, 512, 565, 322, 21539, 2144, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17354700516681282, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 148118, "start": 1491.64, "end": 1495.8400000000001, "text": " The text describes it as finding the natural language of a linear operator.", "tokens": [50888, 440, 2487, 15626, 309, 382, 5006, 264, 3303, 2856, 295, 257, 8213, 12973, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17354700516681282, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 148118, "start": 1496.0, "end": 1496.9, "text": " The natural language, right.", "tokens": [51106, 440, 3303, 2856, 11, 558, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17354700516681282, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 148118, "start": 1496.92, "end": 1502.64, "text": " If I look at a standard matrix, it's usually a messy, dense grid of numbers.", "tokens": [51152, 759, 286, 574, 412, 257, 3832, 8141, 11, 309, 311, 2673, 257, 16191, 11, 18011, 10748, 295, 3547, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17354700516681282, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 148118, "start": 1502.92, "end": 1507.64, "text": " It implies that every single coordinate is tangled up and interacting with every other coordinate.", "tokens": [51452, 467, 18779, 300, 633, 2167, 15670, 307, 47192, 493, 293, 18017, 365, 633, 661, 15670, 13, 51688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17354700516681282, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 150764, "start": 1507.64, "end": 1511.22, "text": " Diagonalization somehow untangles that knot.", "tokens": [50365, 8789, 6709, 304, 2144, 6063, 1701, 656, 904, 300, 16966, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21311631569495568, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8899320042981005e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 150764, "start": 1511.5800000000002, "end": 1512.96, "text": " How does it physically do that?", "tokens": [50562, 1012, 775, 309, 9762, 360, 300, 30, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21311631569495568, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8899320042981005e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 150764, "start": 1513.1000000000001, "end": 1518.14, "text": " It untangles the system by searching for very specific hidden directions called eigenvectors.", "tokens": [50638, 467, 1701, 656, 904, 264, 1185, 538, 10808, 337, 588, 2685, 7633, 11095, 1219, 10446, 303, 5547, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21311631569495568, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8899320042981005e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 150764, "start": 1518.6000000000001, "end": 1519.2, "text": " Eigendector.", "tokens": [50913, 40561, 5445, 1672, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21311631569495568, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8899320042981005e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 150764, "start": 1519.3400000000001, "end": 1523.7800000000002, "text": " To understand this, imagine a transformation that stretches and rotates a geometric space.", "tokens": [50950, 1407, 1223, 341, 11, 3811, 257, 9887, 300, 29058, 293, 42133, 257, 33246, 1901, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21311631569495568, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8899320042981005e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 150764, "start": 1524.64, "end": 1528.18, "text": " Most vectors in that space are going to get knocked off their original path.", "tokens": [51215, 4534, 18875, 294, 300, 1901, 366, 516, 281, 483, 16914, 766, 641, 3380, 3100, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21311631569495568, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8899320042981005e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 150764, "start": 1528.72, "end": 1529.7, "text": " They will change direction.", "tokens": [51419, 814, 486, 1319, 3513, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21311631569495568, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8899320042981005e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 150764, "start": 1529.76, "end": 1531.26, "text": " Because the whole space is spinning.", "tokens": [51471, 1436, 264, 1379, 1901, 307, 15640, 13, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21311631569495568, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8899320042981005e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 150764, "start": 1531.38, "end": 1531.5400000000002, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51552, 865, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21311631569495568, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8899320042981005e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 153154, "start": 1531.54, "end": 1532.06, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 153154, "start": 1532.7, "end": 1535.3799999999999, "text": " But the eigenvectors are immune to the rotation.", "tokens": [50423, 583, 264, 10446, 303, 5547, 366, 11992, 281, 264, 12447, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 153154, "start": 1535.74, "end": 1537.72, "text": " They stay on their exact original line.", "tokens": [50575, 814, 1754, 322, 641, 1900, 3380, 1622, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 153154, "start": 1537.86, "end": 1539.56, "text": " They only stretch or shrink.", "tokens": [50681, 814, 787, 5985, 420, 23060, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 153154, "start": 1540.02, "end": 1542.1599999999999, "text": " The amount they stretch is called their eigenvalue.", "tokens": [50789, 440, 2372, 436, 5985, 307, 1219, 641, 10446, 29155, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 153154, "start": 1542.36, "end": 1547.7, "text": " So they are the pure independent modes of the transformation, the parts that don't get mixed up.", "tokens": [50906, 407, 436, 366, 264, 6075, 6695, 14068, 295, 264, 9887, 11, 264, 3166, 300, 500, 380, 483, 7467, 493, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 153154, "start": 1547.78, "end": 1548.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51177, 7587, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 153154, "start": 1548.3, "end": 1548.48, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51203, 865, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 153154, "start": 1548.6, "end": 1550.68, "text": " If you can change your language, change your basis,", "tokens": [51218, 759, 291, 393, 1319, 428, 2856, 11, 1319, 428, 5143, 11, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 153154, "start": 1550.8999999999999, "end": 1554.86, "text": " so that your entire coordinate system is built exclusively out of these eigenvectors,", "tokens": [51333, 370, 300, 428, 2302, 15670, 1185, 307, 3094, 20638, 484, 295, 613, 10446, 303, 5547, 11, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 153154, "start": 1555.1399999999999, "end": 1557.74, "text": " something magical happens to your messy matrix.", "tokens": [51545, 746, 12066, 2314, 281, 428, 16191, 8141, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 153154, "start": 1557.92, "end": 1558.44, "text": " What happens?", "tokens": [51684, 708, 2314, 30, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 153154, "start": 1558.76, "end": 1560.32, "text": " All the chaotic interactions vanish.", "tokens": [51726, 1057, 264, 27013, 13280, 43584, 13, 51804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18918114855773466, "compression_ratio": 1.7110389610389611, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354650260955397e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 156032, "start": 1560.32, "end": 1565.02, "text": " The matrix collapses into a beautifully simple diagonal line of numbers.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 8141, 48765, 666, 257, 16525, 2199, 21539, 1622, 295, 3547, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552972884405227, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105503191816034e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 156032, "start": 1565.48, "end": 1572.1, "text": " The complex, tangled system is revealed to be just a collection of independent, isolated, stretching actions.", "tokens": [50623, 440, 3997, 11, 47192, 1185, 307, 9599, 281, 312, 445, 257, 5765, 295, 6695, 11, 14621, 11, 19632, 5909, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552972884405227, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105503191816034e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 156032, "start": 1572.32, "end": 1575.48, "text": " I have an analogy for this that might help listeners visualize it.", "tokens": [50965, 286, 362, 364, 21663, 337, 341, 300, 1062, 854, 23274, 23273, 309, 13, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552972884405227, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105503191816034e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 156032, "start": 1575.56, "end": 1575.74, "text": " All right.", "tokens": [51127, 1057, 558, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552972884405227, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105503191816034e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 156032, "start": 1576.3999999999999, "end": 1580.78, "text": " Imagine you are at a concert, listening to a massive symphony orchestra.", "tokens": [51169, 11739, 291, 366, 412, 257, 8543, 11, 4764, 281, 257, 5994, 6697, 28616, 25280, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552972884405227, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105503191816034e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 156032, "start": 1581.0, "end": 1581.26, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51399, 1033, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552972884405227, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105503191816034e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 156032, "start": 1581.46, "end": 1585.9399999999998, "text": " If you were to record that symphony and look at the raw sound wave on a computer, it's a nightmare.", "tokens": [51422, 759, 291, 645, 281, 2136, 300, 6697, 28616, 293, 574, 412, 264, 8936, 1626, 5772, 322, 257, 3820, 11, 309, 311, 257, 18724, 13, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552972884405227, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 2.2105503191816034e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 158594, "start": 1585.94, "end": 1594.04, "text": " It's a single, tangled, chaotic mess of noise where the violins, the cellos, the brass, and the percussion are all blended into one line.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 2167, 11, 47192, 11, 27013, 2082, 295, 5658, 689, 264, 3448, 1292, 11, 264, 2815, 329, 11, 264, 26257, 11, 293, 264, 44430, 366, 439, 27048, 666, 472, 1622, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654646185379994, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.920405891600585e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 158594, "start": 1594.56, "end": 1596.8400000000001, "text": " That raw sound wave is your messy matrix.", "tokens": [50796, 663, 8936, 1626, 5772, 307, 428, 16191, 8141, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654646185379994, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.920405891600585e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 158594, "start": 1596.96, "end": 1597.96, "text": " The tangled representation.", "tokens": [50916, 440, 47192, 10290, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654646185379994, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.920405891600585e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 158594, "start": 1598.5, "end": 1598.8200000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50993, 1779, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654646185379994, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.920405891600585e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 158594, "start": 1599.3600000000001, "end": 1604.14, "text": " Diagonalization is like a mathematical process that suddenly hands you the conductor's sheet music.", "tokens": [51036, 8789, 6709, 304, 2144, 307, 411, 257, 18894, 1399, 300, 5800, 2377, 291, 264, 29957, 311, 8193, 1318, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654646185379994, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.920405891600585e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 160414, "start": 1604.14, "end": 1609.2, "text": " It allows you to perfectly isolate the violin frequency from the trumpet frequency.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 4045, 291, 281, 6239, 25660, 264, 22878, 7893, 490, 264, 35160, 7893, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16809558868408203, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928301188745003e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 160414, "start": 1609.3400000000001, "end": 1609.8400000000001, "text": " Oh, that's good.", "tokens": [50625, 876, 11, 300, 311, 665, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16809558868408203, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928301188745003e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 160414, "start": 1610.1000000000001, "end": 1611.7800000000002, "text": " The physical music hasn't changed.", "tokens": [50663, 440, 4001, 1318, 6132, 380, 3105, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16809558868408203, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928301188745003e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 160414, "start": 1612.0800000000002, "end": 1614.0400000000002, "text": " The symphony is exactly the same.", "tokens": [50762, 440, 6697, 28616, 307, 2293, 264, 912, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16809558868408203, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928301188745003e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 160414, "start": 1614.38, "end": 1620.42, "text": " But your representation of it has shifted, making all the independent fundamental parts crystal clear.", "tokens": [50877, 583, 428, 10290, 295, 309, 575, 18892, 11, 1455, 439, 264, 6695, 8088, 3166, 13662, 1850, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16809558868408203, "compression_ratio": 1.4545454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928301188745003e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 162042, "start": 1620.42, "end": 1624.46, "text": " That is a phenomenal analogy for spectral decomposition.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 257, 17778, 21663, 337, 42761, 48356, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11152788969847532, "compression_ratio": 1.6496598639455782, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105169940034634e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 162042, "start": 1624.98, "end": 1630.14, "text": " You are isolating the fundamental, uncoupled frequencies of a system.", "tokens": [50593, 509, 366, 48912, 264, 8088, 11, 6219, 263, 15551, 20250, 295, 257, 1185, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11152788969847532, "compression_ratio": 1.6496598639455782, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105169940034634e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 162042, "start": 1630.26, "end": 1631.94, "text": " It just makes it so much easier to understand.", "tokens": [50857, 467, 445, 1669, 309, 370, 709, 3571, 281, 1223, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11152788969847532, "compression_ratio": 1.6496598639455782, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105169940034634e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 162042, "start": 1632.3600000000001, "end": 1637.76, "text": " And the beauty of mathematics is that this doesn't just work for finite, discrete grids of numbers.", "tokens": [50962, 400, 264, 6643, 295, 18666, 307, 300, 341, 1177, 380, 445, 589, 337, 19362, 11, 27706, 677, 3742, 295, 3547, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11152788969847532, "compression_ratio": 1.6496598639455782, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105169940034634e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 162042, "start": 1637.96, "end": 1647.46, "text": " If we take your orchestra analogy and push it to infinity, if we apply this logic to continuous functions, we arrive at one of the most powerful tools ever invented.", "tokens": [51242, 759, 321, 747, 428, 25280, 21663, 293, 2944, 309, 281, 13202, 11, 498, 321, 3079, 341, 9952, 281, 10957, 6828, 11, 321, 8881, 412, 472, 295, 264, 881, 4005, 3873, 1562, 14479, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11152788969847532, "compression_ratio": 1.6496598639455782, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105169940034634e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 162042, "start": 1647.64, "end": 1648.74, "text": " The Fourier transform.", "tokens": [51726, 440, 36810, 4088, 13, 51781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11152788969847532, "compression_ratio": 1.6496598639455782, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105169940034634e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 162042, "start": 1649.04, "end": 1649.94, "text": " The Fourier transform.", "tokens": [51796, 440, 36810, 4088, 13, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11152788969847532, "compression_ratio": 1.6496598639455782, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105169940034634e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 164994, "start": 1649.94, "end": 1651.6000000000001, "text": " The ultimate act of translation.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 9705, 605, 295, 12853, 13, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09976530504656268, "compression_ratio": 1.7517241379310344, "no_speech_prob": 2.060269272893822e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 164994, "start": 1651.8, "end": 1655.94, "text": " When I first encountered this, it felt less like math and more like sorcery.", "tokens": [50458, 1133, 286, 700, 20381, 341, 11, 309, 2762, 1570, 411, 5221, 293, 544, 411, 41349, 88, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09976530504656268, "compression_ratio": 1.7517241379310344, "no_speech_prob": 2.060269272893822e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 164994, "start": 1656.06, "end": 1658.3400000000001, "text": " It is the mathematical engine of the modern world.", "tokens": [50671, 467, 307, 264, 18894, 2848, 295, 264, 4363, 1002, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09976530504656268, "compression_ratio": 1.7517241379310344, "no_speech_prob": 2.060269272893822e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 164994, "start": 1658.7, "end": 1669.78, "text": " The Fourier transform takes a function that is spread out over time, what we call the time domain, where events happen sequentially in a tangled mess, and it translates it completely into the frequency domain.", "tokens": [50803, 440, 36810, 4088, 2516, 257, 2445, 300, 307, 3974, 484, 670, 565, 11, 437, 321, 818, 264, 565, 9274, 11, 689, 3931, 1051, 5123, 3137, 294, 257, 47192, 2082, 11, 293, 309, 28468, 309, 2584, 666, 264, 7893, 9274, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09976530504656268, "compression_ratio": 1.7517241379310344, "no_speech_prob": 2.060269272893822e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 164994, "start": 1669.9, "end": 1671.52, "text": " So it shifts the perspective.", "tokens": [51363, 407, 309, 19201, 264, 4585, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09976530504656268, "compression_ratio": 1.7517241379310344, "no_speech_prob": 2.060269272893822e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 164994, "start": 1671.52, "end": 1679.6200000000001, "text": " It shifts the question from when do these events happen to what fundamental frequencies make up this event.", "tokens": [51444, 467, 19201, 264, 1168, 490, 562, 360, 613, 3931, 1051, 281, 437, 8088, 20250, 652, 493, 341, 2280, 13, 51849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09976530504656268, "compression_ratio": 1.7517241379310344, "no_speech_prob": 2.060269272893822e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 167994, "start": 1679.94, "end": 1681.94, "text": " So it does exactly what my symphony analogy did.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 775, 2293, 437, 452, 6697, 28616, 21663, 630, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16062868965996635, "compression_ratio": 1.2869565217391303, "no_speech_prob": 1.2744190468552685e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 167994, "start": 1681.94, "end": 1688.94, "text": " It takes the raw audio wave over time and outputs the exact sheet music of constituent frequencies.", "tokens": [50465, 467, 2516, 264, 8936, 6278, 5772, 670, 565, 293, 23930, 264, 1900, 8193, 1318, 295, 16085, 317, 20250, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16062868965996635, "compression_ratio": 1.2869565217391303, "no_speech_prob": 1.2744190468552685e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 168894, "start": 1688.94, "end": 1694.52, "text": " It does, but the true sorcery of the Fourier transform isn't just that it identifies frequencies.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 775, 11, 457, 264, 2074, 41349, 88, 295, 264, 36810, 4088, 1943, 380, 445, 300, 309, 34597, 20250, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2353383700052897, "compression_ratio": 1.1149425287356323, "no_speech_prob": 2.0927209617993547e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 169452, "start": 1694.52, "end": 1700.3, "text": " The real power is what happens to the underlying calculus when you shift into this new language.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 957, 1347, 307, 437, 2314, 281, 264, 14217, 33400, 562, 291, 5513, 666, 341, 777, 2856, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18500328063964844, "compression_ratio": 1.1566265060240963, "no_speech_prob": 2.0927313701402106e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 170030, "start": 1700.3, "end": 1701.3, "text": " Explain the mechanism there.", "tokens": [50365, 39574, 264, 7513, 456, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2673740594283394, "compression_ratio": 1.146341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682314167223988e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 170030, "start": 1701.3, "end": 1704.3, "text": " Why does changing the language change the difficulty of the math?", "tokens": [50415, 1545, 775, 4473, 264, 2856, 1319, 264, 10360, 295, 264, 5221, 30, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2673740594283394, "compression_ratio": 1.146341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682314167223988e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 170430, "start": 1704.3, "end": 1708.3, "text": " Think about a differential equation in the time domain.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 257, 15756, 5367, 294, 264, 565, 9274, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3112125056130545, "compression_ratio": 0.9322033898305084, "no_speech_prob": 2.3246393959092115e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 170830, "start": 1708.3, "end": 1713.3, "text": " Calculating how a complex system changes over time requires differentiation, calculus.", "tokens": [50365, 3511, 2444, 990, 577, 257, 3997, 1185, 2962, 670, 565, 7029, 38902, 11, 33400, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11022113351260915, "compression_ratio": 1.583710407239819, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417453113469095e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 170830, "start": 1713.3, "end": 1715.3, "text": " Which can be really hard.", "tokens": [50615, 3013, 393, 312, 534, 1152, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11022113351260915, "compression_ratio": 1.583710407239819, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417453113469095e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 170830, "start": 1715.3, "end": 1719.3, "text": " And for complicated systems, computing derivatives is notoriously brutal.", "tokens": [50715, 400, 337, 6179, 3652, 11, 15866, 33733, 307, 46772, 8994, 17878, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11022113351260915, "compression_ratio": 1.583710407239819, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417453113469095e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 170830, "start": 1719.3, "end": 1723.3, "text": " But let's look at the basic building block of a frequency, a sine wave.", "tokens": [50915, 583, 718, 311, 574, 412, 264, 3875, 2390, 3461, 295, 257, 7893, 11, 257, 18609, 5772, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11022113351260915, "compression_ratio": 1.583710407239819, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417453113469095e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 170830, "start": 1723.3, "end": 1725.3, "text": " What is the derivative of a sine wave?", "tokens": [51115, 708, 307, 264, 13760, 295, 257, 18609, 5772, 30, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11022113351260915, "compression_ratio": 1.583710407239819, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417453113469095e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 170830, "start": 1725.3, "end": 1728.3, "text": " It's a cosine wave, but multiplied by the frequency.", "tokens": [51215, 467, 311, 257, 23565, 5772, 11, 457, 17207, 538, 264, 7893, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11022113351260915, "compression_ratio": 1.583710407239819, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417453113469095e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 172830, "start": 1728.3, "end": 1731.3, "text": " The math actually supports your intuition perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5221, 767, 9346, 428, 24002, 6239, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0774150547915942, "compression_ratio": 1.712962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970298643241178e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 172830, "start": 1731.3, "end": 1737.3, "text": " Taking the derivative of a basic wave essentially just pulls the frequency value out to the front.", "tokens": [50515, 17837, 264, 13760, 295, 257, 3875, 5772, 4476, 445, 16982, 264, 7893, 2158, 484, 281, 264, 1868, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0774150547915942, "compression_ratio": 1.712962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970298643241178e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 172830, "start": 1737.3, "end": 1742.3, "text": " So if you translate your entire complicated equation into the frequency domain using Fourier,", "tokens": [50815, 407, 498, 291, 13799, 428, 2302, 6179, 5367, 666, 264, 7893, 9274, 1228, 36810, 11, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0774150547915942, "compression_ratio": 1.712962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970298643241178e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 172830, "start": 1742.3, "end": 1747.3, "text": " taking a derivative doing calculus literally turns into simple multiplication.", "tokens": [51065, 1940, 257, 13760, 884, 33400, 3736, 4523, 666, 2199, 27290, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0774150547915942, "compression_ratio": 1.712962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970298643241178e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 172830, "start": 1747.3, "end": 1750.3, "text": " You just multiply your data by the frequency.", "tokens": [51315, 509, 445, 12972, 428, 1412, 538, 264, 7893, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0774150547915942, "compression_ratio": 1.712962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970298643241178e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 175030, "start": 1750.3, "end": 1755.3, "text": " Are you saying that by translating the problem, we completely bypass calculus?", "tokens": [50365, 2014, 291, 1566, 300, 538, 35030, 264, 1154, 11, 321, 2584, 24996, 33400, 30, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.049159810349747944, "compression_ratio": 1.7331081081081081, "no_speech_prob": 1.5134362946894742e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 175030, "start": 1755.3, "end": 1757.3, "text": " That is exactly what I'm saying.", "tokens": [50615, 663, 307, 2293, 437, 286, 478, 1566, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.049159810349747944, "compression_ratio": 1.7331081081081081, "no_speech_prob": 1.5134362946894742e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 175030, "start": 1757.3, "end": 1762.3, "text": " Incredibly difficult calculus suddenly becomes elementary school algebra.", "tokens": [50715, 27792, 3545, 2252, 33400, 5800, 3643, 16429, 1395, 21989, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.049159810349747944, "compression_ratio": 1.7331081081081081, "no_speech_prob": 1.5134362946894742e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 175030, "start": 1762.3, "end": 1767.3, "text": " You solve the complex differential equation using basic arithmetic in the frequency domain,", "tokens": [50965, 509, 5039, 264, 3997, 15756, 5367, 1228, 3875, 42973, 294, 264, 7893, 9274, 11, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.049159810349747944, "compression_ratio": 1.7331081081081081, "no_speech_prob": 1.5134362946894742e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 175030, "start": 1767.3, "end": 1770.3, "text": " and when you have the answer, you just translate it back to the time domain.", "tokens": [51215, 293, 562, 291, 362, 264, 1867, 11, 291, 445, 13799, 309, 646, 281, 264, 565, 9274, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.049159810349747944, "compression_ratio": 1.7331081081081081, "no_speech_prob": 1.5134362946894742e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 175030, "start": 1770.3, "end": 1771.3, "text": " That is staggering.", "tokens": [51365, 663, 307, 42974, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.049159810349747944, "compression_ratio": 1.7331081081081081, "no_speech_prob": 1.5134362946894742e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 175030, "start": 1771.3, "end": 1773.3, "text": " The fundamental problem hasn't changed.", "tokens": [51415, 440, 8088, 1154, 6132, 380, 3105, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.049159810349747944, "compression_ratio": 1.7331081081081081, "no_speech_prob": 1.5134362946894742e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 175030, "start": 1773.3, "end": 1777.3, "text": " But simply by shifting to the natural language of frequencies,", "tokens": [51515, 583, 2935, 538, 17573, 281, 264, 3303, 2856, 295, 20250, 11, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.049159810349747944, "compression_ratio": 1.7331081081081081, "no_speech_prob": 1.5134362946894742e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 175030, "start": 1777.3, "end": 1779.3, "text": " the math essentially solves itself.", "tokens": [51715, 264, 5221, 4476, 39890, 2564, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.049159810349747944, "compression_ratio": 1.7331081081081081, "no_speech_prob": 1.5134362946894742e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 177930, "start": 1779.3, "end": 1783.3, "text": " It's the ultimate proof that representation matters just as much as computation.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 264, 9705, 8177, 300, 10290, 7001, 445, 382, 709, 382, 24903, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047127758691070276, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554623782234155e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 177930, "start": 1783.3, "end": 1787.3, "text": " And this realization leads mathematicians to a critical pursuit.", "tokens": [50565, 400, 341, 25138, 6689, 32811, 2567, 281, 257, 4924, 23365, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047127758691070276, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554623782234155e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 177930, "start": 1787.3, "end": 1790.3, "text": " If we can manipulate representations this drastically,", "tokens": [50765, 759, 321, 393, 20459, 33358, 341, 29673, 11, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047127758691070276, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554623782234155e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 177930, "start": 1790.3, "end": 1794.3, "text": " if we can jump from coordinates to diagonal matrices to frequency domains,", "tokens": [50915, 498, 321, 393, 3012, 490, 21056, 281, 21539, 32284, 281, 7893, 25514, 11, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047127758691070276, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554623782234155e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 177930, "start": 1794.3, "end": 1796.3, "text": " what actually stays the same?", "tokens": [51115, 437, 767, 10834, 264, 912, 30, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047127758691070276, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554623782234155e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 177930, "start": 1796.3, "end": 1797.3, "text": " The anchor points.", "tokens": [51215, 440, 18487, 2793, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047127758691070276, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554623782234155e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 177930, "start": 1797.3, "end": 1799.3, "text": " The text calls them invariants.", "tokens": [51265, 440, 2487, 5498, 552, 33270, 1719, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047127758691070276, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554623782234155e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 177930, "start": 1799.3, "end": 1802.3, "text": " Invariants are the holy grail of classification.", "tokens": [51365, 31124, 3504, 1719, 366, 264, 10622, 1295, 388, 295, 21538, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047127758691070276, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554623782234155e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 177930, "start": 1802.3, "end": 1808.3, "text": " As representations shift and warp, certain core properties stubbornly refuse to change.", "tokens": [51515, 1018, 33358, 5513, 293, 36030, 11, 1629, 4965, 7221, 24137, 356, 16791, 281, 1319, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047127758691070276, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554623782234155e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 180830, "start": 1808.3, "end": 1809.3, "text": " Like what?", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 437, 30, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04303566349877252, "compression_ratio": 1.6335078534031413, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254790040694857e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 180830, "start": 1809.3, "end": 1811.3, "text": " The dimension of a space is invariant.", "tokens": [50415, 440, 10139, 295, 257, 1901, 307, 33270, 394, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04303566349877252, "compression_ratio": 1.6335078534031413, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254790040694857e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 180830, "start": 1811.3, "end": 1816.3, "text": " The sum of the diagonal elements in a matrix, called the trace, is invariant.", "tokens": [50515, 440, 2408, 295, 264, 21539, 4959, 294, 257, 8141, 11, 1219, 264, 13508, 11, 307, 33270, 394, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04303566349877252, "compression_ratio": 1.6335078534031413, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254790040694857e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 180830, "start": 1816.3, "end": 1819.3, "text": " The eigenvalues we discussed are invariant.", "tokens": [50765, 440, 10446, 46033, 321, 7152, 366, 33270, 394, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04303566349877252, "compression_ratio": 1.6335078534031413, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254790040694857e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 180830, "start": 1819.3, "end": 1824.3, "text": " In the field of topology, the number of physical holes in a shape is an invariant.", "tokens": [50915, 682, 264, 2519, 295, 1192, 1793, 11, 264, 1230, 295, 4001, 8118, 294, 257, 3909, 307, 364, 33270, 394, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04303566349877252, "compression_ratio": 1.6335078534031413, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254790040694857e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 180830, "start": 1824.3, "end": 1826.3, "text": " So they don't care about the language at all?", "tokens": [51165, 407, 436, 500, 380, 1127, 466, 264, 2856, 412, 439, 30, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04303566349877252, "compression_ratio": 1.6335078534031413, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254790040694857e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 180830, "start": 1826.3, "end": 1827.3, "text": " Not at all.", "tokens": [51265, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04303566349877252, "compression_ratio": 1.6335078534031413, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254790040694857e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 182730, "start": 1827.3, "end": 1831.3, "text": " These properties belong to the absolute truth of the mathematical object itself,", "tokens": [50365, 1981, 7221, 5784, 281, 264, 8236, 3494, 295, 264, 18894, 2657, 2564, 11, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07934965061236031, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 182730, "start": 1831.3, "end": 1834.3, "text": " completely independent of the language we use to describe it.", "tokens": [50565, 2584, 6695, 295, 264, 2856, 321, 764, 281, 6786, 309, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07934965061236031, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 182730, "start": 1834.3, "end": 1838.3, "text": " Finding invariants is how mathematicians figure out what is real.", "tokens": [50715, 31947, 33270, 1719, 307, 577, 32811, 2567, 2573, 484, 437, 307, 957, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07934965061236031, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 182730, "start": 1838.3, "end": 1840.3, "text": " Okay, let's take a breath and shift gears.", "tokens": [50915, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 747, 257, 6045, 293, 5513, 20915, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07934965061236031, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 182730, "start": 1840.3, "end": 1845.3, "text": " Up until now, everything we've talked about, the functions, the categories, the translations,", "tokens": [51015, 5858, 1826, 586, 11, 1203, 321, 600, 2825, 466, 11, 264, 6828, 11, 264, 10479, 11, 264, 37578, 11, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07934965061236031, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.868323204479161e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 184530, "start": 1845.3, "end": 1848.3, "text": " it all feels very static, like a single snapshot.", "tokens": [50365, 309, 439, 3417, 588, 13437, 11, 411, 257, 2167, 30163, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05009555438208201, "compression_ratio": 1.4682080924855492, "no_speech_prob": 2.445061948047611e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 184530, "start": 1848.3, "end": 1849.3, "text": " Very frozen in time.", "tokens": [50515, 4372, 12496, 294, 565, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05009555438208201, "compression_ratio": 1.4682080924855492, "no_speech_prob": 2.445061948047611e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 184530, "start": 1849.3, "end": 1853.3, "text": " But what happens when we unleash these transformations over time?", "tokens": [50565, 583, 437, 2314, 562, 321, 49814, 613, 34852, 670, 565, 30, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05009555438208201, "compression_ratio": 1.4682080924855492, "no_speech_prob": 2.445061948047611e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 184530, "start": 1853.3, "end": 1857.3, "text": " What happens when a function doesn't just act once, but acts on its own outputs,", "tokens": [50765, 708, 2314, 562, 257, 2445, 1177, 380, 445, 605, 1564, 11, 457, 10672, 322, 1080, 1065, 23930, 11, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05009555438208201, "compression_ratio": 1.4682080924855492, "no_speech_prob": 2.445061948047611e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 184530, "start": 1857.3, "end": 1859.3, "text": " creating a continuous feedback loop?", "tokens": [50965, 4084, 257, 10957, 5824, 6367, 30, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05009555438208201, "compression_ratio": 1.4682080924855492, "no_speech_prob": 2.445061948047611e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 185930, "start": 1859.3, "end": 1866.3, "text": " We are moving from the algebra of static objects to the dynamics of process.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 2684, 490, 264, 21989, 295, 13437, 6565, 281, 264, 15679, 295, 1399, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05335780882066296, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.905456478365486e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 185930, "start": 1866.3, "end": 1871.3, "text": " When we take a function and feed its output back into itself as a new input", "tokens": [50715, 1133, 321, 747, 257, 2445, 293, 3154, 1080, 5598, 646, 666, 2564, 382, 257, 777, 4846, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05335780882066296, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.905456478365486e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 185930, "start": 1871.3, "end": 1875.3, "text": " calculating f of f of f of x over and over, we are iterating.", "tokens": [50965, 28258, 283, 295, 283, 295, 283, 295, 2031, 670, 293, 670, 11, 321, 366, 17138, 990, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05335780882066296, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.905456478365486e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 185930, "start": 1875.3, "end": 1876.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51165, 1779, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05335780882066296, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.905456478365486e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 185930, "start": 1876.3, "end": 1881.3, "text": " We are taking a static rule and turning it into a dynamic system that unfolds through time.", "tokens": [51215, 492, 366, 1940, 257, 13437, 4978, 293, 6246, 309, 666, 257, 8546, 1185, 300, 17980, 82, 807, 565, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05335780882066296, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.905456478365486e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 185930, "start": 1881.3, "end": 1882.3, "text": " Iteration.", "tokens": [51465, 286, 391, 399, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05335780882066296, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.905456478365486e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 185930, "start": 1882.3, "end": 1885.3, "text": " Okay, so I start with a point, I apply the rule, I get a new point,", "tokens": [51515, 1033, 11, 370, 286, 722, 365, 257, 935, 11, 286, 3079, 264, 4978, 11, 286, 483, 257, 777, 935, 11, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05335780882066296, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.905456478365486e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 185930, "start": 1885.3, "end": 1888.3, "text": " then I immediately apply the exact same rule to that new point.", "tokens": [51665, 550, 286, 4258, 3079, 264, 1900, 912, 4978, 281, 300, 777, 935, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05335780882066296, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.905456478365486e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 188830, "start": 1888.3, "end": 1891.3, "text": " And the central question of dynamical systems theory is,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 5777, 1168, 295, 5999, 804, 3652, 5261, 307, 11, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 188830, "start": 1891.3, "end": 1896.3, "text": " what is the ultimate fate of this process after a massive number of iterations?", "tokens": [50515, 437, 307, 264, 9705, 12738, 295, 341, 1399, 934, 257, 5994, 1230, 295, 36540, 30, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 188830, "start": 1896.3, "end": 1899.3, "text": " Does the point wander aimlessly forever?", "tokens": [50765, 4402, 264, 935, 27541, 5939, 12048, 5680, 30, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 188830, "start": 1899.3, "end": 1901.3, "text": " Does it explode out to infinity?", "tokens": [50915, 4402, 309, 21411, 484, 281, 13202, 30, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 188830, "start": 1901.3, "end": 1903.3, "text": " Or does it settle down into a stable equilibrium?", "tokens": [51015, 1610, 775, 309, 11852, 760, 666, 257, 8351, 15625, 30, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 188830, "start": 1903.3, "end": 1907.3, "text": " And this inquiry leads us directly to the concept of contraction mappings", "tokens": [51115, 400, 341, 25736, 6689, 505, 3838, 281, 264, 3410, 295, 37372, 463, 28968, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 188830, "start": 1907.3, "end": 1909.3, "text": " and the Banach fixed point theorem.", "tokens": [51315, 293, 264, 13850, 608, 6806, 935, 20904, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 188830, "start": 1909.3, "end": 1910.3, "text": " It does indeed.", "tokens": [51415, 467, 775, 6451, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 188830, "start": 1910.3, "end": 1911.3, "text": " That Banach fixed point theorem.", "tokens": [51465, 663, 13850, 608, 6806, 935, 20904, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 188830, "start": 1911.3, "end": 1915.3, "text": " I have a deeply counterintuitive visualization for this that I want to run by you.", "tokens": [51515, 286, 362, 257, 8760, 5682, 686, 48314, 25801, 337, 341, 300, 286, 528, 281, 1190, 538, 291, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 188830, "start": 1915.3, "end": 1916.3, "text": " Please do.", "tokens": [51715, 2555, 360, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05005379021167755, "compression_ratio": 1.7043189368770764, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302487366848026e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 191630, "start": 1916.3, "end": 1921.3, "text": " Imagine you take a completely accurate, flat paper map of your city.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 291, 747, 257, 2584, 8559, 11, 4962, 3035, 4471, 295, 428, 2307, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08711811591838968, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7624321056383674e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 191630, "start": 1921.3, "end": 1922.3, "text": " Okay, a map.", "tokens": [50615, 1033, 11, 257, 4471, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08711811591838968, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7624321056383674e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 191630, "start": 1922.3, "end": 1925.3, "text": " You crumple that map up into a tight, chaotic little ball,", "tokens": [50665, 509, 941, 449, 781, 300, 4471, 493, 666, 257, 4524, 11, 27013, 707, 2594, 11, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08711811591838968, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7624321056383674e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 191630, "start": 1925.3, "end": 1928.3, "text": " and you drop it on the sidewalk somewhere inside the city limits.", "tokens": [50815, 293, 291, 3270, 309, 322, 264, 25360, 4079, 1854, 264, 2307, 10406, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08711811591838968, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7624321056383674e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 191630, "start": 1928.3, "end": 1931.3, "text": " According to the math of the Banach fixed point theorem,", "tokens": [50965, 7328, 281, 264, 5221, 295, 264, 13850, 608, 6806, 935, 20904, 11, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08711811591838968, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7624321056383674e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 191630, "start": 1931.3, "end": 1935.3, "text": " there is exactly one microscopic poo on that crumpled piece of paper", "tokens": [51115, 456, 307, 2293, 472, 47897, 36743, 322, 300, 941, 449, 15551, 2522, 295, 3035, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08711811591838968, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7624321056383674e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 193530, "start": 1935.3, "end": 1941.3, "text": " that is currently hovering perfectly over the exact physical location on the ground that it represents.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 307, 4362, 44923, 6239, 670, 264, 1900, 4001, 4914, 322, 264, 2727, 300, 309, 8855, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07847932468761097, "compression_ratio": 1.4226190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965966813889624e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 193530, "start": 1941.3, "end": 1945.3, "text": " That is a classic, beautiful topological illustration.", "tokens": [50665, 663, 307, 257, 7230, 11, 2238, 1192, 4383, 22645, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07847932468761097, "compression_ratio": 1.4226190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965966813889624e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 193530, "start": 1945.3, "end": 1947.3, "text": " It's so weird to think about.", "tokens": [50865, 467, 311, 370, 3657, 281, 519, 466, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07847932468761097, "compression_ratio": 1.4226190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965966813889624e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 193530, "start": 1947.3, "end": 1950.3, "text": " And the mechanics of why it works are fascinating.", "tokens": [50965, 400, 264, 12939, 295, 983, 309, 1985, 366, 10343, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07847932468761097, "compression_ratio": 1.4226190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965966813889624e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 195030, "start": 1950.3, "end": 1953.3, "text": " Because the map is a contracted, smaller version of the city,", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 264, 4471, 307, 257, 37629, 11, 4356, 3037, 295, 264, 2307, 11, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07013567073925121, "compression_ratio": 1.6161616161616161, "no_speech_prob": 1.904768660507261e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 195030, "start": 1953.3, "end": 1956.3, "text": " and because you dropped it entirely within the city limits,", "tokens": [50515, 293, 570, 291, 8119, 309, 7696, 1951, 264, 2307, 10406, 11, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07013567073925121, "compression_ratio": 1.6161616161616161, "no_speech_prob": 1.904768660507261e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 195030, "start": 1956.3, "end": 1961.3, "text": " the continuous transformation from the real city to the map city", "tokens": [50665, 264, 10957, 9887, 490, 264, 957, 2307, 281, 264, 4471, 2307, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07013567073925121, "compression_ratio": 1.6161616161616161, "no_speech_prob": 1.904768660507261e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 195030, "start": 1961.3, "end": 1965.3, "text": " mathematically guarantees that one point gets mapped strictly to itself.", "tokens": [50915, 44003, 32567, 300, 472, 935, 2170, 33318, 20792, 281, 2564, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07013567073925121, "compression_ratio": 1.6161616161616161, "no_speech_prob": 1.904768660507261e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 195030, "start": 1965.3, "end": 1966.3, "text": " It cannot escape.", "tokens": [51115, 467, 2644, 7615, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07013567073925121, "compression_ratio": 1.6161616161616161, "no_speech_prob": 1.904768660507261e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 195030, "start": 1966.3, "end": 1968.3, "text": " It bends the mind to try and visualize it.", "tokens": [51165, 467, 42990, 264, 1575, 281, 853, 293, 23273, 309, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07013567073925121, "compression_ratio": 1.6161616161616161, "no_speech_prob": 1.904768660507261e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 196830, "start": 1968.3, "end": 1972.3, "text": " It does, but it is also the backbone of modern computation.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 775, 11, 457, 309, 307, 611, 264, 34889, 295, 4363, 24903, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08789461050460588, "compression_ratio": 1.476923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661616105221542e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 196830, "start": 1972.3, "end": 1977.3, "text": " If a mathematical transformation always brings points even slightly closer together,", "tokens": [50565, 759, 257, 18894, 9887, 1009, 5607, 2793, 754, 4748, 4966, 1214, 11, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08789461050460588, "compression_ratio": 1.476923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661616105221542e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 196830, "start": 1977.3, "end": 1978.3, "text": " if it contracts the space,", "tokens": [50815, 498, 309, 13952, 264, 1901, 11, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08789461050460588, "compression_ratio": 1.476923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661616105221542e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 196830, "start": 1978.3, "end": 1984.3, "text": " then iterating that function infinitely will always lock onto one unique, immovable fixed point.", "tokens": [50865, 550, 17138, 990, 300, 2445, 36227, 486, 1009, 4017, 3911, 472, 3845, 11, 566, 3280, 17915, 6806, 935, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08789461050460588, "compression_ratio": 1.476923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661616105221542e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 196830, "start": 1984.3, "end": 1985.3, "text": " So it's inevitable.", "tokens": [51165, 407, 309, 311, 21451, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08789461050460588, "compression_ratio": 1.476923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661616105221542e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 198530, "start": 1985.3, "end": 1986.3, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 198530, "start": 1986.3, "end": 1991.3, "text": " This is how algorithms like Google's page rank or gradiate descent in machine learning actually function.", "tokens": [50415, 639, 307, 577, 14642, 411, 3329, 311, 3028, 6181, 420, 2771, 13024, 23475, 294, 3479, 2539, 767, 2445, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 198530, "start": 1991.3, "end": 1993.3, "text": " We don't solve the equation.", "tokens": [50665, 492, 500, 380, 5039, 264, 5367, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 198530, "start": 1993.3, "end": 1994.3, "text": " We just let the system settle.", "tokens": [50765, 492, 445, 718, 264, 1185, 11852, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 198530, "start": 1994.3, "end": 1997.3, "text": " We don't even try to guess the exact numerical answer.", "tokens": [50815, 492, 500, 380, 754, 853, 281, 2041, 264, 1900, 29054, 1867, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 198530, "start": 1997.3, "end": 1999.3, "text": " We set up a contraction mapping,", "tokens": [50965, 492, 992, 493, 257, 37372, 18350, 11, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 198530, "start": 1999.3, "end": 2001.3, "text": " we feed the messy data into it,", "tokens": [51065, 321, 3154, 264, 16191, 1412, 666, 309, 11, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 198530, "start": 2001.3, "end": 2003.3, "text": " and we let the iterative feedback loop run.", "tokens": [51165, 293, 321, 718, 264, 17138, 1166, 5824, 6367, 1190, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 198530, "start": 2003.3, "end": 2008.3, "text": " The mathematical process automatically seeks out and locks onto the equilibrium for us.", "tokens": [51265, 440, 18894, 1399, 6772, 28840, 484, 293, 20703, 3911, 264, 15625, 337, 505, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 198530, "start": 2008.3, "end": 2011.3, "text": " But, there is a dark side to this, right?", "tokens": [51515, 583, 11, 456, 307, 257, 2877, 1252, 281, 341, 11, 558, 30, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 198530, "start": 2011.3, "end": 2012.3, "text": " A dark side.", "tokens": [51665, 316, 2877, 1252, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07672622468736437, "compression_ratio": 1.6391752577319587, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173002607283715e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 201230, "start": 2012.3, "end": 2015.3, "text": " Not all feedback loops shrink distances.", "tokens": [50365, 1726, 439, 5824, 16121, 23060, 22182, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 201230, "start": 2015.3, "end": 2019.3, "text": " What happens if the rule you are iterating pushes things apart instead of pulling them together?", "tokens": [50515, 708, 2314, 498, 264, 4978, 291, 366, 17138, 990, 21020, 721, 4936, 2602, 295, 8407, 552, 1214, 30, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 201230, "start": 2019.3, "end": 2020.3, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [50715, 2438, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 201230, "start": 2020.3, "end": 2024.3, "text": " If the feedback loop expands the space, you have positive feedback.", "tokens": [50765, 759, 264, 5824, 6367, 33706, 264, 1901, 11, 291, 362, 3353, 5824, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 201230, "start": 2024.3, "end": 2028.3, "text": " And this is the precise mathematical birthplace of chaos.", "tokens": [50965, 400, 341, 307, 264, 13600, 18894, 3965, 6742, 295, 14158, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 201230, "start": 2028.3, "end": 2029.3, "text": " Chaos.", "tokens": [51165, 32644, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 201230, "start": 2029.3, "end": 2033.3, "text": " When most people hear that word, they think of pure, unadulterated randomness.", "tokens": [51215, 1133, 881, 561, 1568, 300, 1349, 11, 436, 519, 295, 6075, 11, 517, 345, 425, 391, 770, 4974, 1287, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 201230, "start": 2033.3, "end": 2035.3, "text": " Just noise without a pattern.", "tokens": [51415, 1449, 5658, 1553, 257, 5102, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 201230, "start": 2035.3, "end": 2039.3, "text": " And the text is incredibly careful to dismantle that misconception.", "tokens": [51515, 400, 264, 2487, 307, 6252, 5026, 281, 30506, 306, 300, 41350, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 201230, "start": 2039.3, "end": 2041.3, "text": " Chaos is explicitly not randomness.", "tokens": [51715, 32644, 307, 20803, 406, 4974, 1287, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055010855197906494, "compression_ratio": 1.6621160409556315, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614802202981726e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 204130, "start": 2041.3, "end": 2042.3, "text": " It's not.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 406, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07710616676895707, "compression_ratio": 1.6007067137809188, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283249906050127e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 204130, "start": 2042.3, "end": 2043.3, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50415, 883, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07710616676895707, "compression_ratio": 1.6007067137809188, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283249906050127e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 204130, "start": 2043.3, "end": 2047.3, "text": " A chaotic system is perfectly 100% deterministic.", "tokens": [50465, 316, 27013, 1185, 307, 6239, 2319, 4, 15957, 3142, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07710616676895707, "compression_ratio": 1.6007067137809188, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283249906050127e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 204130, "start": 2047.3, "end": 2049.3, "text": " There are no dice being rolled.", "tokens": [50665, 821, 366, 572, 10313, 885, 14306, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07710616676895707, "compression_ratio": 1.6007067137809188, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283249906050127e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 204130, "start": 2049.3, "end": 2053.3, "text": " The terrifying unpredictability of chaos does not come from randomness.", "tokens": [50765, 440, 18106, 28341, 2310, 295, 14158, 775, 406, 808, 490, 4974, 1287, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07710616676895707, "compression_ratio": 1.6007067137809188, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283249906050127e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 204130, "start": 2053.3, "end": 2056.3, "text": " It comes entirely from the geometry of the process,", "tokens": [50965, 467, 1487, 7696, 490, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 1399, 11, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07710616676895707, "compression_ratio": 1.6007067137809188, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283249906050127e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 204130, "start": 2056.3, "end": 2061.3, "text": " constantly stretching and amplifying tiny, imperceptible errors until they dominate the entire system.", "tokens": [51115, 6460, 19632, 293, 9731, 5489, 5870, 11, 10100, 1336, 964, 13603, 1826, 436, 28246, 264, 2302, 1185, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07710616676895707, "compression_ratio": 1.6007067137809188, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283249906050127e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 204130, "start": 2061.3, "end": 2067.3, "text": " The text uses this mathematical toy called the doubling map to demonstrate this.", "tokens": [51365, 440, 2487, 4960, 341, 18894, 12058, 1219, 264, 33651, 4471, 281, 11698, 341, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07710616676895707, "compression_ratio": 1.6007067137809188, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283249906050127e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 204130, "start": 2067.3, "end": 2069.3, "text": " Can we walk through the mechanics of that slowly?", "tokens": [51665, 1664, 321, 1792, 807, 264, 12939, 295, 300, 5692, 30, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07710616676895707, "compression_ratio": 1.6007067137809188, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283249906050127e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 206930, "start": 2069.3, "end": 2070.3, "text": " Gladly.", "tokens": [50365, 28301, 356, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0826451200427431, "compression_ratio": 1.3902439024390243, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 206930, "start": 2070.3, "end": 2073.3, "text": " The fundamental rule for the doubling map is simple.", "tokens": [50415, 440, 8088, 4978, 337, 264, 33651, 4471, 307, 2199, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0826451200427431, "compression_ratio": 1.3902439024390243, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 206930, "start": 2073.3, "end": 2075.3, "text": " You take any number between 0 and 1.", "tokens": [50565, 509, 747, 604, 1230, 1296, 1958, 293, 502, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0826451200427431, "compression_ratio": 1.3902439024390243, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 206930, "start": 2075.3, "end": 2076.3, "text": " You multiply it by 2.", "tokens": [50665, 509, 12972, 309, 538, 568, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0826451200427431, "compression_ratio": 1.3902439024390243, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 206930, "start": 2076.3, "end": 2077.3, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50715, 1033, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0826451200427431, "compression_ratio": 1.3902439024390243, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 206930, "start": 2077.3, "end": 2082.3, "text": " If the result happens to be greater than 1, you simply chop off the integer part and keep the decimal.", "tokens": [50765, 759, 264, 1874, 2314, 281, 312, 5044, 813, 502, 11, 291, 2935, 7931, 766, 264, 24922, 644, 293, 1066, 264, 26601, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0826451200427431, "compression_ratio": 1.3902439024390243, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 208230, "start": 2082.3, "end": 2086.3, "text": " So if you start with 0.6, you multiply by 2 to get 1.2.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 291, 722, 365, 1958, 13, 21, 11, 291, 12972, 538, 568, 281, 483, 502, 13, 17, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10272676294500177, "compression_ratio": 1.49009900990099, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776293474043744e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 208230, "start": 2086.3, "end": 2089.3, "text": " You chop off the 1 and your new state is 0.2.", "tokens": [50565, 509, 7931, 766, 264, 502, 293, 428, 777, 1785, 307, 1958, 13, 17, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10272676294500177, "compression_ratio": 1.49009900990099, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776293474043744e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 208230, "start": 2089.3, "end": 2090.3, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50715, 1033, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10272676294500177, "compression_ratio": 1.49009900990099, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776293474043744e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 208230, "start": 2090.3, "end": 2091.3, "text": " That seems totally harmless.", "tokens": [50765, 663, 2544, 3879, 40160, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10272676294500177, "compression_ratio": 1.49009900990099, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776293474043744e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 208230, "start": 2091.3, "end": 2093.3, "text": " We're just multiplying and trimming.", "tokens": [50815, 492, 434, 445, 30955, 293, 47212, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10272676294500177, "compression_ratio": 1.49009900990099, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776293474043744e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 208230, "start": 2093.3, "end": 2095.3, "text": " It seems harmless in standard base 10 math.", "tokens": [50915, 467, 2544, 40160, 294, 3832, 3096, 1266, 5221, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10272676294500177, "compression_ratio": 1.49009900990099, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776293474043744e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 208230, "start": 2095.3, "end": 2098.3, "text": " But let's look at the exact same process in binary decimals.", "tokens": [51015, 583, 718, 311, 574, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 1399, 294, 17434, 979, 332, 1124, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10272676294500177, "compression_ratio": 1.49009900990099, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776293474043744e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 208230, "start": 2098.3, "end": 2099.3, "text": " Binary decimals.", "tokens": [51165, 363, 4066, 979, 332, 1124, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10272676294500177, "compression_ratio": 1.49009900990099, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776293474043744e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 208230, "start": 2099.3, "end": 2100.3, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51215, 1033, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10272676294500177, "compression_ratio": 1.49009900990099, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776293474043744e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 210030, "start": 2100.3, "end": 2105.3, "text": " A binary decimal is just a string of zeros and ones after a decimal point, like 0.1010.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 17434, 26601, 307, 445, 257, 6798, 295, 35193, 293, 2306, 934, 257, 26601, 935, 11, 411, 1958, 13, 3279, 3279, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820040702819825, "compression_ratio": 1.4573170731707317, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077902677090084e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 210030, "start": 2105.3, "end": 2111.3, "text": " In the binary system, multiplying a number by 2 has a very specific geometric effect.", "tokens": [50615, 682, 264, 17434, 1185, 11, 30955, 257, 1230, 538, 568, 575, 257, 588, 2685, 33246, 1802, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820040702819825, "compression_ratio": 1.4573170731707317, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077902677090084e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 210030, "start": 2111.3, "end": 2115.3, "text": " It simply shifts the decimal point exactly one spot to the right.", "tokens": [50915, 467, 2935, 19201, 264, 26601, 935, 2293, 472, 4008, 281, 264, 558, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820040702819825, "compression_ratio": 1.4573170731707317, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077902677090084e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 211530, "start": 2115.3, "end": 2116.3, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 211530, "start": 2116.3, "end": 2117.3, "text": " Let me visualize that.", "tokens": [50415, 961, 385, 23273, 300, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 211530, "start": 2117.3, "end": 2121.3, "text": " So 0.1011 times 2 becomes 1.0110.", "tokens": [50465, 407, 1958, 13, 3279, 5348, 1413, 568, 3643, 502, 13, 10607, 3279, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 211530, "start": 2121.3, "end": 2122.3, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50665, 7587, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 211530, "start": 2122.3, "end": 2124.3, "text": " Now apply the second part of the rule.", "tokens": [50715, 823, 3079, 264, 1150, 644, 295, 264, 4978, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 211530, "start": 2124.3, "end": 2126.3, "text": " Chop off the integer part to the left of the decimal.", "tokens": [50815, 25615, 766, 264, 24922, 644, 281, 264, 1411, 295, 264, 26601, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 211530, "start": 2126.3, "end": 2128.3, "text": " So the 1 disappears.", "tokens": [50915, 407, 264, 502, 25527, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 211530, "start": 2128.3, "end": 2130.3, "text": " I'm left with 0.011's hour.", "tokens": [51015, 286, 478, 1411, 365, 1958, 13, 15, 5348, 311, 1773, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 211530, "start": 2130.3, "end": 2131.3, "text": " Look at what just happened.", "tokens": [51115, 2053, 412, 437, 445, 2011, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 211530, "start": 2131.3, "end": 2136.3, "text": " The very first digit of your original number was permanently deleted.", "tokens": [51165, 440, 588, 700, 14293, 295, 428, 3380, 1230, 390, 24042, 22981, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 211530, "start": 2136.3, "end": 2141.3, "text": " And every single hidden digit further down the line was pulled one position closer to the front.", "tokens": [51415, 400, 633, 2167, 7633, 14293, 3052, 760, 264, 1622, 390, 7373, 472, 2535, 4966, 281, 264, 1868, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 211530, "start": 2141.3, "end": 2142.3, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51665, 876, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 211530, "start": 2142.3, "end": 2143.3, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51715, 876, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 211530, "start": 2143.3, "end": 2144.3, "text": " I see where this is going.", "tokens": [51765, 286, 536, 689, 341, 307, 516, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08575987114625819, "compression_ratio": 1.5653710247349824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043069650528707e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 214430, "start": 2144.3, "end": 2148.3, "text": " Let's say you are a scientist measuring the initial state of a system.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 291, 366, 257, 12662, 13389, 264, 5883, 1785, 295, 257, 1185, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035685682809481055, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899307915899884e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 214430, "start": 2148.3, "end": 2154.3, "text": " You have an incredibly precise instrument, but it is only accurate to 50 decimal places.", "tokens": [50565, 509, 362, 364, 6252, 13600, 7198, 11, 457, 309, 307, 787, 8559, 281, 2625, 26601, 3190, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035685682809481055, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899307915899884e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 214430, "start": 2154.3, "end": 2157.3, "text": " The 51st decimal place is a total mystery.", "tokens": [50865, 440, 18485, 372, 26601, 1081, 307, 257, 3217, 11422, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035685682809481055, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899307915899884e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 214430, "start": 2157.3, "end": 2159.3, "text": " It's a microscopic rounding error.", "tokens": [51015, 467, 311, 257, 47897, 48237, 6713, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035685682809481055, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899307915899884e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 214430, "start": 2159.3, "end": 2164.3, "text": " If I iterate the doubling map 50 times, I delete the first 50 digits.", "tokens": [51115, 759, 286, 44497, 264, 33651, 4471, 2625, 1413, 11, 286, 12097, 264, 700, 2625, 27011, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035685682809481055, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899307915899884e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 214430, "start": 2164.3, "end": 2169.3, "text": " The first 50 iterations methodically destroy all the information you actually measured.", "tokens": [51365, 440, 700, 2625, 36540, 3170, 984, 5293, 439, 264, 1589, 291, 767, 12690, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.035685682809481055, "compression_ratio": 1.6322314049586777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899307915899884e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 216930, "start": 2169.3, "end": 2174.3, "text": " And that tiny, completely unknown rounding error that was sitting in the 51st decimal place.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 5870, 11, 2584, 9841, 48237, 6713, 300, 390, 3798, 294, 264, 18485, 372, 26601, 1081, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11927965054145226, "compression_ratio": 1.4580152671755726, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686909016030982e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 216930, "start": 2174.3, "end": 2177.3, "text": " It has now been shifted 50 places to the left.", "tokens": [50615, 467, 575, 586, 668, 18892, 2625, 3190, 281, 264, 1411, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11927965054145226, "compression_ratio": 1.4580152671755726, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686909016030982e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 216930, "start": 2177.3, "end": 2178.3, "text": " It's the leading digit.", "tokens": [50765, 467, 311, 264, 5775, 14293, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11927965054145226, "compression_ratio": 1.4580152671755726, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686909016030982e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 216930, "start": 2178.3, "end": 2179.3, "text": " It's now the leading digit.", "tokens": [50815, 467, 311, 586, 264, 5775, 14293, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11927965054145226, "compression_ratio": 1.4580152671755726, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686909016030982e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 217930, "start": 2179.3, "end": 2183.3, "text": " It completely and utterly controls the macroscopic behavior of the system.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2584, 293, 30251, 9003, 264, 7912, 38006, 299, 5223, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11306377410888672, "compression_ratio": 1.3788819875776397, "no_speech_prob": 2.1248801329587508e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 217930, "start": 2183.3, "end": 2185.3, "text": " That is genuinely terrifying.", "tokens": [50565, 663, 307, 17839, 18106, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11306377410888672, "compression_ratio": 1.3788819875776397, "no_speech_prob": 2.1248801329587508e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 217930, "start": 2185.3, "end": 2188.3, "text": " It's determinism without predictability.", "tokens": [50665, 467, 311, 15957, 1434, 1553, 6069, 2310, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11306377410888672, "compression_ratio": 1.3788819875776397, "no_speech_prob": 2.1248801329587508e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 217930, "start": 2188.3, "end": 2192.3, "text": " If you somehow possess the infinite knowledge of every single decimal place,", "tokens": [50815, 759, 291, 6063, 17490, 264, 13785, 3601, 295, 633, 2167, 26601, 1081, 11, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11306377410888672, "compression_ratio": 1.3788819875776397, "no_speech_prob": 2.1248801329587508e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 219230, "start": 2192.3, "end": 2195.3, "text": " you could predict the future flawlessly.", "tokens": [50365, 291, 727, 6069, 264, 2027, 13717, 12048, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08699997266133626, "compression_ratio": 1.3432835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806270339095544e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 219230, "start": 2195.3, "end": 2199.3, "text": " But because infinite precision is physically impossible in reality,", "tokens": [50515, 583, 570, 13785, 18356, 307, 9762, 6243, 294, 4103, 11, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08699997266133626, "compression_ratio": 1.3432835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806270339095544e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 219230, "start": 2199.3, "end": 2202.3, "text": " the iterative process acts like a relentless magnifying glass.", "tokens": [50715, 264, 17138, 1166, 1399, 10672, 411, 257, 46136, 4944, 5489, 4276, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08699997266133626, "compression_ratio": 1.3432835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806270339095544e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 219230, "start": 2202.3, "end": 2203.3, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50865, 7587, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08699997266133626, "compression_ratio": 1.3432835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806270339095544e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 220330, "start": 2203.3, "end": 2208.3, "text": " It takes your microscopic ignorance and stretches it until it shatters your ability to predict anything.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2516, 428, 47897, 25390, 293, 29058, 309, 1826, 309, 402, 37690, 428, 3485, 281, 6069, 1340, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05933220853510591, "compression_ratio": 1.7822878228782288, "no_speech_prob": 1.489925804259995e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 220330, "start": 2208.3, "end": 2212.3, "text": " This realization completely upended modern physics.", "tokens": [50615, 639, 25138, 2584, 493, 3502, 4363, 10649, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05933220853510591, "compression_ratio": 1.7822878228782288, "no_speech_prob": 1.489925804259995e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 220330, "start": 2212.3, "end": 2217.3, "text": " We finally understood that systems like global weather patterns, fluid turbulence,", "tokens": [50815, 492, 2721, 7320, 300, 3652, 411, 4338, 5503, 8294, 11, 9113, 48612, 11, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05933220853510591, "compression_ratio": 1.7822878228782288, "no_speech_prob": 1.489925804259995e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 220330, "start": 2217.3, "end": 2222.3, "text": " or the long-term orbits of planets are not unpredictable because they are magically random.", "tokens": [51065, 420, 264, 938, 12, 7039, 43522, 295, 15126, 366, 406, 31160, 570, 436, 366, 39763, 4974, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05933220853510591, "compression_ratio": 1.7822878228782288, "no_speech_prob": 1.489925804259995e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 220330, "start": 2222.3, "end": 2225.3, "text": " They are unpredictable because the iterative geometry of time itself", "tokens": [51315, 814, 366, 31160, 570, 264, 17138, 1166, 18426, 295, 565, 2564, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05933220853510591, "compression_ratio": 1.7822878228782288, "no_speech_prob": 1.489925804259995e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 220330, "start": 2225.3, "end": 2228.3, "text": " continually amplifies our microscopic uncertainty.", "tokens": [51465, 22277, 9731, 11221, 527, 47897, 15697, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05933220853510591, "compression_ratio": 1.7822878228782288, "no_speech_prob": 1.489925804259995e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 220330, "start": 2228.3, "end": 2230.3, "text": " The iterative geometry of time.", "tokens": [51615, 440, 17138, 1166, 18426, 295, 565, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05933220853510591, "compression_ratio": 1.7822878228782288, "no_speech_prob": 1.489925804259995e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 223030, "start": 2230.3, "end": 2235.3, "text": " And speaking of the flow of time, the text brings up an algebraic structure called a semi-group.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 4124, 295, 264, 3095, 295, 565, 11, 264, 2487, 5607, 493, 364, 21989, 299, 3877, 1219, 257, 12909, 12, 17377, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04172551716473086, "compression_ratio": 1.7694704049844237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678667975338906e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 223030, "start": 2235.3, "end": 2238.3, "text": " What does algebra have to do with the arrow of time?", "tokens": [50615, 708, 775, 21989, 362, 281, 360, 365, 264, 11610, 295, 565, 30, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04172551716473086, "compression_ratio": 1.7694704049844237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678667975338906e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 223030, "start": 2238.3, "end": 2242.3, "text": " To understand a semi-group, you have to look at its older sibling, the group.", "tokens": [50765, 1407, 1223, 257, 12909, 12, 17377, 11, 291, 362, 281, 574, 412, 1080, 4906, 39409, 11, 264, 1594, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04172551716473086, "compression_ratio": 1.7694704049844237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678667975338906e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 223030, "start": 2242.3, "end": 2247.3, "text": " In abstract algebra, a group is a structure that demands perfect symmetry.", "tokens": [50965, 682, 12649, 21989, 11, 257, 1594, 307, 257, 3877, 300, 15107, 2176, 25440, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04172551716473086, "compression_ratio": 1.7694704049844237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678667975338906e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 223030, "start": 2247.3, "end": 2251.3, "text": " The core rule of a group is that every single action must have an inverse.", "tokens": [51215, 440, 4965, 4978, 295, 257, 1594, 307, 300, 633, 2167, 3069, 1633, 362, 364, 17340, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04172551716473086, "compression_ratio": 1.7694704049844237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678667975338906e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 223030, "start": 2251.3, "end": 2252.3, "text": " Like an undo button.", "tokens": [51415, 1743, 364, 23779, 2960, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04172551716473086, "compression_ratio": 1.7694704049844237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678667975338906e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 223030, "start": 2252.3, "end": 2253.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51465, 1779, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04172551716473086, "compression_ratio": 1.7694704049844237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678667975338906e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 223030, "start": 2253.3, "end": 2257.3, "text": " Whatever transformation you perform, you can mathematically undo it to get back to where you started.", "tokens": [51515, 8541, 9887, 291, 2042, 11, 291, 393, 44003, 23779, 309, 281, 483, 646, 281, 689, 291, 1409, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04172551716473086, "compression_ratio": 1.7694704049844237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678667975338906e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 223030, "start": 2257.3, "end": 2259.3, "text": " But time in the physical universe doesn't play by that rule.", "tokens": [51715, 583, 565, 294, 264, 4001, 6445, 1177, 380, 862, 538, 300, 4978, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04172551716473086, "compression_ratio": 1.7694704049844237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678667975338906e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 225930, "start": 2259.3, "end": 2263.3, "text": " I can drop a glass on the floor and shatter it, but I cannot unshatter the glass.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 393, 3270, 257, 4276, 322, 264, 4123, 293, 402, 1161, 309, 11, 457, 286, 2644, 2693, 71, 1161, 264, 4276, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08888802641914004, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499354388108348e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 225930, "start": 2263.3, "end": 2265.3, "text": " I can't unscramble an egg.", "tokens": [50565, 286, 393, 380, 2693, 66, 48382, 364, 3777, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08888802641914004, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499354388108348e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 225930, "start": 2265.3, "end": 2268.3, "text": " Physical reality is full of irreversible processes.", "tokens": [50665, 31918, 4103, 307, 1577, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 7555, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08888802641914004, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499354388108348e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 225930, "start": 2268.3, "end": 2275.3, "text": " Once heat dissecates into a room, or once a non-injective function collapses distinct points into a single fiber,", "tokens": [50815, 3443, 3738, 717, 8159, 1024, 666, 257, 1808, 11, 420, 1564, 257, 2107, 12, 259, 1020, 488, 2445, 48765, 10644, 2793, 666, 257, 2167, 12874, 11, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08888802641914004, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499354388108348e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 225930, "start": 2275.3, "end": 2277.3, "text": " the information is gone.", "tokens": [51165, 264, 1589, 307, 2780, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08888802641914004, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499354388108348e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 227730, "start": 2277.3, "end": 2280.3, "text": " You cannot run the equation backward.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 2644, 1190, 264, 5367, 23897, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731529746257083, "compression_ratio": 1.6054054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.438328731291627e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 227730, "start": 2280.3, "end": 2281.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50515, 1779, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731529746257083, "compression_ratio": 1.6054054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.438328731291627e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 227730, "start": 2281.3, "end": 2286.3, "text": " The mathematics of these irreversible processes transformations that can be composed forward into the future,", "tokens": [50565, 440, 18666, 295, 613, 16014, 840, 964, 7555, 34852, 300, 393, 312, 18204, 2128, 666, 264, 2027, 11, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731529746257083, "compression_ratio": 1.6054054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.438328731291627e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 227730, "start": 2286.3, "end": 2290.3, "text": " but never inverted backward into the past, is modeled by a semi-group.", "tokens": [50815, 457, 1128, 38969, 23897, 666, 264, 1791, 11, 307, 37140, 538, 257, 12909, 12, 17377, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731529746257083, "compression_ratio": 1.6054054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.438328731291627e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 227730, "start": 2290.3, "end": 2294.3, "text": " The fact that a semi-group lacks an inverse is not a mathematical flaw.", "tokens": [51015, 440, 1186, 300, 257, 12909, 12, 17377, 31132, 364, 17340, 307, 406, 257, 18894, 13717, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731529746257083, "compression_ratio": 1.6054054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.438328731291627e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 229430, "start": 2294.3, "end": 2299.3, "text": " It is the precise algebraic model for the irreversible arrow of time.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 13600, 21989, 299, 2316, 337, 264, 16014, 840, 964, 11610, 295, 565, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16467978954315185, "compression_ratio": 1.0147058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.897320842103589e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 229930, "start": 2299.3, "end": 2303.3, "text": " So, if chaotic feedback loops are relentlessly amplifying our ignorance,", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 498, 27013, 5824, 16121, 366, 34045, 12048, 9731, 5489, 527, 25390, 11, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06682874606205867, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 2.7718738762616546e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 229930, "start": 2303.3, "end": 2306.3, "text": " and semi-groups are constantly destroying the information of the past,", "tokens": [50565, 293, 12909, 12, 17377, 82, 366, 6460, 19926, 264, 1589, 295, 264, 1791, 11, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06682874606205867, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 2.7718738762616546e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 229930, "start": 2306.3, "end": 2309.3, "text": " how do we actually quantify any of this?", "tokens": [50715, 577, 360, 321, 767, 40421, 604, 295, 341, 30, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06682874606205867, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 2.7718738762616546e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 229930, "start": 2309.3, "end": 2312.3, "text": " How do we mathematically measure the uncertainty we are drowning in?", "tokens": [50865, 1012, 360, 321, 44003, 3481, 264, 15697, 321, 366, 37198, 294, 30, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06682874606205867, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 2.7718738762616546e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 229930, "start": 2312.3, "end": 2317.3, "text": " This brings us to part five, information, entropy, and the mathematics of knowledge.", "tokens": [51015, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 644, 1732, 11, 1589, 11, 30867, 11, 293, 264, 18666, 295, 3601, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06682874606205867, "compression_ratio": 1.5794392523364487, "no_speech_prob": 2.7718738762616546e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 231730, "start": 2317.3, "end": 2320.3, "text": " This section is the culmination of the entire manuscript.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 3541, 307, 264, 28583, 399, 295, 264, 2302, 23928, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03534577064907428, "compression_ratio": 1.7302904564315353, "no_speech_prob": 2.4088814710304662e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 231730, "start": 2320.3, "end": 2321.3, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50515, 865, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03534577064907428, "compression_ratio": 1.7302904564315353, "no_speech_prob": 2.4088814710304662e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 231730, "start": 2321.3, "end": 2326.3, "text": " To measure uncertainty, we first have to mathematically define what information actually is.", "tokens": [50565, 1407, 3481, 15697, 11, 321, 700, 362, 281, 44003, 6964, 437, 1589, 767, 307, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03534577064907428, "compression_ratio": 1.7302904564315353, "no_speech_prob": 2.4088814710304662e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 231730, "start": 2326.3, "end": 2327.3, "text": " It's not just data.", "tokens": [50815, 467, 311, 406, 445, 1412, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03534577064907428, "compression_ratio": 1.7302904564315353, "no_speech_prob": 2.4088814710304662e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 231730, "start": 2327.3, "end": 2332.3, "text": " No. In this context, information is not a collection of facts or Wikipedia articles.", "tokens": [50865, 883, 13, 682, 341, 4319, 11, 1589, 307, 406, 257, 5765, 295, 9130, 420, 28999, 11290, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03534577064907428, "compression_ratio": 1.7302904564315353, "no_speech_prob": 2.4088814710304662e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 231730, "start": 2332.3, "end": 2337.3, "text": " Information is defined purely and strictly as the reduction of uncertainty.", "tokens": [51115, 15357, 307, 7642, 17491, 293, 20792, 382, 264, 11004, 295, 15697, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03534577064907428, "compression_ratio": 1.7302904564315353, "no_speech_prob": 2.4088814710304662e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 231730, "start": 2337.3, "end": 2340.3, "text": " It is the elimination of possible states.", "tokens": [51365, 467, 307, 264, 29224, 295, 1944, 4368, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03534577064907428, "compression_ratio": 1.7302904564315353, "no_speech_prob": 2.4088814710304662e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 231730, "start": 2340.3, "end": 2342.3, "text": " Let me test my understanding of this.", "tokens": [51515, 961, 385, 1500, 452, 3701, 295, 341, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03534577064907428, "compression_ratio": 1.7302904564315353, "no_speech_prob": 2.4088814710304662e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 234230, "start": 2342.3, "end": 2347.3, "text": " If you hand me a coin, and you tell me it's a trick coin with heads on both sides,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 1011, 385, 257, 11464, 11, 293, 291, 980, 385, 309, 311, 257, 4282, 11464, 365, 8050, 322, 1293, 4881, 11, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04788634258767833, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8469945625015916e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 234230, "start": 2347.3, "end": 2350.3, "text": " flipping it gives me absolutely zero information.", "tokens": [50615, 26886, 309, 2709, 385, 3122, 4018, 1589, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04788634258767833, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8469945625015916e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 234230, "start": 2350.3, "end": 2351.3, "text": " Because you already know what's going to happen.", "tokens": [50765, 1436, 291, 1217, 458, 437, 311, 516, 281, 1051, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04788634258767833, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8469945625015916e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 234230, "start": 2351.3, "end": 2353.3, "text": " Right. I already know the outcome.", "tokens": [50815, 1779, 13, 286, 1217, 458, 264, 9700, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04788634258767833, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8469945625015916e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 234230, "start": 2353.3, "end": 2358.3, "text": " There is zero uncertainty, therefore zero information is generated by the flip.", "tokens": [50915, 821, 307, 4018, 15697, 11, 4412, 4018, 1589, 307, 10833, 538, 264, 7929, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04788634258767833, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8469945625015916e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 234230, "start": 2358.3, "end": 2361.3, "text": " But if it is a fair coin, I have uncertainty.", "tokens": [51165, 583, 498, 309, 307, 257, 3143, 11464, 11, 286, 362, 15697, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04788634258767833, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8469945625015916e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 234230, "start": 2361.3, "end": 2366.3, "text": " The moment it lands, a possibility is eliminated, and I gain information.", "tokens": [51315, 440, 1623, 309, 5949, 11, 257, 7959, 307, 20308, 11, 293, 286, 6052, 1589, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04788634258767833, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8469945625015916e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 234230, "start": 2366.3, "end": 2369.3, "text": " The math actually supports your intuition perfectly.", "tokens": [51565, 440, 5221, 767, 9346, 428, 24002, 6239, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04788634258767833, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8469945625015916e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 236930, "start": 2369.3, "end": 2375.3, "text": " The more potential possibilities a process eliminates, the more mathematical information you acquire.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 544, 3995, 12178, 257, 1399, 49893, 11, 264, 544, 18894, 1589, 291, 20001, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048954865028118265, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 2.3075586580434404e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 236930, "start": 2375.3, "end": 2381.3, "text": " And to calculate this formally, the text explains why information theory relies so heavily on logarithms.", "tokens": [50665, 400, 281, 8873, 341, 25983, 11, 264, 2487, 13948, 983, 1589, 5261, 30910, 370, 10950, 322, 41473, 355, 2592, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048954865028118265, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 2.3075586580434404e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 236930, "start": 2381.3, "end": 2384.3, "text": " Yeah, the logarithms. Why do they always show up when we talk about data and bits?", "tokens": [50965, 865, 11, 264, 41473, 355, 2592, 13, 1545, 360, 436, 1009, 855, 493, 562, 321, 751, 466, 1412, 293, 9239, 30, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048954865028118265, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 2.3075586580434404e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 236930, "start": 2384.3, "end": 2388.3, "text": " It solves a fundamental problem of how choices interact.", "tokens": [51115, 467, 39890, 257, 8088, 1154, 295, 577, 7994, 4648, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048954865028118265, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 2.3075586580434404e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 236930, "start": 2388.3, "end": 2390.3, "text": " Let's stick with your coins.", "tokens": [51315, 961, 311, 2897, 365, 428, 13561, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048954865028118265, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 2.3075586580434404e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 236930, "start": 2390.3, "end": 2394.3, "text": " If you flip one fair coin, you have two possible outcomes.", "tokens": [51415, 759, 291, 7929, 472, 3143, 11464, 11, 291, 362, 732, 1944, 10070, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048954865028118265, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 2.3075586580434404e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 236930, "start": 2394.3, "end": 2397.3, "text": " If you flip two independent coins, how many outcomes do you have?", "tokens": [51615, 759, 291, 7929, 732, 6695, 13561, 11, 577, 867, 10070, 360, 291, 362, 30, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.048954865028118265, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 2.3075586580434404e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 239730, "start": 2397.3, "end": 2400.3, "text": " Two times two. Four possible outcomes.", "tokens": [50365, 4453, 1413, 732, 13, 7451, 1944, 10070, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061199699129377096, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179211391453065e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 239730, "start": 2400.3, "end": 2402.3, "text": " Notice what happened mathematically.", "tokens": [50515, 13428, 437, 2011, 44003, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061199699129377096, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179211391453065e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 239730, "start": 2402.3, "end": 2405.3, "text": " Independent choices multiply the number of possible states.", "tokens": [50615, 40310, 7994, 12972, 264, 1230, 295, 1944, 4368, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061199699129377096, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179211391453065e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 239730, "start": 2405.3, "end": 2411.3, "text": " But when we measure the information gained from those choices, we want the measurement to be additive.", "tokens": [50765, 583, 562, 321, 3481, 264, 1589, 12634, 490, 729, 7994, 11, 321, 528, 264, 13160, 281, 312, 45558, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061199699129377096, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179211391453065e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 239730, "start": 2411.3, "end": 2412.3, "text": " Additive.", "tokens": [51065, 5349, 2187, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061199699129377096, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179211391453065e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 239730, "start": 2412.3, "end": 2419.3, "text": " If one coin flip yields one bit of information, two coin flips should yield one plus one, which is two bits of information.", "tokens": [51115, 759, 472, 11464, 7929, 32168, 472, 857, 295, 1589, 11, 732, 11464, 40249, 820, 11257, 472, 1804, 472, 11, 597, 307, 732, 9239, 295, 1589, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061199699129377096, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179211391453065e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 241930, "start": 2419.3, "end": 2426.3, "text": " We need a mathematical function that takes the multiplication of physical states and magically converts it into the addition of informational bits.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 643, 257, 18894, 2445, 300, 2516, 264, 27290, 295, 4001, 4368, 293, 39763, 38874, 309, 666, 264, 4500, 295, 49391, 9239, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06732041605057255, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7685174071718768e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 241930, "start": 2426.3, "end": 2429.3, "text": " And that is exactly the defining property of a logarithm.", "tokens": [50715, 400, 300, 307, 2293, 264, 17827, 4707, 295, 257, 41473, 32674, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06732041605057255, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7685174071718768e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 241930, "start": 2429.3, "end": 2434.3, "text": " The log of a times b is equal to the log of a plus the log of b.", "tokens": [50865, 440, 3565, 295, 257, 1413, 272, 307, 2681, 281, 264, 3565, 295, 257, 1804, 264, 3565, 295, 272, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06732041605057255, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7685174071718768e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 243430, "start": 2434.3, "end": 2437.3, "text": " It isn't just an arbitrary complex button on a calculator.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1943, 380, 445, 364, 23211, 3997, 2960, 322, 257, 24993, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03937595784664154, "compression_ratio": 1.7264957264957266, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 243430, "start": 2437.3, "end": 2443.3, "text": " It is the fundamental mathematical bridge between multiplicative probability and additive information.", "tokens": [50515, 467, 307, 264, 8088, 18894, 7283, 1296, 17596, 1166, 8482, 293, 45558, 1589, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03937595784664154, "compression_ratio": 1.7264957264957266, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 243430, "start": 2443.3, "end": 2447.3, "text": " It is the only function that makes the universe of information additive.", "tokens": [50815, 467, 307, 264, 787, 2445, 300, 1669, 264, 6445, 295, 1589, 45558, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03937595784664154, "compression_ratio": 1.7264957264957266, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 243430, "start": 2447.3, "end": 2452.3, "text": " And this leads directly to Claude Shannon's monumental concept of entropy.", "tokens": [51015, 400, 341, 6689, 3838, 281, 12947, 2303, 28974, 311, 43105, 3410, 295, 30867, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03937595784664154, "compression_ratio": 1.7264957264957266, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 243430, "start": 2452.3, "end": 2457.3, "text": " Shannon entropy is the mathematical measurement of the average uncertainty of a random source.", "tokens": [51265, 28974, 30867, 307, 264, 18894, 13160, 295, 264, 4274, 15697, 295, 257, 4974, 4009, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03937595784664154, "compression_ratio": 1.7264957264957266, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 245730, "start": 2457.3, "end": 2464.3, "text": " Okay, so if I have a completely fair coin, it has 50-50 odds, it is maximally unpredictable, so it has very high entropy.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 498, 286, 362, 257, 2584, 3143, 11464, 11, 309, 575, 2625, 12, 2803, 17439, 11, 309, 307, 5138, 379, 31160, 11, 370, 309, 575, 588, 1090, 30867, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05793547257781029, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 3.266065152704445e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 245730, "start": 2464.3, "end": 2465.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50715, 1779, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05793547257781029, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 3.266065152704445e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 245730, "start": 2465.3, "end": 2467.3, "text": " But what if the coin is heavily biased?", "tokens": [50765, 583, 437, 498, 264, 11464, 307, 10950, 28035, 30, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05793547257781029, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 3.266065152704445e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 245730, "start": 2467.3, "end": 2472.3, "text": " Let's say it lands on heads 99% of the time and tails only 1% of the time.", "tokens": [50865, 961, 311, 584, 309, 5949, 322, 8050, 11803, 4, 295, 264, 565, 293, 28537, 787, 502, 4, 295, 264, 565, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05793547257781029, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 3.266065152704445e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 245730, "start": 2472.3, "end": 2476.3, "text": " If the coin is heavily biased, your internal uncertainty plummets.", "tokens": [51115, 759, 264, 11464, 307, 10950, 28035, 11, 428, 6920, 15697, 25854, 76, 1385, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05793547257781029, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 3.266065152704445e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 245730, "start": 2476.3, "end": 2478.3, "text": " You fully expect it to land on heads.", "tokens": [51315, 509, 4498, 2066, 309, 281, 2117, 322, 8050, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05793547257781029, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 3.266065152704445e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 245730, "start": 2478.3, "end": 2481.3, "text": " When it does, you learn almost nothing.", "tokens": [51415, 1133, 309, 775, 11, 291, 1466, 1920, 1825, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05793547257781029, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 3.266065152704445e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 245730, "start": 2481.3, "end": 2482.3, "text": " You aren't surprised.", "tokens": [51565, 509, 3212, 380, 6100, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05793547257781029, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 3.266065152704445e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 245730, "start": 2482.3, "end": 2483.3, "text": " Let's say your entropy is low.", "tokens": [51615, 961, 311, 584, 428, 30867, 307, 2295, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05793547257781029, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 3.266065152704445e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 248330, "start": 2483.3, "end": 2488.3, "text": " Therefore, the average uncertainty, the Shannon entropy of that biased coin is incredibly low.", "tokens": [50365, 7504, 11, 264, 4274, 15697, 11, 264, 28974, 30867, 295, 300, 28035, 11464, 307, 6252, 2295, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07205418423489407, "compression_ratio": 1.6372881355932203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488050074564553e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 248330, "start": 2488.3, "end": 2492.3, "text": " Entropy is dictated by how evenly the probability is distributed across the states.", "tokens": [50615, 3951, 27514, 307, 12569, 770, 538, 577, 17658, 264, 8482, 307, 12631, 2108, 264, 4368, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07205418423489407, "compression_ratio": 1.6372881355932203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488050074564553e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 248330, "start": 2492.3, "end": 2494.3, "text": " And this isn't just abstract philosophy, right?", "tokens": [50815, 400, 341, 1943, 380, 445, 12649, 10675, 11, 558, 30, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07205418423489407, "compression_ratio": 1.6372881355932203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488050074564553e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 248330, "start": 2494.3, "end": 2498.3, "text": " This directly dictates how our computers compress data.", "tokens": [50915, 639, 3838, 12569, 1024, 577, 527, 10807, 14778, 1412, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07205418423489407, "compression_ratio": 1.6372881355932203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488050074564553e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 248330, "start": 2498.3, "end": 2500.3, "text": " The text calls this coding theory.", "tokens": [51115, 440, 2487, 5498, 341, 17720, 5261, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07205418423489407, "compression_ratio": 1.6372881355932203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488050074564553e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 248330, "start": 2500.3, "end": 2502.3, "text": " It is entirely practical.", "tokens": [51215, 467, 307, 7696, 8496, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07205418423489407, "compression_ratio": 1.6372881355932203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488050074564553e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 248330, "start": 2502.3, "end": 2506.3, "text": " To understand data compression, look at the historical precedent Morse code.", "tokens": [51315, 1407, 1223, 1412, 19355, 11, 574, 412, 264, 8584, 37388, 5146, 405, 3089, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07205418423489407, "compression_ratio": 1.6372881355932203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488050074564553e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 248330, "start": 2506.3, "end": 2511.3, "text": " Why did Samuel Morse assign a single short dot to the letter E", "tokens": [51515, 1545, 630, 23036, 5146, 405, 6269, 257, 2167, 2099, 5893, 281, 264, 5063, 462, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07205418423489407, "compression_ratio": 1.6372881355932203, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488050074564553e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 251130, "start": 2511.3, "end": 2516.3, "text": " while assigning a long complex dash dash dot dot to the letter Z?", "tokens": [50365, 1339, 49602, 257, 938, 3997, 8240, 8240, 5893, 5893, 281, 264, 5063, 1176, 30, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07513442509610888, "compression_ratio": 1.4952380952380953, "no_speech_prob": 2.201722094571923e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 251130, "start": 2516.3, "end": 2521.3, "text": " Because E is everywhere in the English language and Z is incredibly rare.", "tokens": [50615, 1436, 462, 307, 5315, 294, 264, 3669, 2856, 293, 1176, 307, 6252, 5892, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07513442509610888, "compression_ratio": 1.4952380952380953, "no_speech_prob": 2.201722094571923e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 251130, "start": 2521.3, "end": 2527.3, "text": " If you gave E a long code, telegraph operators would waste hours tapping out simple sentences.", "tokens": [50865, 759, 291, 2729, 462, 257, 938, 3089, 11, 4304, 34091, 19077, 576, 5964, 2496, 21444, 484, 2199, 16579, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07513442509610888, "compression_ratio": 1.4952380952380953, "no_speech_prob": 2.201722094571923e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 251130, "start": 2527.3, "end": 2532.3, "text": " You give the shortest descriptions to the most common events to save bandwidth.", "tokens": [51165, 509, 976, 264, 31875, 24406, 281, 264, 881, 2689, 3931, 281, 3155, 23647, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07513442509610888, "compression_ratio": 1.4952380952380953, "no_speech_prob": 2.201722094571923e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 253230, "start": 2532.3, "end": 2535.3, "text": " That is the conceptual heart of variable length coding.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 24106, 1917, 295, 7006, 4641, 17720, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970128071772588, "compression_ratio": 1.6394849785407726, "no_speech_prob": 1.3459168675400424e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 253230, "start": 2535.3, "end": 2541.3, "text": " Optimal data compression algorithms mathematically assign short binary descriptions to highly probable data", "tokens": [50515, 21455, 10650, 1412, 19355, 14642, 44003, 6269, 2099, 17434, 24406, 281, 5405, 21759, 1412, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970128071772588, "compression_ratio": 1.6394849785407726, "no_speech_prob": 1.3459168675400424e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 253230, "start": 2541.3, "end": 2544.3, "text": " and long descriptions to rare surprising data.", "tokens": [50815, 293, 938, 24406, 281, 5892, 8830, 1412, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970128071772588, "compression_ratio": 1.6394849785407726, "no_speech_prob": 1.3459168675400424e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 253230, "start": 2544.3, "end": 2546.3, "text": " Right, to optimize the space.", "tokens": [50965, 1779, 11, 281, 19719, 264, 1901, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970128071772588, "compression_ratio": 1.6394849785407726, "no_speech_prob": 1.3459168675400424e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 253230, "start": 2546.3, "end": 2554.3, "text": " Claude Shannon proved mathematically that the entropy of a data source acts as the absolute unbreakable speed limit for lossless compression.", "tokens": [51065, 12947, 2303, 28974, 14617, 44003, 300, 264, 30867, 295, 257, 1412, 4009, 10672, 382, 264, 8236, 517, 13225, 712, 3073, 4948, 337, 4470, 1832, 19355, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970128071772588, "compression_ratio": 1.6394849785407726, "no_speech_prob": 1.3459168675400424e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 255430, "start": 2554.3, "end": 2561.3, "text": " You physically cannot compress a file into a size smaller than its inherent entropy without permanently collapsing distinctions and losing data.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 9762, 2644, 14778, 257, 3991, 666, 257, 2744, 4356, 813, 1080, 26387, 30867, 1553, 24042, 45339, 1483, 49798, 293, 7027, 1412, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06359797657126247, "compression_ratio": 1.594306049822064, "no_speech_prob": 2.210017108553175e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 255430, "start": 2561.3, "end": 2564.3, "text": " Compression is amazing because it squeezes out all the redundancy.", "tokens": [50715, 6620, 2775, 307, 2243, 570, 309, 22390, 279, 484, 439, 264, 27830, 6717, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06359797657126247, "compression_ratio": 1.594306049822064, "no_speech_prob": 2.210017108553175e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 255430, "start": 2564.3, "end": 2566.3, "text": " But wait, I have a practical pushback here.", "tokens": [50865, 583, 1699, 11, 286, 362, 257, 8496, 2944, 3207, 510, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06359797657126247, "compression_ratio": 1.594306049822064, "no_speech_prob": 2.210017108553175e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 255430, "start": 2566.3, "end": 2567.3, "text": " Okay, what is it?", "tokens": [50965, 1033, 11, 437, 307, 309, 30, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06359797657126247, "compression_ratio": 1.594306049822064, "no_speech_prob": 2.210017108553175e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 255430, "start": 2567.3, "end": 2571.3, "text": " If I compress a vital file perfectly, I have removed every single redundant bit.", "tokens": [51015, 759, 286, 14778, 257, 11707, 3991, 6239, 11, 286, 362, 7261, 633, 2167, 40997, 857, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06359797657126247, "compression_ratio": 1.594306049822064, "no_speech_prob": 2.210017108553175e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 255430, "start": 2571.3, "end": 2576.3, "text": " That means every remaining 1 and 0 is carrying a massive amount of crucial structural weight.", "tokens": [51215, 663, 1355, 633, 8877, 502, 293, 1958, 307, 9792, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 11462, 15067, 3364, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06359797657126247, "compression_ratio": 1.594306049822064, "no_speech_prob": 2.210017108553175e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 257630, "start": 2576.3, "end": 2583.3, "text": " But what if I am transmitting that perfectly compressed file over a noisy, terrible Wi-Fi connection?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 437, 498, 286, 669, 7715, 2414, 300, 6239, 30353, 3991, 670, 257, 24518, 11, 6237, 14035, 12, 13229, 4984, 30, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04840276137642238, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.854057489134031e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 257630, "start": 2583.3, "end": 2590.3, "text": " If a thermal spike in the router flips just a single bit from a 0 to a 1, my entire file is hopelessly corrupted because there is no backup data?", "tokens": [50715, 759, 257, 15070, 21053, 294, 264, 22492, 40249, 445, 257, 2167, 857, 490, 257, 1958, 281, 257, 502, 11, 452, 2302, 3991, 307, 27317, 356, 39480, 570, 456, 307, 572, 14807, 1412, 30, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04840276137642238, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.854057489134031e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 257630, "start": 2590.3, "end": 2592.3, "text": " Doesn't the real world require redundancy?", "tokens": [51065, 12955, 380, 264, 957, 1002, 3651, 27830, 6717, 30, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04840276137642238, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.854057489134031e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 257630, "start": 2592.3, "end": 2598.3, "text": " That is a phenomenal observation and it highlights the exact boundary between compression and error correction.", "tokens": [51165, 663, 307, 257, 17778, 14816, 293, 309, 14254, 264, 1900, 12866, 1296, 19355, 293, 6713, 19984, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04840276137642238, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.854057489134031e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 257630, "start": 2598.3, "end": 2599.3, "text": " Error correction?", "tokens": [51465, 3300, 2874, 19984, 30, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04840276137642238, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.854057489134031e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 257630, "start": 2599.3, "end": 2600.3, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51515, 1079, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04840276137642238, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.854057489134031e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 257630, "start": 2600.3, "end": 2604.3, "text": " Compression actively seeks to eliminate redundancy to save storage space.", "tokens": [51565, 6620, 2775, 13022, 28840, 281, 13819, 27830, 6717, 281, 3155, 6725, 1901, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04840276137642238, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.854057489134031e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 260430, "start": 2604.3, "end": 2607.3, "text": " Error correcting codes do the exact opposite.", "tokens": [50365, 3300, 2874, 47032, 14211, 360, 264, 1900, 6182, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06538459429374108, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 2.634667657652745e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 260430, "start": 2607.3, "end": 2616.3, "text": " They deliberately and systematically embed mathematically structured redundancy into the data so that the core information can survive the chaotic noise of physical reality.", "tokens": [50515, 814, 23506, 293, 39531, 12240, 44003, 18519, 27830, 6717, 666, 264, 1412, 370, 300, 264, 4965, 1589, 393, 7867, 264, 27013, 5658, 295, 4001, 4103, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06538459429374108, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 2.634667657652745e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 260430, "start": 2616.3, "end": 2618.3, "text": " How does that actually work mechanically?", "tokens": [50965, 1012, 775, 300, 767, 589, 4236, 984, 30, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06538459429374108, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 2.634667657652745e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 260430, "start": 2618.3, "end": 2621.3, "text": " How do you mathematically build armor for a piece of data?", "tokens": [51065, 1012, 360, 291, 44003, 1322, 13124, 337, 257, 2522, 295, 1412, 30, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06538459429374108, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 2.634667657652745e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 260430, "start": 2621.3, "end": 2624.3, "text": " It is achieved through the geometry of packing.", "tokens": [51215, 467, 307, 11042, 807, 264, 18426, 295, 20815, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06538459429374108, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 2.634667657652745e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 260430, "start": 2624.3, "end": 2631.3, "text": " We take our fragile compressed messages and we forcefully embed them into a vastly larger, higher dimensional arena called a hamming space.", "tokens": [51365, 492, 747, 527, 23847, 30353, 7897, 293, 321, 3464, 2277, 12240, 552, 666, 257, 41426, 4833, 11, 2946, 18795, 18451, 1219, 257, 36600, 278, 1901, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06538459429374108, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 2.634667657652745e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 263130, "start": 2631.3, "end": 2632.3, "text": " Hamming space.", "tokens": [50365, 8234, 2810, 1901, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221564460046512, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.9859634730067253e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 263130, "start": 2632.3, "end": 2633.3, "text": " Hamming space.", "tokens": [50415, 8234, 2810, 1901, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221564460046512, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.9859634730067253e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 263130, "start": 2633.3, "end": 2635.3, "text": " I need help visualizing that.", "tokens": [50465, 286, 643, 854, 5056, 3319, 300, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221564460046512, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.9859634730067253e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 263130, "start": 2635.3, "end": 2637.3, "text": " Imagine a three-dimensional cube.", "tokens": [50565, 11739, 257, 1045, 12, 18759, 13728, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221564460046512, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.9859634730067253e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 263130, "start": 2637.3, "end": 2644.3, "text": " Each of the eight corners of the cube represents a three-bit code word like 0000 or 111.", "tokens": [50665, 6947, 295, 264, 3180, 12413, 295, 264, 13728, 8855, 257, 1045, 12, 5260, 3089, 1349, 411, 7143, 628, 420, 2975, 16, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221564460046512, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.9859634730067253e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 263130, "start": 2644.3, "end": 2645.3, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51015, 1033, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221564460046512, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.9859634730067253e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 263130, "start": 2645.3, "end": 2646.3, "text": " A cube with binary corners.", "tokens": [51065, 316, 13728, 365, 17434, 12413, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221564460046512, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.9859634730067253e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 263130, "start": 2646.3, "end": 2651.3, "text": " Moving along one physical edge of the cube represents flipping exactly one bit.", "tokens": [51115, 14242, 2051, 472, 4001, 4691, 295, 264, 13728, 8855, 26886, 2293, 472, 857, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221564460046512, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.9859634730067253e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 263130, "start": 2651.3, "end": 2654.3, "text": " The distance between corners is called the Hamming distance.", "tokens": [51365, 440, 4560, 1296, 12413, 307, 1219, 264, 8234, 2810, 4560, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221564460046512, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.9859634730067253e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 265430, "start": 2654.3, "end": 2660.3, "text": " The mathematical strategy is to select a tiny subset of those corners to be your valid code words.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18894, 5206, 307, 281, 3048, 257, 5870, 25993, 295, 729, 12413, 281, 312, 428, 7363, 3089, 2283, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06618856073735835, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 2.068042568789674e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 265430, "start": 2660.3, "end": 2664.3, "text": " And you ensure those valid corners are geometrically packed very far apart from each other.", "tokens": [50665, 400, 291, 5586, 729, 7363, 12413, 366, 12956, 81, 984, 13265, 588, 1400, 4936, 490, 1184, 661, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06618856073735835, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 2.068042568789674e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 265430, "start": 2664.3, "end": 2672.3, "text": " So instead of using all the corners, I only allow my computer to use the coordinates 0000 and 111 as valid messages.", "tokens": [50865, 407, 2602, 295, 1228, 439, 264, 12413, 11, 286, 787, 2089, 452, 3820, 281, 764, 264, 21056, 7143, 628, 293, 2975, 16, 382, 7363, 7897, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06618856073735835, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 2.068042568789674e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 265430, "start": 2672.3, "end": 2674.3, "text": " They are on complete opposite sides of the cube.", "tokens": [51265, 814, 366, 322, 3566, 6182, 4881, 295, 264, 13728, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06618856073735835, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 2.068042568789674e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 265430, "start": 2674.3, "end": 2675.3, "text": " They are three steps apart.", "tokens": [51365, 814, 366, 1045, 4439, 4936, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06618856073735835, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 2.068042568789674e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 267530, "start": 2675.3, "end": 2676.3, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0784428201872727, "compression_ratio": 1.5167464114832536, "no_speech_prob": 2.1088300376781444e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 267530, "start": 2676.3, "end": 2685.3, "text": " Now, suppose you transmit the valid word 0000, but as it travels, thermal noise or a physical scratch on a CD flips the single bit.", "tokens": [50415, 823, 11, 7297, 291, 17831, 264, 7363, 1349, 7143, 628, 11, 457, 382, 309, 19863, 11, 15070, 5658, 420, 257, 4001, 8459, 322, 257, 6743, 40249, 264, 2167, 857, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0784428201872727, "compression_ratio": 1.5167464114832536, "no_speech_prob": 2.1088300376781444e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 267530, "start": 2685.3, "end": 2686.3, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50865, 1033, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0784428201872727, "compression_ratio": 1.5167464114832536, "no_speech_prob": 2.1088300376781444e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 267530, "start": 2686.3, "end": 2687.3, "text": " The receiver gets the word 001.", "tokens": [50915, 440, 20086, 2170, 264, 1349, 7143, 16, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0784428201872727, "compression_ratio": 1.5167464114832536, "no_speech_prob": 2.1088300376781444e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 267530, "start": 2687.3, "end": 2692.3, "text": " The receiver looks at his mathematical dictionary and sees that 001 is not a valid corner of the cube.", "tokens": [50965, 440, 20086, 1542, 412, 702, 18894, 25890, 293, 8194, 300, 7143, 16, 307, 406, 257, 7363, 4538, 295, 264, 13728, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0784428201872727, "compression_ratio": 1.5167464114832536, "no_speech_prob": 2.1088300376781444e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 267530, "start": 2692.3, "end": 2695.3, "text": " Because we only allow 0000 and 111.", "tokens": [51215, 1436, 321, 787, 2089, 7143, 628, 293, 2975, 16, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0784428201872727, "compression_ratio": 1.5167464114832536, "no_speech_prob": 2.1088300376781444e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 269530, "start": 2695.3, "end": 2696.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05143530434424724, "compression_ratio": 1.7035714285714285, "no_speech_prob": 1.495761414033181e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 269530, "start": 2696.3, "end": 2704.3, "text": " But geometrically, the corrupted word 001 is only one step away from 0000, while it is two steps away from 1011.", "tokens": [50415, 583, 12956, 81, 984, 11, 264, 39480, 1349, 7143, 16, 307, 787, 472, 1823, 1314, 490, 7143, 628, 11, 1339, 309, 307, 732, 4439, 1314, 490, 1266, 5348, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05143530434424724, "compression_ratio": 1.7035714285714285, "no_speech_prob": 1.495761414033181e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 269530, "start": 2704.3, "end": 2710.3, "text": " The receiver mathematically calculates the closest valid geometry and automatically repairs the damage.", "tokens": [50815, 440, 20086, 44003, 4322, 1024, 264, 13699, 7363, 18426, 293, 6772, 28823, 264, 4344, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05143530434424724, "compression_ratio": 1.7035714285714285, "no_speech_prob": 1.495761414033181e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 269530, "start": 2710.3, "end": 2711.3, "text": " That is incredible.", "tokens": [51115, 663, 307, 4651, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05143530434424724, "compression_ratio": 1.7035714285714285, "no_speech_prob": 1.495761414033181e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 269530, "start": 2711.3, "end": 2717.3, "text": " We are literally using the extra dimensions of math as geometric armor against physical noise in the real world.", "tokens": [51165, 492, 366, 3736, 1228, 264, 2857, 12819, 295, 5221, 382, 33246, 13124, 1970, 4001, 5658, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05143530434424724, "compression_ratio": 1.7035714285714285, "no_speech_prob": 1.495761414033181e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 269530, "start": 2717.3, "end": 2720.3, "text": " The extra dimensions don't convey any new meaning.", "tokens": [51465, 440, 2857, 12819, 500, 380, 16965, 604, 777, 3620, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05143530434424724, "compression_ratio": 1.7035714285714285, "no_speech_prob": 1.495761414033181e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 269530, "start": 2720.3, "end": 2724.3, "text": " They create a spatial buffer to protect the distinctions that matter.", "tokens": [51615, 814, 1884, 257, 23598, 21762, 281, 2371, 264, 1483, 49798, 300, 1871, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05143530434424724, "compression_ratio": 1.7035714285714285, "no_speech_prob": 1.495761414033181e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 272430, "start": 2724.3, "end": 2728.3, "text": " And moving from how we protect information, the text asks one final question.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2684, 490, 577, 321, 2371, 1589, 11, 264, 2487, 8962, 472, 2572, 1168, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04833033038120644, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.8688219374785042e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 272430, "start": 2728.3, "end": 2731.3, "text": " How do we formally acquire it over time?", "tokens": [50565, 1012, 360, 321, 25983, 20001, 309, 670, 565, 30, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04833033038120644, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.8688219374785042e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 272430, "start": 2731.3, "end": 2734.3, "text": " How do we mathematically model the process of learning?", "tokens": [50715, 1012, 360, 321, 44003, 2316, 264, 1399, 295, 2539, 30, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04833033038120644, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.8688219374785042e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 272430, "start": 2734.3, "end": 2737.3, "text": " This transitions us to Bayesian inference.", "tokens": [50865, 639, 23767, 505, 281, 7840, 42434, 38253, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04833033038120644, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.8688219374785042e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 272430, "start": 2737.3, "end": 2738.3, "text": " Bayesian updating.", "tokens": [51015, 7840, 42434, 25113, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04833033038120644, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.8688219374785042e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 272430, "start": 2738.3, "end": 2742.3, "text": " You hear this term thrown around constantly in modern statistics, AI, and machine learning.", "tokens": [51065, 509, 1568, 341, 1433, 11732, 926, 6460, 294, 4363, 12523, 11, 7318, 11, 293, 3479, 2539, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04833033038120644, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.8688219374785042e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 272430, "start": 2742.3, "end": 2746.3, "text": " Because it is the rigorous mathematical formalization of rational learning.", "tokens": [51265, 1436, 309, 307, 264, 29882, 18894, 9860, 2144, 295, 15090, 2539, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04833033038120644, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.8688219374785042e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 272430, "start": 2746.3, "end": 2749.3, "text": " It is a dynamical system for belief.", "tokens": [51465, 467, 307, 257, 5999, 804, 1185, 337, 7107, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04833033038120644, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.8688219374785042e-12}, {"id": 846, "seek": 274930, "start": 2749.3, "end": 2754.3, "text": " You begin with a prior belief, your initial probability distribution about the state of the world.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1841, 365, 257, 4059, 7107, 11, 428, 5883, 8482, 7316, 466, 264, 1785, 295, 264, 1002, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05849252169645285, "compression_ratio": 1.6541666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.832465386028548e-12}, {"id": 847, "seek": 274930, "start": 2754.3, "end": 2755.3, "text": " Your starting guess.", "tokens": [50615, 2260, 2891, 2041, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05849252169645285, "compression_ratio": 1.6541666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.832465386028548e-12}, {"id": 848, "seek": 274930, "start": 2755.3, "end": 2757.3, "text": " Then you observe new evidence.", "tokens": [50665, 1396, 291, 11441, 777, 4467, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05849252169645285, "compression_ratio": 1.6541666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.832465386028548e-12}, {"id": 849, "seek": 274930, "start": 2757.3, "end": 2765.3, "text": " The Bayesian formula dictates exactly how you must mathematically combine your prior with the evidence to generate a posterior belief.", "tokens": [50765, 440, 7840, 42434, 8513, 12569, 1024, 2293, 577, 291, 1633, 44003, 10432, 428, 4059, 365, 264, 4467, 281, 8460, 257, 33529, 7107, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05849252169645285, "compression_ratio": 1.6541666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.832465386028548e-12}, {"id": 850, "seek": 274930, "start": 2765.3, "end": 2771.3, "text": " You are iteratively updating your internal representation of reality to systematically reduce your uncertainty.", "tokens": [51165, 509, 366, 17138, 19020, 25113, 428, 6920, 10290, 295, 4103, 281, 39531, 5407, 428, 15697, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05849252169645285, "compression_ratio": 1.6541666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.832465386028548e-12}, {"id": 851, "seek": 277130, "start": 2771.3, "end": 2775.3, "text": " But Bayesian inference relies entirely on probability distributions.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 7840, 42434, 38253, 30910, 7696, 322, 8482, 37870, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08590447743733724, "compression_ratio": 1.6009389671361502, "no_speech_prob": 2.2712786512668615e-12}, {"id": 852, "seek": 277130, "start": 2775.3, "end": 2777.3, "text": " What if you aren't dealing with probabilities?", "tokens": [50565, 708, 498, 291, 3212, 380, 6260, 365, 33783, 30, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08590447743733724, "compression_ratio": 1.6009389671361502, "no_speech_prob": 2.2712786512668615e-12}, {"id": 853, "seek": 277130, "start": 2777.3, "end": 2787.3, "text": " What if you are just staring at a single isolated string of data and you want to know how complex it is without knowing anything about how it was generated?", "tokens": [50665, 708, 498, 291, 366, 445, 18043, 412, 257, 2167, 14621, 6798, 295, 1412, 293, 291, 528, 281, 458, 577, 3997, 309, 307, 1553, 5276, 1340, 466, 577, 309, 390, 10833, 30, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08590447743733724, "compression_ratio": 1.6009389671361502, "no_speech_prob": 2.2712786512668615e-12}, {"id": 854, "seek": 277130, "start": 2787.3, "end": 2791.3, "text": " The text contrasts Bayes with something called Komagorov complexity.", "tokens": [51165, 440, 2487, 8712, 82, 7840, 279, 365, 746, 1219, 14286, 559, 284, 5179, 14024, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08590447743733724, "compression_ratio": 1.6009389671361502, "no_speech_prob": 2.2712786512668615e-12}, {"id": 855, "seek": 279130, "start": 2791.3, "end": 2798.3, "text": " Komagorov complexity, or algorithmic information theory, approaches the problem from a completely different angle.", "tokens": [50365, 14286, 559, 284, 5179, 14024, 11, 420, 9284, 299, 1589, 5261, 11, 11587, 264, 1154, 490, 257, 2584, 819, 5802, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0511512815952301, "compression_ratio": 1.6317991631799162, "no_speech_prob": 1.920416299941441e-12}, {"id": 856, "seek": 279130, "start": 2798.3, "end": 2803.3, "text": " It asks how much inherent information is contained in one specific isolated object.", "tokens": [50715, 467, 8962, 577, 709, 26387, 1589, 307, 16212, 294, 472, 2685, 14621, 2657, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0511512815952301, "compression_ratio": 1.6317991631799162, "no_speech_prob": 1.920416299941441e-12}, {"id": 857, "seek": 279130, "start": 2803.3, "end": 2806.3, "text": " And the mathematical answer is startlingly concrete.", "tokens": [50965, 400, 264, 18894, 1867, 307, 722, 1688, 356, 9859, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0511512815952301, "compression_ratio": 1.6317991631799162, "no_speech_prob": 1.920416299941441e-12}, {"id": 858, "seek": 279130, "start": 2806.3, "end": 2813.3, "text": " The complexity of a string of data is defined as the exact length of the absolute shortest computer program required to print that string.", "tokens": [51115, 440, 14024, 295, 257, 6798, 295, 1412, 307, 7642, 382, 264, 1900, 4641, 295, 264, 8236, 31875, 3820, 1461, 4739, 281, 4482, 300, 6798, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0511512815952301, "compression_ratio": 1.6317991631799162, "no_speech_prob": 1.920416299941441e-12}, {"id": 859, "seek": 281330, "start": 2813.3, "end": 2814.3, "text": " Okay, let's test that.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1500, 300, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154820442199707, "compression_ratio": 1.6425855513307985, "no_speech_prob": 2.8715556408404064e-12}, {"id": 860, "seek": 281330, "start": 2814.3, "end": 2821.3, "text": " If my string of data is just 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1 repeating for a million digits, it looks massive.", "tokens": [50415, 759, 452, 6798, 295, 1412, 307, 445, 1958, 11, 502, 11, 1958, 11, 502, 11, 1958, 11, 502, 18617, 337, 257, 2459, 27011, 11, 309, 1542, 5994, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154820442199707, "compression_ratio": 1.6425855513307985, "no_speech_prob": 2.8715556408404064e-12}, {"id": 861, "seek": 281330, "start": 2821.3, "end": 2827.3, "text": " But it isn't complex because the computer program to generate it is just print 0, 1, 1 million times.", "tokens": [50765, 583, 309, 1943, 380, 3997, 570, 264, 3820, 1461, 281, 8460, 309, 307, 445, 4482, 1958, 11, 502, 11, 502, 2459, 1413, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154820442199707, "compression_ratio": 1.6425855513307985, "no_speech_prob": 2.8715556408404064e-12}, {"id": 862, "seek": 281330, "start": 2827.3, "end": 2828.3, "text": " That program is tiny.", "tokens": [51065, 663, 1461, 307, 5870, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154820442199707, "compression_ratio": 1.6425855513307985, "no_speech_prob": 2.8715556408404064e-12}, {"id": 863, "seek": 281330, "start": 2828.3, "end": 2831.3, "text": " The string is massive but highly compressible.", "tokens": [51115, 440, 6798, 307, 5994, 457, 5405, 14778, 964, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154820442199707, "compression_ratio": 1.6425855513307985, "no_speech_prob": 2.8715556408404064e-12}, {"id": 864, "seek": 281330, "start": 2831.3, "end": 2834.3, "text": " Therefore, its algorithmic complexity is incredibly low.", "tokens": [51265, 7504, 11, 1080, 9284, 299, 14024, 307, 6252, 2295, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154820442199707, "compression_ratio": 1.6425855513307985, "no_speech_prob": 2.8715556408404064e-12}, {"id": 865, "seek": 281330, "start": 2834.3, "end": 2835.3, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51415, 865, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154820442199707, "compression_ratio": 1.6425855513307985, "no_speech_prob": 2.8715556408404064e-12}, {"id": 866, "seek": 281330, "start": 2835.3, "end": 2838.3, "text": " But what if the string has absolutely no discernible pattern?", "tokens": [51465, 583, 437, 498, 264, 6798, 575, 3122, 572, 30868, 964, 5102, 30, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154820442199707, "compression_ratio": 1.6425855513307985, "no_speech_prob": 2.8715556408404064e-12}, {"id": 867, "seek": 281330, "start": 2838.3, "end": 2839.3, "text": " Like total noise.", "tokens": [51615, 1743, 3217, 5658, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154820442199707, "compression_ratio": 1.6425855513307985, "no_speech_prob": 2.8715556408404064e-12}, {"id": 868, "seek": 283930, "start": 2839.3, "end": 2851.3, "text": " What if you exhaust every possible algorithm and the absolute shortest computer program that can successfully print the string is just the command print, followed by the exact million digit string itself?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 498, 291, 14687, 633, 1944, 9284, 293, 264, 8236, 31875, 3820, 1461, 300, 393, 10727, 4482, 264, 6798, 307, 445, 264, 5622, 4482, 11, 6263, 538, 264, 1900, 2459, 14293, 6798, 2564, 30, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052695489144540045, "compression_ratio": 1.7114093959731544, "no_speech_prob": 2.5841254049779883e-12}, {"id": 869, "seek": 283930, "start": 2851.3, "end": 2854.3, "text": " Then the program is exactly as long as the data it's trying to print.", "tokens": [50965, 1396, 264, 1461, 307, 2293, 382, 938, 382, 264, 1412, 309, 311, 1382, 281, 4482, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052695489144540045, "compression_ratio": 1.7114093959731544, "no_speech_prob": 2.5841254049779883e-12}, {"id": 870, "seek": 283930, "start": 2854.3, "end": 2856.3, "text": " You haven't saved any space at all.", "tokens": [51115, 509, 2378, 380, 6624, 604, 1901, 412, 439, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052695489144540045, "compression_ratio": 1.7114093959731544, "no_speech_prob": 2.5841254049779883e-12}, {"id": 871, "seek": 283930, "start": 2856.3, "end": 2861.3, "text": " And in the realm of mathematics, that incompressibility is the formal definition of randomness.", "tokens": [51215, 400, 294, 264, 15355, 295, 18666, 11, 300, 40393, 735, 2841, 307, 264, 9860, 7123, 295, 4974, 1287, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052695489144540045, "compression_ratio": 1.7114093959731544, "no_speech_prob": 2.5841254049779883e-12}, {"id": 872, "seek": 283930, "start": 2861.3, "end": 2867.3, "text": " If a string of data cannot be compressed into a shorter algorithmic rule, it is algorithmically random.", "tokens": [51465, 759, 257, 6798, 295, 1412, 2644, 312, 30353, 666, 257, 11639, 9284, 299, 4978, 11, 309, 307, 9284, 984, 4974, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052695489144540045, "compression_ratio": 1.7114093959731544, "no_speech_prob": 2.5841254049779883e-12}, {"id": 873, "seek": 286730, "start": 2867.3, "end": 2871.3, "text": " True information is identified with irreducible description.", "tokens": [50365, 13587, 1589, 307, 9234, 365, 16014, 769, 32128, 3855, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.029922776222229004, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205522588938706e-12}, {"id": 874, "seek": 286730, "start": 2871.3, "end": 2874.3, "text": " That completely inverts how I conceptualize randomness.", "tokens": [50565, 663, 2584, 28653, 1373, 577, 286, 24106, 1125, 4974, 1287, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.029922776222229004, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205522588938706e-12}, {"id": 875, "seek": 286730, "start": 2874.3, "end": 2876.3, "text": " It isn't just about unpredictability.", "tokens": [50715, 467, 1943, 380, 445, 466, 28341, 2310, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.029922776222229004, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205522588938706e-12}, {"id": 876, "seek": 286730, "start": 2876.3, "end": 2879.3, "text": " It is about absolute incompressibility.", "tokens": [50815, 467, 307, 466, 8236, 40393, 735, 2841, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.029922776222229004, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205522588938706e-12}, {"id": 877, "seek": 286730, "start": 2879.3, "end": 2885.3, "text": " And the text ties all these threads together at the end with mutual information and relative entropy.", "tokens": [50965, 400, 264, 2487, 14039, 439, 613, 19314, 1214, 412, 264, 917, 365, 16917, 1589, 293, 4972, 30867, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.029922776222229004, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205522588938706e-12}, {"id": 878, "seek": 286730, "start": 2885.3, "end": 2888.3, "text": " Mutual information essentially measures the overlap of knowledge.", "tokens": [51265, 18517, 901, 1589, 4476, 8000, 264, 19959, 295, 3601, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.029922776222229004, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205522588938706e-12}, {"id": 879, "seek": 286730, "start": 2888.3, "end": 2896.3, "text": " It quantifies how much knowing the state of one variable actively reduces your mathematical uncertainty about another.", "tokens": [51415, 467, 4426, 11221, 577, 709, 5276, 264, 1785, 295, 472, 7006, 13022, 18081, 428, 18894, 15697, 466, 1071, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.029922776222229004, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205522588938706e-12}, {"id": 880, "seek": 289630, "start": 2896.3, "end": 2897.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052127105849129815, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211776708742077e-12}, {"id": 881, "seek": 289630, "start": 2897.3, "end": 2906.3, "text": " And relative entropy, which is often called the Kolbach-Leibler divergence, measures the pure informational distance between two competing descriptions of reality.", "tokens": [50415, 400, 4972, 30867, 11, 597, 307, 2049, 1219, 264, 26137, 32096, 12, 11020, 897, 1918, 47387, 11, 8000, 264, 6075, 49391, 4560, 1296, 732, 15439, 24406, 295, 4103, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052127105849129815, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211776708742077e-12}, {"id": 882, "seek": 289630, "start": 2906.3, "end": 2919.3, "text": " If the universe is flipping a fair coin, but your internal model stubbornly insists the coin is heavily biased, the relative entropy mathematically quantifies exactly how many bits of information you are wasting by clinging to the wrong model.", "tokens": [50865, 759, 264, 6445, 307, 26886, 257, 3143, 11464, 11, 457, 428, 6920, 2316, 24137, 356, 50137, 264, 11464, 307, 10950, 28035, 11, 264, 4972, 30867, 44003, 4426, 11221, 2293, 577, 867, 9239, 295, 1589, 291, 366, 20457, 538, 596, 8716, 281, 264, 2085, 2316, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052127105849129815, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211776708742077e-12}, {"id": 883, "seek": 291930, "start": 2919.3, "end": 2923.3, "text": " It is the geometric distance between your belief and the actual truth.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 33246, 4560, 1296, 428, 7107, 293, 264, 3539, 3494, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09649103879928589, "compression_ratio": 1.4777070063694266, "no_speech_prob": 2.6866738001007917e-12}, {"id": 884, "seek": 291930, "start": 2923.3, "end": 2929.3, "text": " I think we need to take a massive step back and look at the whole board because the arc of this deep dive is staggering.", "tokens": [50565, 286, 519, 321, 643, 281, 747, 257, 5994, 1823, 646, 293, 574, 412, 264, 1379, 3150, 570, 264, 10346, 295, 341, 2452, 9192, 307, 42974, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09649103879928589, "compression_ratio": 1.4777070063694266, "no_speech_prob": 2.6866738001007917e-12}, {"id": 885, "seek": 291930, "start": 2929.3, "end": 2931.3, "text": " The text calls it the grand unification.", "tokens": [50865, 440, 2487, 5498, 309, 264, 2697, 517, 3774, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09649103879928589, "compression_ratio": 1.4777070063694266, "no_speech_prob": 2.6866738001007917e-12}, {"id": 886, "seek": 293130, "start": 2931.3, "end": 2934.3, "text": " We started with the basic algebra of high school functions.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1409, 365, 264, 3875, 21989, 295, 1090, 1395, 6828, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060315977732340494, "compression_ratio": 1.5270935960591132, "no_speech_prob": 2.2349619984568525e-12}, {"id": 887, "seek": 293130, "start": 2934.3, "end": 2935.3, "text": " We did.", "tokens": [50515, 492, 630, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060315977732340494, "compression_ratio": 1.5270935960591132, "no_speech_prob": 2.2349619984568525e-12}, {"id": 888, "seek": 293130, "start": 2935.3, "end": 2939.3, "text": " We explored the geometric collapse of the isomorphism theorems.", "tokens": [50565, 492, 24016, 264, 33246, 15584, 295, 264, 307, 32702, 1434, 10299, 2592, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060315977732340494, "compression_ratio": 1.5270935960591132, "no_speech_prob": 2.2349619984568525e-12}, {"id": 889, "seek": 293130, "start": 2939.3, "end": 2943.3, "text": " We rebuilt math using the arrows of category theory.", "tokens": [50765, 492, 38532, 5221, 1228, 264, 19669, 295, 7719, 5261, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060315977732340494, "compression_ratio": 1.5270935960591132, "no_speech_prob": 2.2349619984568525e-12}, {"id": 890, "seek": 293130, "start": 2943.3, "end": 2949.3, "text": " We translated coordinates, diagonalized matrices, and bypassed calculus with the Fourier transform.", "tokens": [50965, 492, 16805, 21056, 11, 21539, 1602, 32284, 11, 293, 24996, 292, 33400, 365, 264, 36810, 4088, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060315977732340494, "compression_ratio": 1.5270935960591132, "no_speech_prob": 2.2349619984568525e-12}, {"id": 891, "seek": 293130, "start": 2949.3, "end": 2950.3, "text": " It's been a long journey.", "tokens": [51265, 467, 311, 668, 257, 938, 4671, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060315977732340494, "compression_ratio": 1.5270935960591132, "no_speech_prob": 2.2349619984568525e-12}, {"id": 892, "seek": 295030, "start": 2950.3, "end": 2953.3, "text": " We watched iterative feedback loops breed chaos.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 6337, 17138, 1166, 5824, 16121, 18971, 14158, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04409370317563906, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201275548192843e-12}, {"id": 893, "seek": 295030, "start": 2953.3, "end": 2958.3, "text": " And we measured the limits of human knowledge with entropy and algorithmic complexity.", "tokens": [50515, 400, 321, 12690, 264, 10406, 295, 1952, 3601, 365, 30867, 293, 9284, 299, 14024, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04409370317563906, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201275548192843e-12}, {"id": 894, "seek": 295030, "start": 2958.3, "end": 2962.3, "text": " It spans nearly every major discipline of mathematics.", "tokens": [50765, 467, 44086, 6217, 633, 2563, 13635, 295, 18666, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04409370317563906, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201275548192843e-12}, {"id": 895, "seek": 295030, "start": 2962.3, "end": 2977.3, "text": " But the revelation is that whether we are talking about an injective function perfectly preserving its domain, a lossless compression algorithm packing data, or a hamming space protecting a CD from a physical scratch, it is all the exact same math.", "tokens": [50965, 583, 264, 23456, 307, 300, 1968, 321, 366, 1417, 466, 364, 10711, 488, 2445, 6239, 33173, 1080, 9274, 11, 257, 4470, 1832, 19355, 9284, 20815, 1412, 11, 420, 257, 36600, 278, 1901, 12316, 257, 6743, 490, 257, 4001, 8459, 11, 309, 307, 439, 264, 1900, 912, 5221, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04409370317563906, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201275548192843e-12}, {"id": 896, "seek": 297730, "start": 2977.3, "end": 2978.3, "text": " It truly is.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 4908, 307, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06873086486199889, "compression_ratio": 1.6183745583038869, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834716772331284e-12}, {"id": 897, "seek": 297730, "start": 2978.3, "end": 2983.3, "text": " At every level, mathematics is simply the rigorous study of what distinctions survive a transformation.", "tokens": [50415, 1711, 633, 1496, 11, 18666, 307, 2935, 264, 29882, 2979, 295, 437, 1483, 49798, 7867, 257, 9887, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06873086486199889, "compression_ratio": 1.6183745583038869, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834716772331284e-12}, {"id": 898, "seek": 297730, "start": 2983.3, "end": 2986.3, "text": " Every single field is just asking a variation of the same question.", "tokens": [50665, 2048, 2167, 2519, 307, 445, 3365, 257, 12990, 295, 264, 912, 1168, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06873086486199889, "compression_ratio": 1.6183745583038869, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834716772331284e-12}, {"id": 899, "seek": 297730, "start": 2986.3, "end": 2990.3, "text": " Do the differences between these original states survive this new process?", "tokens": [50815, 1144, 264, 7300, 1296, 613, 3380, 4368, 7867, 341, 777, 1399, 30, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06873086486199889, "compression_ratio": 1.6183745583038869, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834716772331284e-12}, {"id": 900, "seek": 297730, "start": 2990.3, "end": 2996.3, "text": " Which brings us to the final and undoubtedly most provocative concept from the source material's closing chapter, chapter 7.", "tokens": [51015, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 2572, 293, 35211, 881, 47663, 3410, 490, 264, 4009, 2527, 311, 10377, 7187, 11, 7187, 1614, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06873086486199889, "compression_ratio": 1.6183745583038869, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834716772331284e-12}, {"id": 901, "seek": 297730, "start": 2996.3, "end": 2998.3, "text": " I have been waiting for this.", "tokens": [51315, 286, 362, 668, 3806, 337, 341, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06873086486199889, "compression_ratio": 1.6183745583038869, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834716772331284e-12}, {"id": 902, "seek": 297730, "start": 2998.3, "end": 3000.3, "text": " The ultimate implication of the manuscript.", "tokens": [51415, 440, 9705, 37814, 295, 264, 23928, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06873086486199889, "compression_ratio": 1.6183745583038869, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834716772331284e-12}, {"id": 903, "seek": 300030, "start": 3000.3, "end": 3008.3, "text": " Throughout this entire journey, we have learned how to track what changes, what is lost, and how to measure the remainder.", "tokens": [50365, 22775, 341, 2302, 4671, 11, 321, 362, 3264, 577, 281, 2837, 437, 2962, 11, 437, 307, 2731, 11, 293, 577, 281, 3481, 264, 29837, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.054763537186842695, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129233787273936e-12}, {"id": 904, "seek": 300030, "start": 3008.3, "end": 3015.3, "text": " But tracking what changes naturally leads to the ultimate question of both modern physics and mathematics, symmetry.", "tokens": [50765, 583, 11603, 437, 2962, 8195, 6689, 281, 264, 9705, 1168, 295, 1293, 4363, 10649, 293, 18666, 11, 25440, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.054763537186842695, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129233787273936e-12}, {"id": 905, "seek": 300030, "start": 3015.3, "end": 3016.3, "text": " Symmetry.", "tokens": [51115, 3902, 2174, 9889, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.054763537186842695, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129233787273936e-12}, {"id": 906, "seek": 300030, "start": 3016.3, "end": 3021.3, "text": " Usually when I hear symmetry, I just picture a square being rotated 90 degrees and looking the same.", "tokens": [51165, 11419, 562, 286, 1568, 25440, 11, 286, 445, 3036, 257, 3732, 885, 42146, 4289, 5310, 293, 1237, 264, 912, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.054763537186842695, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129233787273936e-12}, {"id": 907, "seek": 302130, "start": 3021.3, "end": 3026.3, "text": " Take that geometric intuition and expand it to the fabric of reality.", "tokens": [50365, 3664, 300, 33246, 24002, 293, 5268, 309, 281, 264, 7253, 295, 4103, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06018701424965492, "compression_ratio": 1.8129770992366412, "no_speech_prob": 2.253109808100784e-12}, {"id": 908, "seek": 302130, "start": 3026.3, "end": 3030.3, "text": " A mathematical object is not defined by its physical substance.", "tokens": [50615, 316, 18894, 2657, 307, 406, 7642, 538, 1080, 4001, 12961, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06018701424965492, "compression_ratio": 1.8129770992366412, "no_speech_prob": 2.253109808100784e-12}, {"id": 909, "seek": 302130, "start": 3030.3, "end": 3034.3, "text": " It is entirely defined by the set of transformations that leave it completely unchanged.", "tokens": [50815, 467, 307, 7696, 7642, 538, 264, 992, 295, 34852, 300, 1856, 309, 2584, 44553, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06018701424965492, "compression_ratio": 1.8129770992366412, "no_speech_prob": 2.253109808100784e-12}, {"id": 910, "seek": 302130, "start": 3034.3, "end": 3035.3, "text": " Unchanged.", "tokens": [51015, 1156, 339, 10296, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06018701424965492, "compression_ratio": 1.8129770992366412, "no_speech_prob": 2.253109808100784e-12}, {"id": 911, "seek": 302130, "start": 3035.3, "end": 3036.3, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51065, 1033, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06018701424965492, "compression_ratio": 1.8129770992366412, "no_speech_prob": 2.253109808100784e-12}, {"id": 912, "seek": 302130, "start": 3036.3, "end": 3040.3, "text": " A sphere is defined by the fact that it is invariant under continuous rotation.", "tokens": [51115, 316, 16687, 307, 7642, 538, 264, 1186, 300, 309, 307, 33270, 394, 833, 10957, 12447, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06018701424965492, "compression_ratio": 1.8129770992366412, "no_speech_prob": 2.253109808100784e-12}, {"id": 913, "seek": 302130, "start": 3040.3, "end": 3048.3, "text": " The fundamental laws of physics, conservation of energy, conservation of momentum are entirely defined by their invariance across shifts in time and space.", "tokens": [51315, 440, 8088, 6064, 295, 10649, 11, 16185, 295, 2281, 11, 16185, 295, 11244, 366, 7696, 7642, 538, 641, 33270, 719, 2108, 19201, 294, 565, 293, 1901, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06018701424965492, "compression_ratio": 1.8129770992366412, "no_speech_prob": 2.253109808100784e-12}, {"id": 914, "seek": 304830, "start": 3048.3, "end": 3050.3, "text": " The invariants are the reality.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 33270, 1719, 366, 264, 4103, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05953735180115432, "compression_ratio": 1.5866141732283465, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506462417551163e-12}, {"id": 915, "seek": 304830, "start": 3050.3, "end": 3051.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50465, 1779, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05953735180115432, "compression_ratio": 1.5866141732283465, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506462417551163e-12}, {"id": 916, "seek": 304830, "start": 3051.3, "end": 3054.3, "text": " The core properties that stubbornly survive all the representation changes.", "tokens": [50515, 440, 4965, 7221, 300, 24137, 356, 7867, 439, 264, 10290, 2962, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05953735180115432, "compression_ratio": 1.5866141732283465, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506462417551163e-12}, {"id": 917, "seek": 304830, "start": 3054.3, "end": 3063.3, "text": " So if every single property we mathematically care about is ultimately just an invariant under some specific transformation, the author poses a final provocation.", "tokens": [50665, 407, 498, 633, 2167, 4707, 321, 44003, 1127, 466, 307, 6284, 445, 364, 33270, 394, 833, 512, 2685, 9887, 11, 264, 3793, 26059, 257, 2572, 24568, 399, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05953735180115432, "compression_ratio": 1.5866141732283465, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506462417551163e-12}, {"id": 918, "seek": 304830, "start": 3063.3, "end": 3067.3, "text": " Do the physical objects of our universe even truly exist?", "tokens": [51115, 1144, 264, 4001, 6565, 295, 527, 6445, 754, 4908, 2514, 30, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05953735180115432, "compression_ratio": 1.5866141732283465, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506462417551163e-12}, {"id": 919, "seek": 304830, "start": 3067.3, "end": 3072.3, "text": " Or is reality itself just a complex web of intersecting symmetries?", "tokens": [51315, 1610, 307, 4103, 2564, 445, 257, 3997, 3670, 295, 27815, 278, 14232, 302, 2244, 30, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05953735180115432, "compression_ratio": 1.5866141732283465, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506462417551163e-12}, {"id": 920, "seek": 307230, "start": 3072.3, "end": 3073.3, "text": " Hmm.", "tokens": [50365, 8239, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 921, "seek": 307230, "start": 3073.3, "end": 3077.3, "text": " When we study a particle, are we actually studying a physical thing?", "tokens": [50415, 1133, 321, 2979, 257, 12359, 11, 366, 321, 767, 7601, 257, 4001, 551, 30, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 922, "seek": 307230, "start": 3077.3, "end": 3083.3, "text": " Or are we merely studying the empty mathematical spaces where various transformations happen to cancel out?", "tokens": [50615, 1610, 366, 321, 17003, 7601, 264, 6707, 18894, 7673, 689, 3683, 34852, 1051, 281, 10373, 484, 30, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 923, "seek": 307230, "start": 3083.3, "end": 3084.3, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50915, 3153, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 924, "seek": 307230, "start": 3084.3, "end": 3087.3, "text": " Is there even a there there or is it nothing but the network of relationships?", "tokens": [50965, 1119, 456, 754, 257, 456, 456, 420, 307, 309, 1825, 457, 264, 3209, 295, 6159, 30, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 925, "seek": 307230, "start": 3087.3, "end": 3090.3, "text": " It drags us right back to our very first analogy.", "tokens": [51115, 467, 5286, 82, 505, 558, 646, 281, 527, 588, 700, 21663, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 926, "seek": 307230, "start": 3090.3, "end": 3091.3, "text": " The filing system.", "tokens": [51265, 440, 26854, 1185, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 927, "seek": 307230, "start": 3091.3, "end": 3092.3, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51315, 7587, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 928, "seek": 307230, "start": 3092.3, "end": 3095.3, "text": " Maybe the physical documents and the folders don't even exist.", "tokens": [51365, 2704, 264, 4001, 8512, 293, 264, 31082, 500, 380, 754, 2514, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 929, "seek": 307230, "start": 3095.3, "end": 3100.3, "text": " Maybe the only thing that is actually real are the rules for how we sort the empty space.", "tokens": [51515, 2704, 264, 787, 551, 300, 307, 767, 957, 366, 264, 4474, 337, 577, 321, 1333, 264, 6707, 1901, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.052281641569293914, "compression_ratio": 1.70446735395189, "no_speech_prob": 1.846836052143974e-12}, {"id": 930, "seek": 310030, "start": 3100.3, "end": 3106.3, "text": " It fundamentally challenges you to question the physical nature of the landscape we started this entire conversation on.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 17879, 4759, 291, 281, 1168, 264, 4001, 3687, 295, 264, 9661, 321, 1409, 341, 2302, 3761, 322, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.051454750696818034, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 2.100923168074642e-12}, {"id": 931, "seek": 310030, "start": 3106.3, "end": 3107.3, "text": " It absolutely does.", "tokens": [50665, 467, 3122, 775, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.051454750696818034, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 2.100923168074642e-12}, {"id": 932, "seek": 310030, "start": 3107.3, "end": 3111.3, "text": " And on that slightly existential note, we will leave you to ponder it.", "tokens": [50715, 400, 322, 300, 4748, 37133, 3637, 11, 321, 486, 1856, 291, 281, 280, 8548, 309, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.051454750696818034, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 2.100923168074642e-12}, {"id": 933, "seek": 310030, "start": 3111.3, "end": 3123.3, "text": " We invite you to look around your world today and think about the invisible structures, the deliberate blind spots in your own mental transformations and the intersecting mathematical symmetries that are secretly governing your daily life.", "tokens": [50915, 492, 7980, 291, 281, 574, 926, 428, 1002, 965, 293, 519, 466, 264, 14603, 9227, 11, 264, 30515, 6865, 10681, 294, 428, 1065, 4973, 34852, 293, 264, 27815, 278, 18894, 14232, 302, 2244, 300, 366, 22611, 30054, 428, 5212, 993, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.051454750696818034, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 2.100923168074642e-12}, {"id": 934, "seek": 312330, "start": 3123.3, "end": 3124.3, "text": " Thanks for joining us on this Deep Dive.", "tokens": [50365, 2561, 337, 5549, 505, 322, 341, 413, 475, 413, 488, 13, 50415], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -0.6486744513878455, "compression_ratio": 2.1379310344827585, "no_speech_prob": 3.3407198448548447e-12}], "language": "en"}

